      <div class="view" id="view-admin">
        <div class="control-page-toolbar">
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" id="kgvPageToggle" onclick="toggleKgValidationPage()">Metric Definitions</button>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" onclick="nav('overview')">← Home</button>
        </div>
        <div class="page-head kgv-results-content">
          <div class="eyebrow">CONTROL TOWER · KNOWLEDGE GRAPH ASSURANCE</div>
          <div class="page-title" id="controlTowerTitle">Eight-Layer KG Validation</div>
          <div class="page-sub" id="controlTowerSubtitle">Evidence-first validation across domain, use case, upload Tracking ID, and Scenario ID.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="card kgv-results-content" style="margin-bottom:18px">
          <div class="card-head">
            <div class="card-title">Validation Scope</div>
            <span id="kgvContextState" class="kgv-zone amber">Loading contexts</span>
          </div>
          <div class="kgv-toolbar">
            <div class="kgv-field"><label for="kgvDomain">Domain</label><select id="kgvDomain" class="inp" onchange="kgvContextFilterChanged('domain')"></select></div>
            <div class="kgv-field"><label for="kgvUseCase">Use case</label><select id="kgvUseCase" class="inp" onchange="kgvContextFilterChanged('use_case')"></select></div>
            <div class="kgv-field"><label for="kgvTrackingId">Upload Tracking ID</label><select id="kgvTrackingId" class="inp" onchange="kgvContextFilterChanged('tracking_id')"></select></div>
            <div class="kgv-field"><label for="kgvScenarioId">Scenario ID</label><select id="kgvScenarioId" class="inp" onchange="kgvContextFilterChanged('scenario_id')"></select></div>
          </div>
          <div class="kgv-actions">
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" id="kgvRunButton" onclick="runKgValidation()">Run 8-Layer Validation</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" onclick="refreshKgValidationContexts()">Refresh Contexts</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" id="kgvJsonButton" onclick="exportKgValidation('json')" disabled>Export JSON</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" id="kgvCsvButton" onclick="exportKgValidation('csv')" disabled>Export CSV</button>
          </div>
          <div class="kgv-note">Green: score ≥ 90. Amber: 75–89.99. Red: score below 75 or a hard integrity failure. Missing evidence never receives a synthesized passing result.</div>
        </div>
        <section class="kgv-methodology" id="kgvDefinitionsPage" aria-label="Metric definitions">
          <div class="kgv-methodology-head">
            <div class="eyebrow">CONTROL TOWER · VALIDATION METHODOLOGY</div>
            <div class="page-title">Metric Definitions, Calculation and Zone Thresholds</div>
            <div class="page-sub">Definitions and executable scoring rules for all eight knowledge-graph validation layers.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="kgv-methodology-body">
            <div class="kgv-formula">
              Standard layer score = Σ(check score × check weight) ÷ Σ(check weight). All current checks have equal weight and normally score either 100 (pass) or 0 (fail). Each layer ranges from 0–100. Overall score = arithmetic mean of all 8 layer scores.
            </div>
            <div class="kgv-zone-rules">
              <div class="kgv-zone-rule"><b><span class="kgv-zone green">Green</span> 90.00–100</b>Evidence demonstrates that the layer meets its executable acceptance criteria and has no hard failure.</div>
              <div class="kgv-zone-rule"><b><span class="kgv-zone amber">Amber</span> 75.00–89.99</b>Partially validated or awaiting a repeat/baseline comparison. Review failed checks before relying on the output.</div>
              <div class="kgv-zone-rule"><b><span class="kgv-zone red">Red</span> 0–74.99</b>Insufficient or contradictory evidence. A <span class="kgv-hard">hard failure forces Red</span> even when the numerical score is 75 or higher.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="kgv-note">
              Overall zone rule: the numerical mean uses all eight layers. However, the overall result is capped at Red whenever required layer L1, L2, L4, or L8 is Red. Missing evidence is scored as a failure, not inferred by the LLM.
            </div>
            <div class="kgv-definition-grid">
              <div class="kgv-definition">
                <h4>L1 · Structural integrity</h4>
                <p>Measures whether the graph is technically well-formed. Range: 0–100; 7 equal checks.</p>
                <ul><li>Nodes and relationships exist</li><li>Every node has a stable, unique ID</li><li>Every relationship endpoint resolves</li><li>Nodes have types/labels</li><li>Every graph fact has provenance</li><li class="kgv-hard">Hard: missing nodes/edges/IDs, duplicate IDs, or invalid endpoints</li></ul>
              </div>
              <div class="kgv-definition">
                <h4>L2 · Cross-source linkage</h4>
                <p>Measures whether structured and unstructured evidence is linked correctly. Range: 0–100; 5 equal checks.</p>
                <ul><li>Both tabular and document evidence exist</li><li>Relationships retain source references</li><li>References resolve to uploaded files</li><li>At least one edge is supported by multiple sources</li><li>No accidental self-links</li><li class="kgv-hard">Hard: missing source classes, unknown sources, or no cross-source edge</li></ul>
              </div>
              <div class="kgv-definition">
                <h4>L3 · Pattern injection test</h4>
                <p>Validates the test engine itself using known inputs and expected outputs. Range: 0–100; 5 equal checks.</p>
                <ul><li>Creates exactly 3 fixture nodes and 2 edges</li><li>Resolves all fixture endpoints</li><li>Recovers the known two-hop path</li><li>Rejects an injected orphan edge</li><li class="kgv-hard">All fixture checks are mandatory</li></ul>
              </div>
              <div class="kgv-definition">
                <h4>L4 · Rule coverage test</h4>
                <p>Measures whether configured detection rules are executable and tested. Range: 0–100; 6 equal checks.</p>
                <ul><li>Rules are configured</li><li>Every rule was executed</li><li>Every rule retains result evidence</li><li>Positive, negative and boundary controls exist</li><li class="kgv-hard">Hard: no rules or incomplete execution</li></ul>
              </div>
              <div class="kgv-definition">
                <h4>L5 · Graph topology test</h4>
                <p>Detects statistically abnormal graph structure. Range: 0–100; 6 equal checks.</p>
                <ul><li>Nodes and edges are available</li><li>No unintended self-loops</li><li>Isolated nodes are below 10%</li><li>Components ≤ 15% of node count, minimum allowance 1</li><li>Density is greater than 0 and at most 0.65</li><li>Maximum degree ≤ max(4, 80% of nodes)</li><li class="kgv-hard">Hard: topology unavailable</li></ul>
              </div>
              <div class="kgv-definition">
                <h4>L6 · Determinism &amp; regression</h4>
                <p>Measures repeatability against the previous run for the same Tracking and Scenario IDs. Range: 0–100.</p>
                <ul><li>First run creates a baseline and is fixed at 80 (Amber)</li><li>Later runs compare canonical snapshot hashes</li><li>Validation-score drift must be ≤ 5 points</li><li>Layout coordinates and timestamps are excluded from the hash</li><li class="kgv-hard">Hard: changed canonical facts for unchanged context</li></ul>
              </div>
              <div class="kgv-definition">
                <h4>L7 · Output consistency test</h4>
                <p>Measures agreement among detections, findings and reports. Range: 0–100; 5 equal checks.</p>
                <ul><li>Detection and report outputs exist</li><li>Severity uses approved labels</li><li>Every finding is evidence-grounded</li><li>Reports align with graph/detection findings</li><li>LLM-only facts are explicitly labelled</li><li class="kgv-hard">Hard: outputs or finding evidence missing</li></ul>
              </div>
              <div class="kgv-definition">
                <h4>L8 · End-to-end journey test</h4>
                <p>Measures complete lineage through the user journey. Range: 0–100; 8 equal checks.</p>
                <ul><li>Domain, use case, Tracking ID and Scenario ID are bound</li><li>Persisted files exist</li><li>Schema and real entity-resolution execution exist</li><li>Construction and graph evidence exist</li><li>Detections and reports completed</li><li>Next AI grounding status exists</li><li class="kgv-hard">Hard: identity, files, or constructed graph missing</li></ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
        <div id="kgvSummary" class="kgv-summary kgv-results-content" style="display:none">
          <div class="kgv-summary-card"><span>Overall validation</span><strong id="kgvOverallScore">—</strong><div id="kgvOverallZone" style="margin-top:9px"></div></div>
          <div class="kgv-summary-card"><span>Green layers</span><strong id="kgvGreenCount">0</strong></div>
          <div class="kgv-summary-card"><span>Amber layers</span><strong id="kgvAmberCount">0</strong></div>
          <div class="kgv-summary-card"><span>Red layers</span><strong id="kgvRedCount">0</strong></div>
        </div>
        <div id="kgvLayerGrid" class="kgv-layer-grid kgv-results-content">
          <div class="kgv-empty">Select a validation context and run the eight-layer test.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="card kgv-detail kgv-results-content" id="kgvDetailCard" style="display:none">
          <div class="card-head"><div class="card-title" id="kgvDetailTitle">Layer details</div><div id="kgvDetailZone"></div></div>
          <div id="kgvCheckList"></div>
          <div id="kgvRemediation" class="kgv-remediation"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="card kgv-results-content">
          <div class="card-head">
            <div class="card-title">Validation Run History</div>
            <span id="kgvHistoryCount" style="font-size:11px;color:var(--tx-2)">0 runs</span>
          </div>
          <div id="kgvHistory"><div class="kgv-empty">No validation runs have been recorded.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="view" id="view-eval">
        <div class="page-head">
          <div class="eyebrow">⑥ SYSTEM EVALUATION</div>
          <div class="page-title">RAGAS & Performance Metrics</div>
          <div class="page-sub">Pre-computed benchmark scores evaluating Graph-RAG retrieval accuracy and Text-to-Cypher translation via the RAGAS framework.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid-2" style="margin-bottom:18px">
          <!-- RAGAS Metrics Card -->
          <div class="card">
            <div class="card-head">
              <div class="card-title">🎯 RAGAS Quality Metrics</div>
            </div>
            <div style="padding: 16px;">
              <!-- Faithfulness -->
              <div style="margin-bottom:16px;">
                <div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; margin-bottom:6px; font-size:14px;">
                  <span style="color:var(--tx-1)">Faithfulness</span>
                  <span style="font-weight:600; color:var(--emerald)">0.92</span>
                </div>
                <div style="background:var(--bg-2); border-radius:4px; height:8px; overflow:hidden;">
                  <div style="background:var(--emerald); width:92%; height:100%;"></div>
                </div>
                <div style="font-size:11px; color:var(--tx-2); margin-top:4px;">Measures lack of hallucination against graph context.</div>
              </div>
              
              <!-- Answer Relevancy -->
              <div style="margin-bottom:16px;">
                <div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; margin-bottom:6px; font-size:14px;">
                  <span style="color:var(--tx-1)">Answer Relevancy</span>
                  <span style="font-weight:600; color:var(--emerald)">0.88</span>
                </div>
                <div style="background:var(--bg-2); border-radius:4px; height:8px; overflow:hidden;">
                  <div style="background:var(--emerald); width:88%; height:100%;"></div>
                </div>
                <div style="font-size:11px; color:var(--tx-2); margin-top:4px;">Measures how directly the answer addresses the question.</div>
              </div>

              <!-- Context Precision -->
              <div style="margin-bottom:16px;">
                <div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; margin-bottom:6px; font-size:14px;">
                  <span style="color:var(--tx-1)">Context Precision</span>
                  <span style="font-weight:600; color:var(--amber)">0.75</span>
                </div>
                <div style="background:var(--bg-2); border-radius:4px; height:8px; overflow:hidden;">
                  <div style="background:var(--amber); width:75%; height:100%;"></div>
                </div>
                <div style="font-size:11px; color:var(--tx-2); margin-top:4px;">Signal-to-noise ratio of retrieved nodes & chunks.</div>
              </div>

              <!-- Context Recall -->
              <div>
                <div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; margin-bottom:6px; font-size:14px;">
                  <span style="color:var(--tx-1)">Context Recall</span>
                  <span style="font-weight:600; color:var(--emerald)">1.00</span>
                </div>
                <div style="background:var(--bg-2); border-radius:4px; height:8px; overflow:hidden;">
                  <div style="background:var(--emerald); width:100%; height:100%;"></div>
                </div>
                <div style="font-size:11px; color:var(--tx-2); margin-top:4px;">Measures if all required information was successfully retrieved.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Cypher Metrics Card -->
          <div class="card">
            <div class="card-head">
              <div class="card-title">🕸️ Text-to-Cypher Execution</div>
            </div>
            <div style="padding: 16px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; justify-content:center; align-items:center; height:100%;">
              <div style="font-size:64px; font-weight:800; color:var(--emerald); line-height:1">100%</div>
              <div style="font-size:14px; color:var(--tx-2); margin-top:12px; text-align:center;">
                Syntactically valid Cypher generated<br/>(3/3 queries executed successfully)
              </div>
              <div style="margin-top:24px; width:100%; border-top:1px solid var(--line); padding-top:16px;">
                <div class="stat-row"><span class="k">Test Queries</span><span class="v">3</span></div>
                <div class="stat-row"><span class="k">Parse Errors</span><span class="v">0</span></div>
                <div class="stat-row"><span class="k">LLM Model</span><span class="v">llama-3.1-70b-versatile</span></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-head">
            <div class="card-title">Golden Dataset Sample</div>
          </div>
          <table class="risk-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Test Question</th>
                <th>Ground Truth (Expected)</th>
                <th>Graph-RAG Output</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td style="width:25%; font-weight:500;">Which documents expire in the next 90 days?</td>
                <td style="width:37%; color:var(--tx-2);">LG-C317 (76 days), LG-A192 (42 days), LG-G731 (58 days).</td>
                <td style="width:37%;">Based on the portfolio, LG-A192 (Vantage Analytics) expires in 42 days, LG-G731 (Coastal Retail Group) expires in 58 days, and LG-C317 (Brightline Legal) expires in 76 days.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td style="font-weight:500;">What is the average base rent psf?</td>
                <td style="color:var(--tx-2);">$38.40 per sqft.</td>
                <td>The average base rent across the queried documents is $38.40 psf.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td style="font-weight:500;">Which tenant has the highest concentration risk?</td>
                <td style="color:var(--tx-2);">Vantage Analytics with 50,800 sqft.</td>
                <td>Vantage Analytics represents the highest concentration risk with a total of 50,800 sqft across 3 documents (45% portfolio share).</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>

  <script>
    /* ============================================================
       MOCK DATA — mirrors the real Neo4j ontology graph schema
       ============================================================ */
    const PROPERTIES = [
      { id: 'P1', address: '456 Commerce Blvd', city: 'Dallas', state: 'TX', sqft: 42000 },
      { id: 'P2', address: '120 Innovation Way', city: 'Austin', state: 'TX', sqft: 28500 },
      { id: 'P3', address: '875 Riverfront Dr', city: 'Houston', state: 'TX', sqft: 51000 },
      { id: 'P4', address: '33 Peachtree Center', city: 'Atlanta', state: 'GA', sqft: 36750 },
      { id: 'P5', address: '901 Lakeside Plaza', city: 'Denver', state: 'CO', sqft: 19800 },
      { id: 'P6', address: '1500 Tech Park Loop', city: 'Austin', state: 'TX', sqft: 64200 },
    ];
    const TENANTS = [
      { id: 'T1', name: 'Vantage Analytics', industry: 'Technology' },
      { id: 'T2', name: 'Meridian Health Group', industry: 'Healthcare' },
      { id: 'T3', name: 'Brightline Legal', industry: 'Legal' },
      { id: 'T4', name: 'Northgate Financial', industry: 'Finance' },
      { id: 'T5', name: 'Vantage Analytics', industry: 'Technology' }, // appears twice — multi-document tenant
      { id: 'T6', name: 'Coastal Retail Group', industry: 'Retail' },
    ];
    const today = new Date('2026-06-30');
    function addDays(d, n) { const r = new Date(d); r.setDate(r.getDate() + n); return r; }
    function fmt(d) { return d.toISOString().slice(0, 10); }

    const LEASES = [
      { id: 'LG-A192', prop: 'P1', tenant: 'T1', start: '2022-03-01', end: fmt(addDays(today, 42)), rent: 36.5, sqft: 18000, type: 'NNN' },
      { id: 'LG-B204', prop: 'P2', tenant: 'T2', start: '2021-07-15', end: fmt(addDays(today, 1100)), rent: 41.0, sqft: 9500, type: 'Gross' },
      { id: 'LG-C317', prop: 'P3', tenant: 'T3', start: '2023-01-10', end: fmt(addDays(today, 76)), rent: 29.0, sqft: 14200, type: 'Modified Gross' },
      { id: 'LG-D408', prop: 'P4', tenant: 'T4', start: '2020-09-01', end: fmt(addDays(today, 820)), rent: 33.5, sqft: 21000, type: 'NNN' },
      { id: 'LG-E519', prop: 'P5', tenant: 'T5', start: '2022-11-20', end: fmt(addDays(today, 1450)), rent: 45.0, sqft: 8800, type: 'Gross' },
      { id: 'LG-F626', prop: 'P6', tenant: 'T1', start: '2024-02-01', end: fmt(addDays(today, 1820)), rent: 39.5, sqft: 24000, type: 'NNN' },
      { id: 'LG-G731', prop: 'P1', tenant: 'T6', start: '2023-06-01', end: fmt(addDays(today, 58)), rent: 28.0, sqft: 6500, type: 'Modified Gross' },
      { id: 'LG-H845', prop: 'P2', tenant: 'T4', start: '2021-01-01', end: fmt(addDays(today, 940)), rent: 37.0, sqft: 11000, type: 'Gross' },
    ];

    const CLAUSES = [
      { document: 'LG-A192', text: 'Tenant may terminate this Document effective the last day of Year 3 with 12 months prior written notice.', type: 'Termination Right' },
      { document: 'LG-C317', text: 'Co-Tenancy Provision: if anchor tenant vacates the Property, Tenant rent is reduced by 25% until anchor is replaced.', type: 'Co-Tenancy' },
      { document: 'LG-D408', text: 'Landlord shall not document any other space in the Property to a directly competing financial services business.', type: 'Exclusivity' },
      { document: 'LG-G731', text: 'Tenant has a one-time early termination right after Month 24 with payment of 6 months base rent as penalty.', type: 'Termination Right' },
      { document: 'LG-F626', text: 'Right of First Refusal: Tenant may match any third-party offer on adjacent vacant suite within 30 days.', type: 'ROFR' },
    ];

    const RENEWALS = [
      { document: 'LG-A192', term: 5, notice: 12, rent_basis: 'FMR' },
      { document: 'LG-B204', term: 3, notice: 9, rent_basis: 'FMR' },
      { document: 'LG-D408', term: 5, notice: 12, rent_basis: 'FMR' },
      { document: 'LG-F626', term: 5, notice: 6, rent_basis: 'Fixed' },
    ];

    const TERMINATIONS = [
      { document: 'LG-A192', effective_after_year: 3, notice_months: 12, penalty_months: 0 },
      { document: 'LG-G731', effective_after_year: 2, notice_months: 6, penalty_months: 6 },
    ];

    let llmCallCount = 0;
    function bumpLLM() {
      llmCallCount++;
      const el = document.getElementById('sb-llm');
      if (el) el.textContent = llmCallCount;
    }

    function updateSidebarLiveStats() {
      const setText = (id, value) => {
        const el = document.getElementById(id);
        if (el) el.textContent = String(value);
      };

      const csvCount = (typeof uploadedCsvFiles !== 'undefined' && uploadedCsvFiles)
        ? uploadedCsvFiles.length : 0;
      const pdfCount = (typeof uploadedPdfFiles !== 'undefined' && uploadedPdfFiles)
        ? uploadedPdfFiles.length : 0;
      let csvTarget = csvCount || 8;
      let pdfTarget = pdfCount || 7;
      try {
        const inventory = typeof getConstructInventory === 'function'
          ? getConstructInventory() : null;
        if (inventory) {
          csvTarget = Math.max(csvCount, (inventory.csvNames || []).length || csvTarget);
          pdfTarget = Math.max(pdfCount, (inventory.docNames || []).length || pdfTarget);
        }
      } catch (_) {}

      const graph = window.igGraphCache || {};
      let nodeCount = Array.isArray(graph.nodes) ? graph.nodes.length : 0;
      let edgeCount = Array.isArray(graph.links) ? graph.links.length : 0;
      let alertCount = 0;
      const snapshotMetrics = (window.graphenConstructSnapshot || {}).metrics || {};
      if (!nodeCount) nodeCount = Number(snapshotMetrics.nodes_total || 0);
      if (!edgeCount) edgeCount = Number(snapshotMetrics.edges_total || 0);
      alertCount = Number(snapshotMetrics.alerts || 0);
      try {
        if (typeof cyphCompletedDets !== 'undefined') {
          alertCount = Math.max(alertCount, cyphCompletedDets.size);
        }
        if (typeof cyphFlagWrites !== 'undefined') {
          alertCount = Math.max(alertCount, Object.keys(cyphFlagWrites).length);
        }
      } catch (_) {}

      setText('liveCsvStat', csvCount + '/' + csvTarget);
      setText('livePdfStat', pdfCount + '/' + pdfTarget);
      setText('liveNodeStat', nodeCount);
      setText('liveEdgeStat', edgeCount);
      setText('liveAlertStat', alertCount);
    }

    /* ============================================================
       NAVIGATION
       ============================================================ */
    let dashboardLoaded = false;
    async function loadDashboardData() {
      // retained for Admin metrics if needed; Dashboard tab removed
      if (dashboardLoaded) return;
      try {
        const res = await fetch('/api/summary');
        if (res.ok) {
          const s = await res.json();
          const set = (id, v) => { const el = document.getElementById(id); if (el) el.textContent = v; };
          set('dash-leases', s.lease_count ?? s.leases ?? '—');
          set('dash-tenants', s.tenant_count ?? s.tenants ?? '—');
          set('dash-sqft', s.total_sqft ?? '—');
          set('dash-clauses', s.high_risk_clauses ?? '—');
        }
      } catch (_) {}
      dashboardLoaded = true;
    }

    /* ============================================================
       DOMAIN CONFIGURATOR — authoritative journey context
       ============================================================ */
    const DOMAIN_CATALOG = [
      {
        industry: 'Financial Services', icon: '🏦',
        sub: 'AML · Fraud · KYC · Credit Risk',
        entities: ['Customer', 'Account', 'Transaction', 'Company'],
        relationships: ['OWNS', 'TRANSFERRED_TO', 'CONNECTED_TO'],
        detections: ['transaction rings', 'sanctions exposure', 'identity overlap'],
        ontology: ['FIBO', 'ISO 20022'],
      },
      {
        industry: 'Healthcare & Life Sciences', icon: '🏥',
        sub: 'Clinical · Patient · Drug Safety · Genomics',
        entities: ['Patient', 'Provider', 'Claim', 'Product'],
        relationships: ['TREATED_BY', 'HAS_CLAIM', 'REFERRED_TO'],
        detections: ['referral loops', 'safety signals', 'care-path anomalies'],
        ontology: ['FHIR', 'SNOMED CT'],
      },
      {
        industry: 'Manufacturing & Supply Chain', icon: '🏭',
        sub: 'Digital Twin · Supplier Risk · Quality',
        entities: ['Product', 'Asset', 'Supplier', 'Component'],
        relationships: ['CONTAINS', 'SOURCED_FROM', 'INSTALLED_AT'],
        detections: ['dependency concentration', 'quality propagation', 'asset failure paths'],
        ontology: ['ISA-95', 'ISO 10303 STEP'],
      },
      {
        industry: 'Telecommunications', icon: '📡',
        sub: 'Network Fraud · Faults · Customer 360',
        entities: ['Subscriber', 'Device', 'Network Element', 'Service'],
        relationships: ['USES', 'CONNECTED_TO', 'DEPENDS_ON'],
        detections: ['SIM/device overlap', 'network fault paths', 'churn signals'],
        ontology: ['TM Forum SID', '3GPP'],
      },
      {
        industry: 'Retail & E-Commerce', icon: '🛒',
        sub: 'Product KG · Recommendation · Customer 360',
        entities: ['Customer', 'Product', 'Order', 'Location'],
        relationships: ['PURCHASED', 'VIEWED', 'FULFILLED_BY'],
        detections: ['product affinity', 'returns anomalies', 'inventory dependency'],
        ontology: ['GS1', 'schema.org'],
      },
    ];
    let domainSelectedIndustry = '';
    let domainSelectedUseCase = '';
    let domainConfiguration = null;
    let domainTrendingUseCases = [];
    let domainTrendingIndustry = '';
    let domainTrendingLoading = false;
    let domainTrendingGeneration = 0;
    let domainCustomMode = false;
    let domainSavedScenarios = [];
    let domainKeepFormOnNextEntry = false;
    window.currentJourneyTrackingId = null;

    function domainEscape(value) {
      return String(value == null ? '' : value)
        .replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;')
        .replace(/"/g, '&quot;').replace(/'/g, '&#39;');
    }

    function domainCatalogEntry() {
      return DOMAIN_CATALOG.find(item => item.industry === domainSelectedIndustry) || null;
    }

    function renderDomainConfigurator() {
      const industryGrid = document.getElementById('domainIndustryGrid');
      if (industryGrid) {
        industryGrid.innerHTML = DOMAIN_CATALOG.map((item, index) =>
          '<button type="button" class="domain-industry-card' +
          (item.industry === domainSelectedIndustry ? ' selected' : '') +
          '" onclick="selectDomainIndustry(' + index + ')"><span class="domain-industry-icon">' +
          item.icon + '</span><span class="domain-industry-name">' + domainEscape(item.industry) +
          '</span><span class="domain-industry-sub">' + domainEscape(item.sub) + '</span></button>'
        ).join('');
      }
      const useCaseGrid = document.getElementById('domainUseCaseGrid');
      if (useCaseGrid) {
        if (!domainSelectedIndustry) {
          useCaseGrid.innerHTML = '<div class="crossdoc-empty">Select an industry to load its five trending use cases.</div>';
        } else if (domainTrendingLoading && !domainTrendingUseCases.length) {
          useCaseGrid.innerHTML = '<div class="crossdoc-empty">AI is ranking current ' +
            domainEscape(domainSelectedIndustry) + ' use cases…</div>';
        } else {
          const trendCards = domainTrendingUseCases.slice(0, 5).map((item, index) =>
            '<button type="button" class="domain-usecase-card' +
            (item.title === domainSelectedUseCase && !domainCustomMode ? ' selected' : '') +
            '" onclick="selectDomainUseCase(' + index + ')"><div class="domain-usecase-icon">' +
            domainEscape(item.icon || '◆') + '</div><div class="domain-usecase-name">' +
            domainEscape(item.title) + '</div><div class="domain-usecase-sub">' +
            domainEscape(item.description) + '</div><div class="domain-trend-badge">' +
            domainEscape(item.trend_note || 'Trending now') + '</div></button>'
          ).join('');
          const customCard =
            '<button type="button" class="domain-usecase-card custom' +
            (domainCustomMode ? ' selected' : '') +
            '" onclick="openCustomUseCase()"><div class="domain-usecase-icon">✎</div>' +
            '<div class="domain-usecase-name">User-Defined Use Case</div>' +
            '<div class="domain-usecase-sub">Write a scenario in your own words and let AI synthesize the graph journey.</div>' +
            '<div class="domain-trend-badge">Your custom scenario</div></button>';
          useCaseGrid.innerHTML = trendCards + customCard;
        }
      }
      const customPanel = document.getElementById('domainCustomUseCasePanel');
      if (customPanel) customPanel.hidden = !domainCustomMode;
      if (domainConfiguration && domainConfiguration.intake) {
        const intake = domainConfiguration.intake;
        setDomainFormValues(intake, false);
      }
      updateDomainPreview(domainConfiguration);
      renderSavedDomainScenarios();
    }

    async function selectDomainIndustry(index) {
      const item = DOMAIN_CATALOG[index];
      if (!item) return;
      domainSelectedIndustry = item.industry;
      domainSelectedUseCase = '';
      domainCustomMode = false;
      domainConfiguration = null;
      domainTrendingUseCases = [];
      renderDomainConfigurator();
      updateDomainStatus();
      await loadTrendingUseCases(true);
    }

    function selectDomainUseCase(index) {
      const item = domainTrendingUseCases[index];
      if (!item) return;
      domainSelectedUseCase = item.title;
      domainCustomMode = false;
      domainConfiguration = null;
      renderDomainConfigurator();
      updateDomainStatus();
    }

    function setDomainFormValues(intake, overwrite) {
      const fields = {
        domainOrganization: intake && intake.organization_context,
        domainObjective: intake && intake.objective,
        domainDataAvailable: intake && intake.data_available,
        domainGeography: intake && intake.geography,
        domainAudience: intake && intake.decision_audience,
        domainNotes: intake && intake.notes,
      };
      Object.entries(fields).forEach(([id, value]) => {
        const el = document.getElementById(id);
        if (el && (overwrite || !el.value)) el.value = value || '';
      });
    }

    async function trendingUseCasesApiRequest(payload) {
      const options = {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify(payload),
      };
      try {
        const response = await fetch('/api/domain/trending-use-cases', options);
        if (response.status !== 404) return response;
      } catch (_) {}
      return fetch('http://127.0.0.1:8011/api/domain/trending-use-cases', options);
    }

    async function fetchTrendingUseCases(skipLlm, generation) {
      const intake = domainIntakePayload(true);
      const response = await trendingUseCasesApiRequest({
        industry: domainSelectedIndustry,
        organization_context: intake.organization_context,
        geography: intake.geography,
        objective: intake.objective,
        refresh_seed: Date.now() + generation,
        skip_llm: !!skipLlm,
      });
      if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Trending use cases HTTP ' + response.status);
      return response.json();
    }

    async function loadTrendingUseCases(forceRefresh) {
      if (!domainSelectedIndustry) return;
      const generation = ++domainTrendingGeneration;
      domainTrendingLoading = true;
      if (forceRefresh) domainTrendingUseCases = [];
      renderDomainConfigurator();
      const trendMeta = document.getElementById('domainTrendSource');
      if (trendMeta) trendMeta.textContent = 'Ranking current ' + domainSelectedIndustry + ' trends…';
      try {
        const fast = await fetchTrendingUseCases(true, generation);
        if (generation !== domainTrendingGeneration) return;
        domainTrendingUseCases = (fast.use_cases || []).slice(0, 5);
        domainTrendingIndustry = fast.industry || domainSelectedIndustry;
        domainTrendingLoading = false;
        if (trendMeta) trendMeta.textContent =
          'Trending now · ' + (fast.period || 'current period') + ' · trend fallback';
        renderDomainConfigurator();

        domainTrendingLoading = true;
        const refined = await fetchTrendingUseCases(false, generation);
        if (generation !== domainTrendingGeneration) return;
        if (refined && Array.isArray(refined.use_cases) && refined.use_cases.length === 5) {
          const selected = domainTrendingUseCases.find(
            item => item.title === domainSelectedUseCase
          );
          domainTrendingUseCases = refined.use_cases;
          if (selected && !domainCustomMode &&
              !domainTrendingUseCases.some(item => item.title === selected.title)) {
            domainTrendingUseCases[4] = selected;
          }
          domainTrendingIndustry = refined.industry || domainSelectedIndustry;
        }
        if (trendMeta) trendMeta.textContent =
          'Trending now · ' + (refined.period || 'current period') +
          (refined.source === 'llm' ? ' · AI-ranked' : ' · current ranking');
      } catch (error) {
        console.warn('trending use cases failed', error);
        if (trendMeta) trendMeta.textContent = domainTrendingUseCases.length
          ? 'Trending now · current fallback'
          : 'Trend service unavailable — refresh to retry';
      } finally {
        if (generation === domainTrendingGeneration) {
          domainTrendingLoading = false;
          renderDomainConfigurator();
        }
      }
    }

    function refreshTrendingUseCases() {
      if (!domainSelectedIndustry) {
        updateDomainStatus('Select an industry before refreshing trends.', 'error');
        return;
      }
      domainSelectedUseCase = '';
      domainCustomMode = false;
      domainConfiguration = null;
      loadTrendingUseCases(true);
    }

    function openCustomUseCase() {
      if (!domainSelectedIndustry) {
        updateDomainStatus('Select an industry before defining a use case.', 'error');
        return;
      }
      domainCustomMode = true;
      domainConfiguration = null;
      renderDomainConfigurator();
      const title = document.getElementById('domainCustomTitle');
      if (title) title.focus();
    }

    function syncCustomUseCaseFromForm() {
      if (!domainCustomMode) return;
      const titleEl = document.getElementById('domainCustomTitle');
      const descriptionEl = document.getElementById('domainCustomDescription');
      const title = titleEl ? titleEl.value.trim() : '';
      const description = descriptionEl ? descriptionEl.value.trim() : '';
      if (title) domainSelectedUseCase = title;
      const objective = document.getElementById('domainObjective');
      if (objective && !objective.value.trim() && description) objective.value = description;
      const notes = document.getElementById('domainNotes');
      if (notes && !notes.value.trim() && description) {
        notes.value = 'User-defined scenario: ' + description;
      }
    }

    async function synthesizeCustomUseCase() {
      syncCustomUseCaseFromForm();
      const titleEl = document.getElementById('domainCustomTitle');
      const descriptionEl = document.getElementById('domainCustomDescription');
      const title = titleEl ? titleEl.value.trim() : '';
      const description = descriptionEl ? descriptionEl.value.trim() : '';
      if (!domainSelectedIndustry || !title || !description) {
        updateDomainStatus('Select an industry and enter a custom title and description.', 'error');
        return;
      }
      domainSelectedUseCase = title;
      domainCustomMode = true;
      const button = document.getElementById('domainCustomAiBtn');
      if (button) { button.disabled = true; button.textContent = 'AI is synthesizing…'; }
      try {
        const fast = await requestDomainConfiguration(false);
        if (fast) {
          updateDomainPreview(fast);
          applyDomainConfiguration(fast);
        }
        const refined = await requestDomainConfiguration(true);
        if (refined) {
          updateDomainPreview(refined);
          applyDomainConfiguration(refined);
          updateDomainStatus(
            'Custom use case synthesized into Configuration Preview. Review it, then save or continue.',
            'ok'
          );
        }
      } catch (error) {
        console.warn('custom use-case synthesis failed', error);
        updateDomainStatus('AI synthesis was unavailable; the custom scenario remains selected.', 'error');
      } finally {
        if (button) { button.disabled = false; button.textContent = '✦ Synthesize with AI'; }
      }
    }

    function domainIntakePayload(skipLlm) {
      syncCustomUseCaseFromForm();
      const value = id => {
        const el = document.getElementById(id);
        return el ? el.value.trim() : '';
      };
      return {
        industry: domainSelectedIndustry,
        use_case: domainSelectedUseCase,
        organization_context: value('domainOrganization'),
        objective: value('domainObjective'),
        data_available: value('domainDataAvailable'),
        geography: value('domainGeography'),
        decision_audience: value('domainAudience'),
        notes: value('domainNotes'),
        skip_llm: !!skipLlm,
      };
    }

    function updateDomainStatus(message, kind) {
      const status = document.getElementById('domainFormStatus');
      if (!status) return;
      const payload = domainIntakePayload(true);
      const ready = payload.industry && payload.use_case && payload.objective;
      status.className = 'domain-form-status' + (kind ? ' ' + kind : (ready ? ' ok' : ''));
      status.textContent = message || (ready
        ? 'Intake ready. Click AI Assist or Synthesize with AI to populate Configuration Preview.'
        : 'Select an industry, use case, and enter the primary objective.');
    }

    function updateDomainPreview(config) {
      const preview = (config && config.preview) || {};
      const ready = !!(config && config.preview);
      const panel = document.getElementById('domainPreviewPanel');
      if (panel) panel.classList.toggle('ready', ready);
      const setText = (id, value) => {
        const el = document.getElementById(id);
        if (el) el.textContent = value || '—';
      };
      const joinList = items => (items && items.length ? items.join(' · ') : '');
      setText(
        'domainPreviewBadge',
        ready
          ? (config.source === 'llm' ? 'AI synthesized · ready' : 'Synthesized · ready')
          : 'Awaiting synthesis'
      );
      setText(
        'domainPreviewTitle',
        ready
          ? (config.industry + ' · ' + config.use_case)
          : (domainSelectedIndustry
            ? (domainSelectedIndustry + (domainSelectedUseCase ? ' · ' + domainSelectedUseCase : ''))
            : 'Your domain journey will appear here')
      );
      setText(
        'domainPreviewCaption',
        ready && config.journey_caption
          ? config.journey_caption
          : (ready
            ? (config.industry + ' · ' + config.use_case + ' — ' + (config.objective || ''))
            : 'Fill the intake, then click AI Assist or Synthesize with AI.')
      );
      setText(
        'domainPreviewGuidance',
        ready && config.ai_guidance
          ? config.ai_guidance
          : 'The synthesized preview becomes the authoritative journey context carried into Schema Registry and every downstream pillar.'
      );
      setText('domainPreviewObjective', ready ? config.objective : '');
      setText('domainPreviewEntities', joinList(preview.primary_entities));
      setText('domainPreviewRelationships', joinList(preview.key_relationships));
      setText('domainPreviewDetections', joinList(preview.detection_focus));
      setText('domainPreviewOntology', joinList(preview.ontology_standards));
      setText('domainPreviewStructured', ready ? preview.structured_focus : '');
      setText('domainPreviewUnstructured', ready ? preview.unstructured_focus : '');
      setText('domainPreviewAudience', ready ? config.decision_audience : '');
      setText('domainPreviewGeography', ready ? config.geography : '');
      setText(
        'domainPreviewNote',
        ready
          ? 'This Configuration Preview is the authoritative journey context for Schema Registry and all downstream pillars.'
          : 'Save Scenario or Continue only after this preview is synthesized for your domain and use case.'
      );
    }

    async function domainConfigurationApiRequest(payload) {
      const options = {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify(payload),
      };
      try {
        const response = await fetch('/api/domain/configure', options);
        if (response.status !== 404) return response;
      } catch (_) {}
      return fetch('http://127.0.0.1:8011/api/domain/configure', options);
    }

    async function requestDomainConfiguration(fullLlm) {
      const payload = domainIntakePayload(!fullLlm);
      if (!payload.industry || !payload.use_case || !payload.objective) {
        updateDomainStatus('Select an industry and use case, then describe the primary objective.', 'error');
        return null;
      }
      const response = await domainConfigurationApiRequest(payload);
      if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Domain configuration HTTP ' + response.status);
      const data = await response.json();
      data.intake = payload;
      domainSelectedIndustry = data.industry;
      domainSelectedUseCase = data.use_case;
      domainConfiguration = data;
      renderDomainConfigurator();
      return data;
    }

    async function assistDomainConfiguration() {
      syncCustomUseCaseFromForm();
      const button = document.getElementById('domainAiBtn');
      if (button) { button.disabled = true; button.textContent = 'AI is configuring…'; }
      try {
        const fast = await requestDomainConfiguration(false);
        if (fast) {
          updateDomainPreview(fast);
          applyDomainConfiguration(fast);
          updateDomainStatus('Evidence-based Configuration Preview ready; AI is refining…', 'ok');
        }
        const refined = await requestDomainConfiguration(true);
        if (refined) {
          updateDomainPreview(refined);
          applyDomainConfiguration(refined);
          updateDomainStatus(
            'Configuration Preview synthesized. Review it, then save or continue.',
            'ok'
          );
        }
      } catch (error) {
        console.warn('domain AI assist failed', error);
        updateDomainStatus('AI assistance was unavailable; the configured fallback remains usable.', 'error');
      } finally {
        if (button) { button.disabled = false; button.textContent = '✦ AI Assist'; }
      }
    }

    function renderSavedDomainScenarios() {
      const container = document.getElementById('domainSavedScenarios');
      if (!container) return;
      const title = document.getElementById('domainSavedTitle');
      const sub = document.getElementById('domainSavedSub');
      if (!domainSelectedIndustry) {
        if (title) title.textContent = 'Last 5 Saved Scenarios';
        if (sub) sub.textContent = 'Select a domain to view only its saved scenarios.';
        container.innerHTML =
          '<div class="crossdoc-empty">Select an industry above to view its last five saved scenarios.</div>';
        return;
      }
      const domainKey = domainSelectedIndustry.toLowerCase();
      const visible = domainSavedScenarios
        .map((scenario, index) => ({ scenario, index }))
        .filter(item => String(item.scenario.industry || '').toLowerCase() === domainKey)
        .slice(0, 5);
      if (title) title.textContent = 'Last 5 Saved Scenarios · ' + domainSelectedIndustry;
      if (sub) {
        sub.textContent = 'Only ' + domainSelectedIndustry +
          ' scenarios are shown. Select one to populate its requirements.';
      }
      if (!visible.length) {
        container.innerHTML =
          '<div class="crossdoc-empty">No saved scenarios for ' +
          domainEscape(domainSelectedIndustry) + ' yet.</div>';
        return;
      }
      container.innerHTML = visible.map(({ scenario, index }) =>
        '<button type="button" class="domain-saved-card" onclick="startSavedDomainScenario(' +
        index + ')"><span class="domain-saved-delete" role="button" tabindex="0" ' +
        'title="Delete this saved scenario" aria-label="Delete saved scenario" ' +
        'onclick="event.stopPropagation(); deleteSavedDomainScenario(' + index +
        ')">×</span><div class="domain-saved-industry">' +
        domainEscape(scenario.industry) + '</div><div class="domain-saved-usecase">' +
        domainEscape(scenario.use_case) + '</div><div class="domain-saved-tracking">ID · ' +
        domainEscape(compactTrackingId(
          scenario.tracking_id || scenario.id,
          scenario.industry,
          scenario.use_case,
          scenario.saved_at
        )) +
        '</div><div class="domain-saved-date">' +
        domainEscape(scenario.saved_label || '') + '</div>' +
        '<div class="domain-saved-start">Load requirements →</div></button>'
      ).join('');
    }

    function limitSavedScenariosPerDomain(items) {
      const counts = new Map();
      return items.filter(scenario => {
        const key = String(scenario.industry || '').toLowerCase();
        const count = counts.get(key) || 0;
        if (count >= 5) return false;
        counts.set(key, count + 1);
        return true;
      });
    }

    function deleteSavedDomainScenario(index) {
      const scenario = domainSavedScenarios[index];
      if (!scenario) return;
      const displayId = compactTrackingId(
        scenario.tracking_id || scenario.id,
        scenario.industry,
        scenario.use_case,
        scenario.saved_at
      );
      if (typeof window.confirm === 'function' &&
          !window.confirm('Delete saved scenario ' + scenario.use_case + ' (' + displayId + ')?')) {
        return;
      }
      const deletedId = scenario.tracking_id || scenario.id;
      domainSavedScenarios.splice(index, 1);
      localStorage.setItem(
        'graphenSavedDomainScenarios',
        JSON.stringify(domainSavedScenarios)
      );
      if (window.currentJourneyTrackingId === deletedId) {
        window.currentJourneyTrackingId = null;
      }
      renderSavedDomainScenarios();
      updateDomainStatus(
        'Saved scenario deleted. Remaining ' + scenario.industry +
        ' scenarios have moved up in recency order.',
        'ok'
      );
    }

    function compactTrackingId(id, industry, useCase, dateValue) {
      if (!id) return 'Not assigned';
      const raw = String(id);
      if (raw.length <= 30) return raw;
      const acronym = value => String(value || '')
        .split(/[^a-z0-9]+/i).filter(Boolean)
        .map(word => word[0]).join('').toUpperCase().slice(0, 5) || 'SCN';
      const useSlug = String(useCase || 'CASE')
        .replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/gi, '').toUpperCase().slice(0, 10) || 'CASE';
      let date = new Date(dateValue || '');
      if (Number.isNaN(date.getTime())) {
        const timestamp = raw.match(/(20\d{6})T?(\d{6})/);
        if (timestamp) {
          date = new Date(
            timestamp[1].slice(0, 4) + '-' + timestamp[1].slice(4, 6) + '-' +
            timestamp[1].slice(6, 8) + 'T' + timestamp[2].slice(0, 2) + ':' +
            timestamp[2].slice(2, 4) + ':' + timestamp[2].slice(4, 6) + 'Z'
          );
        }
      }
      const stamp = Number.isNaN(date.getTime())
        ? raw.slice(-12).replace(/[^a-z0-9]/gi, '').toUpperCase()
        : date.toISOString().slice(2, 19).replace(/[-:T]/g, '');
      return acronym(industry) + '-' + useSlug + '-' + stamp;
    }

    function domainScenarioTrackingId(industry, useCase, savedAt) {
      const date = savedAt instanceof Date ? savedAt : new Date(savedAt || Date.now());
      return compactTrackingId(
        'force-compact-id-generation-because-this-value-is-long',
        industry,
        useCase,
        date
      );
    }

    function normalizeSavedDomainScenario(scenario) {
      if (!scenario || !scenario.industry || !scenario.use_case) return null;
      const savedAt = scenario.saved_at || new Date().toISOString();
      const trackingId = scenario.tracking_id || domainScenarioTrackingId(
        scenario.industry, scenario.use_case, savedAt
      );
      return {
        ...scenario,
        id: trackingId,
        tracking_id: trackingId,
        saved_at: savedAt,
        saved_label: scenario.saved_label ||
          ('Saved ' + new Date(savedAt).toLocaleString()),
      };
    }

    async function saveDomainScenario() {
      const payload = domainIntakePayload(false);
      if (!payload.industry || !payload.use_case || !payload.objective) {
        updateDomainStatus('Complete the industry, use case, and primary objective before saving.', 'error');
        return;
      }
      const button = document.getElementById('domainSaveBtn');
      if (button) { button.disabled = true; button.textContent = 'Saving…'; }
      try {
        let config = domainConfiguration;
        if (!config || config.industry !== payload.industry ||
            config.use_case !== payload.use_case || config.objective !== payload.objective) {
          config = await requestDomainConfiguration(true);
        }
        if (!config) return;
        config.intake = payload;
        applyDomainConfiguration(config);
        const now = new Date();
        const trackingId = domainScenarioTrackingId(
          config.industry, config.use_case, now
        );
        config.scenario_tracking_id = trackingId;
        try {
          localStorage.setItem('graphenDomainConfiguration', JSON.stringify(config));
        } catch (_) {}
        const scenario = {
          id: trackingId,
          tracking_id: trackingId,
          industry: config.industry,
          use_case: config.use_case,
          objective: config.objective,
          saved_at: now.toISOString(),
          saved_label: 'Saved ' + now.toLocaleString(),
          custom: !!domainCustomMode,
          custom_title: domainCustomMode
            ? ((document.getElementById('domainCustomTitle') || {}).value || config.use_case)
            : '',
          custom_description: domainCustomMode
            ? ((document.getElementById('domainCustomDescription') || {}).value || '')
            : '',
          config: JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(config)),
          intake: { ...payload },
        };
        const key = [scenario.industry, scenario.use_case].join('|').toLowerCase();
        domainSavedScenarios = [
          scenario,
          ...domainSavedScenarios.filter(item =>
            [item.industry, item.use_case].join('|').toLowerCase() !== key
          ),
        ];
        domainSavedScenarios = limitSavedScenariosPerDomain(
          domainSavedScenarios
        );
        localStorage.setItem('graphenSavedDomainScenarios', JSON.stringify(domainSavedScenarios));
        renderSavedDomainScenarios();
        window.currentJourneyTrackingId = trackingId;
        updateDomainStatus(
          'Scenario saved as ' +
          compactTrackingId(trackingId, config.industry, config.use_case, now) +
          '. It is available below.',
          'ok'
        );
      } catch (error) {
        console.warn('save domain scenario failed', error);
        updateDomainStatus('The scenario could not be saved. Please retry.', 'error');
      } finally {
        if (button) { button.disabled = false; button.textContent = '☆ Save Scenario'; }
      }
    }

    async function startSavedDomainScenario(index) {
      const scenario = domainSavedScenarios[index];
      if (!scenario || !scenario.config) return;
      domainSelectedIndustry = scenario.industry;
      domainSelectedUseCase = scenario.use_case;
      domainCustomMode = !!scenario.custom;
      domainConfiguration = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(scenario.config));
      window.currentJourneyTrackingId = scenario.tracking_id || scenario.id || null;
      domainConfiguration.scenario_tracking_id = window.currentJourneyTrackingId;
      setDomainFormValues(scenario.intake || domainConfiguration.intake || {}, true);
      const customTitle = document.getElementById('domainCustomTitle');
      const customDescription = document.getElementById('domainCustomDescription');
      if (customTitle) customTitle.value = scenario.custom_title || scenario.use_case;
      if (customDescription) customDescription.value = scenario.custom_description || '';
      applyDomainConfiguration(domainConfiguration);
      domainKeepFormOnNextEntry = true;
      nav('domain');
      renderDomainConfigurator();
      updateDomainStatus(
        'Saved scenario ' + compactTrackingId(
          window.currentJourneyTrackingId,
          scenario.industry,
          scenario.use_case,
          scenario.saved_at
        ) + ' restored. Review or update the populated requirements, then continue.',
        'ok'
      );
    }

    function clearDomainFormOnEntry() {
      domainSelectedIndustry = '';
      domainSelectedUseCase = '';
      domainConfiguration = null;
      domainTrendingUseCases = [];
      domainTrendingIndustry = '';
      domainTrendingLoading = false;
      domainCustomMode = false;
      window.currentJourneyTrackingId = null;
      setDomainFormValues({}, true);
      const customTitle = document.getElementById('domainCustomTitle');
      const customDescription = document.getElementById('domainCustomDescription');
      if (customTitle) customTitle.value = '';
      if (customDescription) customDescription.value = '';
      renderDomainConfigurator();
      updateDomainStatus(
        'Select a domain and use case, or choose a saved scenario to populate the requirements.'
      );
    }

    function resetDomainConfigurator() {
      if (typeof window.confirm === 'function' &&
          !window.confirm('Reset the active journey and form? Saved scenarios will be preserved.')) {
        return;
      }
      domainTrendingGeneration++;
      domainSelectedIndustry = '';
      domainSelectedUseCase = '';
      domainConfiguration = null;
      domainTrendingUseCases = [];
      domainTrendingIndustry = '';
      domainTrendingLoading = false;
      domainCustomMode = false;
      try {
        localStorage.removeItem('graphenDomainConfiguration');
        localStorage.removeItem('graphenSchemaRegistry');
      } catch (_) {}
      try { sessionStorage.clear(); } catch (_) {}
      window.graphenDomain = null;
      window.graphenSchemaRegistry = null;
      window.graphenUseCaseHint = '';
      window.igTabsMeta = null;
      window.currentJourneyTrackingId = null;
      schemaRegistryPayload = null;
      setDomainFormValues({}, true);
      const customTitle = document.getElementById('domainCustomTitle');
      const customDescription = document.getElementById('domainCustomDescription');
      if (customTitle) customTitle.value = '';
      if (customDescription) customDescription.value = '';
      try { startNewUploadSession(); } catch (_) {}
      try { resetDomainDependentState(); } catch (_) {}
      resetDomainNavigationChrome();
      renderDomainConfigurator();
      nav('domain');
      updateDomainStatus(
        'Active journey reset. Saved scenarios are preserved and ready to restore.',
        'ok'
      );
    }

    function resetDomainNavigationChrome() {
      const defaults = {
        ingest: '0 files · multi-modal',
        entity: 'Match evidence identities',
        construction: 'MERGE nodes and relationships',
        graph: 'Explore live Neo4j graph',
        cypher: 'Pattern and traversal queries',
        crossdoc: 'Multi-document links',
        intel: 'User-specific decision brief',
        report: 'Executive actions and decisions',
        ask: 'Hybrid RAG & Graph-RAG chatbot',
        admin: 'Admin · platform controls',
      };
      pillarSetText('domainNavSub', 'Select industry and use case');
      pillarSetText('schemaNavSub', 'Entity & relationship types');
      Object.entries(defaults).forEach(([view, label]) => pillarNavSub(view, label));
    }

    function applyDomainConfiguration(config) {
      if (!config) return;
      const previous = window.graphenDomain;
      const domainChanged = !!previous && (
        previous.industry !== config.industry ||
        previous.use_case !== config.use_case ||
        previous.objective !== config.objective
      );
      config.is_custom = !!domainCustomMode;
      domainConfiguration = config;
      window.graphenDomain = config;
      window.graphenUseCaseHint = [
        config.industry, config.use_case, config.objective, config.intake_summary,
      ].filter(Boolean).join(' | ');
      try { localStorage.setItem('graphenDomainConfiguration', JSON.stringify(config)); } catch (_) {}
      try { localStorage.removeItem('graphenSchemaRegistry'); } catch (_) {}
      schemaRegistryPayload = null;
      window.graphenSchemaRegistry = null;
      try { igTabsMeta = null; } catch (_) {}
      window.igTabsMeta = null;
      const navSub = document.getElementById('domainNavSub');
      if (navSub) navSub.textContent = config.industry + ' · ' + config.use_case;
      updateJourneyCaption();
      updateDomainSpecificChrome();
      if (domainChanged) setTimeout(resetDomainDependentState, 0);
    }

    function resetDomainDependentState() {
      try {
        structCompleted.clear(); structActiveStep = 0; renderStructResultsFeed();
        const next = document.getElementById('btnNextUnstructured');
        if (next) next.disabled = true;
      } catch (_) {}
      try {
        unstructCompleted.clear(); unstructActiveStep = 0; renderUnstructResultsFeed();
        const next = document.getElementById('btnNextAfterUnstruct');
        if (next) next.disabled = true;
      } catch (_) {}
      try {
        constructCompleted.clear(); constructActiveStep = 0; CONSTRUCT_STEP_META = [];
        constructInventorySig = ''; buildConstructStepCards(); renderConstructResultsFeed();
        const next = document.getElementById('btnNextAfterConstruct');
        if (next) next.disabled = true;
      } catch (_) {}
      try {
        cyphStopPlay(); cyphPayload = null; cyphActiveDet = null; cyphCompletedDets.clear();
        cyphFlagWrites = {}; cyphStepIdx = 0;
      } catch (_) {}
      try { crossdocPayload = null; } catch (_) {}
      try { intelligenceReportPayload = null; } catch (_) {}
      try { finalReportPayload = null; } catch (_) {}
      try {
        nextAiConversation = []; nextAiContextSignature = '';
        nextAiLastUnavailableQuestion = '';
        const chat = document.getElementById('chatScroll');
        if (chat) {
          chat.innerHTML = '<div class="msg ai"><div class="msg-bubble" id="nextAiWelcome">' +
            'Configure a domain and upload evidence to prepare Next AI.</div></div>';
        }
        const evidence = document.getElementById('nextAiEvidenceList');
        if (evidence) evidence.innerHTML = '<div class="crossdoc-empty">No evidence retrieved yet.</div>';
        const fallback = document.getElementById('nextAiFallback');
        if (fallback) fallback.style.display = 'none';
      } catch (_) {}
      window.igTabsMeta = null;
      window.igGraphCache = { nodes: [], links: [] };
      updateSidebarLiveStats();
      applyPillarBlueprint();
    }

    async function beginConfiguredJourney() {
      const button = document.getElementById('domainBeginBtn');
      syncCustomUseCaseFromForm();
      const payload = domainIntakePayload(false);
      if (!payload.industry || !payload.use_case || !payload.objective) {
        updateDomainStatus('Industry, use case, and primary objective are required.', 'error');
        return;
      }
      if (button) { button.disabled = true; button.textContent = 'Preparing journey…'; }
      try {
        let config = domainConfiguration;
        const matchesPreview = config &&
          config.industry === payload.industry &&
          config.use_case === payload.use_case &&
          config.objective === payload.objective &&
          config.preview;
        if (!matchesPreview) {
          config = await requestDomainConfiguration(true);
        }
        if (!config) return;
        config.intake = payload;
        updateDomainPreview(config);
        applyDomainConfiguration(config);
        updateDomainStatus('Journey configured from Configuration Preview.', 'ok');
        nav('schema');
      } catch (error) {
        console.warn('begin configured journey failed', error);
        updateDomainStatus('The journey could not be configured. Please retry.', 'error');
      } finally {
        if (button) { button.disabled = false; button.textContent = 'Continue to Schema Registry →'; }
      }
    }

    let schemaRegistryPayload = null;

    function schemaEsc(value) {
      return String(value == null ? '' : value)
        .replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;')
        .replace(/"/g, '&quot;').replace(/'/g, '&#39;');
    }

    async function schemaRegistryApiRequest(payload) {
      const options = {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify(payload),
      };
      try {
        const response = await fetch('/api/schema/registry', options);
        if (response.status !== 404) return response;
      } catch (_) {}
      return fetch('http://127.0.0.1:8011/api/schema/registry', options);
    }

    function renderSchemaRegistry(payload) {
      if (!payload) return;
      schemaRegistryPayload = payload;
      window.graphenSchemaRegistry = payload;
      const setText = (id, value) => {
        const el = document.getElementById(id);
        if (el) el.textContent = value || '';
      };
      setText('schemaPhase', payload.phase_label || 'Step 2 of 11 · Schema Registry');
      setText('schemaIndustryPill', (payload.industry || 'Domain') + ' · ' + (payload.use_case || 'Use Case'));
      setText('schemaTitle', payload.title || 'Schema Registry — Entity & Relationship Types');
      setText('schemaSubtitle', payload.subtitle || '');
      setText('schemaIntro', payload.intro || '');
      setText('schemaReferenceNote', payload.reference_note ||
        'Reference example only — nothing on this page is an upload requirement.');
      setText('schemaConceptLineage',
        'Synthesized from Domain Configurator: ' + (payload.industry || 'Domain') +
        ' · ' + (payload.use_case || 'Use Case') + ' · Objective: ' +
        (payload.objective || 'Configured journey'));
      setText('schemaNodeTitle', 'Node Types — ' + (payload.node_count || (payload.node_types || []).length) + ' entity labels');
      setText('schemaRelTitle', 'Relationship Types — ' + (payload.relationship_count || (payload.relationship_types || []).length) + ' edge types');
      setText('schemaDimensionTitle', 'Reference Dimensions — ' +
        (payload.dimension_count || (payload.dimensions || []).length) + ' examples');
      setText('schemaTableTitle', 'Illustrative Logical Tables — ' +
        (payload.table_count || (payload.reference_tables || []).length) + ' examples');
      const cypher = document.getElementById('schemaCypherPreview');
      if (cypher) cypher.textContent = payload.cypher_preview || '// No Cypher preview';

      const nodeRows = document.getElementById('schemaNodeRows');
      if (nodeRows) {
        const nodes = payload.node_types || [];
        nodeRows.innerHTML = nodes.length ? nodes.map(node =>
          '<tr><td>:' + schemaEsc(node.label) + '</td><td>' + schemaEsc(node.primary_key) +
          '</td><td>' + schemaEsc(node.key_properties) + '</td></tr>'
        ).join('') : '<tr><td colspan="3">No node types available for this configuration.</td></tr>';
      }

      const relRows = document.getElementById('schemaRelRows');
      if (relRows) {
        const rels = payload.relationship_types || [];
        relRows.innerHTML = rels.length ? rels.map(rel =>
          '<tr><td>' + schemaEsc(rel.type) + '</td><td>:' + schemaEsc(rel.from) +
          '</td><td>:' + schemaEsc(rel.to) + '</td><td>' + schemaEsc(rel.description) + '</td></tr>'
        ).join('') : '<tr><td colspan="4">No relationship types available for this configuration.</td></tr>';
      }

      const dimensionRows = document.getElementById('schemaDimensionRows');
      if (dimensionRows) {
        const dimensions = payload.dimensions || [];
        dimensionRows.innerHTML = dimensions.length ? dimensions.map(item =>
          '<div class="schema-dimension-item"><div class="schema-dimension-name">' +
          schemaEsc(item.name) + '</div><div class="schema-dimension-purpose">' +
          schemaEsc(item.purpose) + '</div><div class="schema-dimension-examples">' +
          schemaEsc(item.example_attributes) + '</div></div>'
        ).join('') : '<div class="crossdoc-empty">No reference dimensions available.</div>';
      }

      const referenceTableRows = document.getElementById('schemaReferenceTableRows');
      if (referenceTableRows) {
        const tables = payload.reference_tables || [];
        referenceTableRows.innerHTML = tables.length ? tables.map(item =>
          '<tr><td>' + schemaEsc(item.table) + '</td><td>' +
          schemaEsc(item.grain) + '</td><td><b>' + schemaEsc(item.primary_key) +
          '</b> · ' + schemaEsc(item.example_columns) + '</td></tr>'
        ).join('') : '<tr><td colspan="3">No illustrative tables available.</td></tr>';
      }

      const navSub = document.getElementById('schemaNavSub');
      if (navSub) navSub.textContent = (payload.industry || 'Schema') + ' · ' + (payload.node_count || 0) + ' nodes';
    }

    async function refreshSchemaRegistry(fullLlm) {
      const config = window.graphenDomain || domainConfiguration;
      if (!config || !config.industry) {
        const intro = document.getElementById('schemaIntro');
        if (intro) intro.textContent = 'Complete Domain Configurator first. The schema is generated from your industry and use-case selection.';
        return null;
      }
      const payload = {
        industry: config.industry || '',
        use_case: config.use_case || '',
        objective: config.objective || '',
        primary_entities: ((config.preview || {}).primary_entities || []),
        key_relationships: ((config.preview || {}).key_relationships || []),
        skip_llm: !fullLlm,
      };
      try {
        const response = await schemaRegistryApiRequest(payload);
        if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Schema registry HTTP ' + response.status);
        const data = await response.json();
        renderSchemaRegistry(data);
        try { localStorage.setItem('graphenSchemaRegistry', JSON.stringify(data)); } catch (_) {}
        return data;
      } catch (error) {
        console.warn('schema registry refresh failed', error);
        const intro = document.getElementById('schemaIntro');
        if (intro) intro.textContent = 'Schema registry could not be loaded. Retry after domain configuration.';
        return null;
      }
    }

    function restoreSchemaRegistry() {
      try {
        const stored = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('graphenSchemaRegistry') || 'null');
        if (stored && stored.node_types) renderSchemaRegistry(stored);
      } catch (_) {}
    }

    function updateJourneyCaption(view) {
      const caption = document.getElementById('journeyCaption');
      const title = document.getElementById('journeyCaptionTitle');
      const label = document.getElementById('journeyCaptionLabel');
      const config = window.graphenDomain || domainConfiguration;
      const activeView = view || (document.querySelector('.view.active') || {}).id || '';
      const hideFor = activeView.includes('overview') || activeView.includes('domain');
      const show = !!config && !hideFor;
      if (caption) caption.hidden = !show;
      if (label) {
        label.textContent = window.currentJourneyTrackingId
          ? ('Saved Scenario · ' + compactTrackingId(
            window.currentJourneyTrackingId,
            config && config.industry,
            config && config.use_case,
            config && config.saved_at
          ))
          : 'Configured GRAPHEN Journey';
      }
      if (title && config) title.textContent = config.journey_caption ||
        (config.industry + ' · ' + config.use_case + ' — ' + config.objective);
    }

    function updateDomainSpecificChrome() {
      const config = window.graphenDomain || domainConfiguration;
      if (!config) return;
      const pillars = config.pillar_blueprint || {};
      const upload = pillars.upload_files || {};
      const uploadScenario = uploadScenarioContext();
      const uploadConfig = (uploadScenario && uploadScenario.config) || config;
      const title = document.getElementById('ingestDomainTitle');
      const subtitle = document.getElementById('ingestDomainSubtitle');
      if (title) {
        title.textContent = 'Upload Evidence for ' +
          (uploadConfig.use_case || config.use_case);
      }
      if (subtitle) {
        const scenarioId = uploadScenario &&
          (uploadScenario.tracking_id || uploadScenario.id);
        subtitle.textContent = scenarioId
          ? ('Latest saved scenario: ' + compactTrackingId(
            scenarioId,
            uploadScenario.industry,
            uploadScenario.use_case,
            uploadScenario.saved_at
          ) + ' · ' +
            uploadConfig.industry + ' · ' + uploadConfig.use_case +
            '. Clicking Upload Files stores the evidence under this scenario and a new upload Tracking ID.')
          : (upload.subtitle ||
            'Save the configured scenario before uploading evidence. The saved scenario and upload Tracking ID are stored together.');
      }
      applyPillarBlueprint(config);
      setTimeout(() => applyPillarBlueprint(config), 0);
    }

    function pillarEscape(value) {
      return String(value == null ? '' : value)
        .replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;')
        .replace(/"/g, '&quot;').replace(/'/g, '&#39;');
    }

    function pillarSetText(id, value) {
      const element = document.getElementById(id);
      if (element && value) element.textContent = String(value);
    }

    function pillarNavSub(view, value) {
      const element = document.querySelector('#appSidebar [data-view="' + view + '"] .nav-sub');
      if (element && value) element.textContent = String(value);
    }

    const ENTITY_RESOLUTION_TABLES = [
      'entity_resolution_candidates',
      'entity_resolution_match_scores',
      'entity_resolution_merged_identities',
      'entity_resolution_provenance',
    ];

    function entityResolutionStepRows(stepIndex, examples) {
      return examples.map((example, index) => {
        const common = {
          row_id: 'ER-' + String(index + 1).padStart(3, '0'),
          source_candidate: example.source || '',
          target_candidate: example.target || '',
        };
        if (stepIndex === 0) {
          return { ...common, stage_status: 'CANDIDATE_COLLECTED' };
        }
        if (stepIndex === 1) {
          return {
            ...common,
            match_method: example.method || '',
            match_confidence: example.confidence ||
              'Above configured merge threshold',
            stage_status: 'IDENTITY_SCORED',
          };
        }
        if (stepIndex === 2) {
          return {
            ...common,
            merge_result: example.enrichment || '',
            stage_status: 'IDENTITY_MERGED',
          };
        }
        return {
          ...common,
          match_method: example.method || '',
          resolved_identity: example.target || '',
          provenance_result: example.enrichment || '',
          scenario_tracking_id: window.currentJourneyTrackingId || '',
          upload_tracking_id: window.currentTrackingId || '',
          stage_status: 'PROVENANCE_PRESERVED',
        };
      });
    }

    function entityResolutionMergedTableName(example, index) {
      const suffix = String((example && example.target) || ('record-' + (index + 1)))
        .replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/gi, '_').replace(/^_+|_+$/g, '').toLowerCase();
      return 'entity_resolution_merged_' + (suffix || ('record_' + (index + 1)));
    }

    function entityResolutionMergedRow(example, index) {
      return {
        record_id: 'ER-' + String(index + 1).padStart(3, '0'),
        source_mention: example.source || '',
        structured_record: example.target || '',
        match_method: example.method || '',
        confidence_decision: example.confidence ||
          'Above configured merge threshold',
        merge_status: 'MERGED',
        merged_output: example.enrichment || '',
        scenario_tracking_id: window.currentJourneyTrackingId || '',
        upload_tracking_id: window.currentTrackingId || '',
      };
    }

    function renderEntityResolutionMergedOutputs(resolution) {
      const container = document.getElementById('entityMatchCards');
      const examples = resolution && Array.isArray(resolution.examples)
        ? resolution.examples.slice(0, 5) : [];
      if (!container || !examples.length) return;
      container.innerHTML = examples.map((example, index) => {
        const tableName = entityResolutionMergedTableName(example, index);
        return '<div class="match-card"><div class="match-row"><span class="src">📄 ' +
          pillarEscape(example.source) + '</span><span class="merge">MERGE →</span>' +
          '<span class="tgt">📊 ' + pillarEscape(example.target) + '</span></div>' +
          '<div class="match-label">Match method</div><div class="match-meta">' +
          pillarEscape(example.method) + '</div><div class="match-label">Confidence decision</div>' +
          '<div class="match-meta">' +
          pillarEscape(example.confidence || 'Above configured merge threshold') +
          '</div><div class="match-label">Merged output</div>' +
          '<div class="match-enrich">' + pillarEscape(example.enrichment) + '</div>' +
          '<div class="merged-output-actions"><div class="logic-table-name">TABLE · ' +
          pillarEscape(tableName) + '</div>' +
          '<button type="button" class="step-export-btn" title="Download this merged output as CSV" ' +
          'onclick="exportEntityResolutionMergedRecord(' + index + ', &#39;csv&#39;)">⇩ CSV</button>' +
          '<button type="button" class="step-export-btn" title="Download this merged output as JSON" ' +
          'onclick="exportEntityResolutionMergedRecord(' + index + ', &#39;json&#39;)">⇩ JSON</button>' +
          '</div></div>';
      }).join('');
    }

    function exportEntityResolutionMergedRecord(index, format) {
      const config = window.graphenDomain || domainConfiguration;
      const resolution = config && config.pillar_blueprint &&
        config.pillar_blueprint.entity_resolution;
      const example = resolution && Array.isArray(resolution.examples)
        ? resolution.examples[index] : null;
      if (!config || !example) {
        alert('This merged output is not available for export.');
        return;
      }
      const tableName = entityResolutionMergedTableName(example, index);
      const row = entityResolutionMergedRow(example, index);
      const payload = {
        table_name: tableName,
        export_type: 'GRAPHEN_ENTITY_RESOLUTION_MERGED_OUTPUT',
        exported_at: new Date().toISOString(),
        domain: config.industry || '',
        use_case: config.use_case || '',
        row,
      };
      const selectedFormat = String(format || 'csv').toLowerCase();
      let content;
      let mime;
      let extension;
      if (selectedFormat === 'json') {
        content = JSON.stringify(payload, null, 2);
        mime = 'application/json';
        extension = 'json';
      } else {
        const headers = Object.keys(row);
        const csvCell = value => '"' +
          String(value == null ? '' : value).replace(/"/g, '""') + '"';
        content = '\uFEFF' + [
          headers.map(csvCell).join(','),
          headers.map(key => csvCell(row[key])).join(','),
        ].join('\r\n');
        mime = 'text/csv;charset=utf-8';
        extension = 'csv';
      }
      const link = document.createElement('a');
      link.href = URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([content], { type: mime }));
      link.download = tableName + '.' + extension;
      document.body.appendChild(link);
      link.click();
      link.remove();
      setTimeout(() => URL.revokeObjectURL(link.href), 500);
    }

    function exportEntityResolutionStep(stepIndex, format) {
      const config = window.graphenDomain || domainConfiguration;
      const resolution = config && config.pillar_blueprint &&
        config.pillar_blueprint.entity_resolution;
      const methods = resolution && Array.isArray(resolution.method_steps)
        ? resolution.method_steps : [];
      const examples = resolution && Array.isArray(resolution.examples)
        ? resolution.examples.slice(0, 5) : [];
      if (!config || !methods[stepIndex] || !examples.length) {
        alert('Configure and save a domain journey before exporting this table.');
        return;
      }
      const tableName = ENTITY_RESOLUTION_TABLES[stepIndex];
      const rows = entityResolutionStepRows(stepIndex, examples);
      const payload = {
        table_name: tableName,
        export_type: 'GRAPHEN_ENTITY_RESOLUTION_STEP',
        exported_at: new Date().toISOString(),
        domain: config.industry || '',
        use_case: config.use_case || '',
        step: 'STEP ' + String.fromCharCode(65 + stepIndex),
        step_title: methods[stepIndex].title || '',
        step_description: methods[stepIndex].description || '',
        rows,
      };
      const selectedFormat = String(format || 'csv').toLowerCase();
      let content;
      let mime;
      let extension;
      if (selectedFormat === 'json') {
        content = JSON.stringify(payload, null, 2);
        mime = 'application/json';
        extension = 'json';
      } else {
        const headers = rows.reduce((all, row) => {
          Object.keys(row).forEach(key => {
            if (!all.includes(key)) all.push(key);
          });
          return all;
        }, []);
        const csvCell = value => '"' +
          String(value == null ? '' : value).replace(/"/g, '""') + '"';
        content = '\uFEFF' + [
          headers.map(csvCell).join(','),
          ...rows.map(row => headers.map(key => csvCell(row[key])).join(',')),
        ].join('\r\n');
        mime = 'text/csv;charset=utf-8';
        extension = 'csv';
      }
      const link = document.createElement('a');
      link.href = URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([content], { type: mime }));
      link.download = tableName + '.' + extension;
      document.body.appendChild(link);
      link.click();
      link.remove();
      setTimeout(() => URL.revokeObjectURL(link.href), 500);
    }

    function applyPillarBlueprint(config) {
      config = config || window.graphenDomain || domainConfiguration;
      if (!config) return;
      const pillars = config.pillar_blueprint || {};
      const preview = config.preview || {};
      const entities = preview.primary_entities || [];
      const relationships = preview.key_relationships || [];
      const detections = preview.detection_focus || [];
      const resolution = pillars.entity_resolution || {};
      pillarSetText('entityPageTitle', resolution.title || ('Entity Resolution for ' + config.use_case));
      pillarSetText('entityPageSub', resolution.subtitle);
      pillarSetText(
        'entityNavSub',
        'Post-merge pipeline · ' + config.use_case + ' identities with source-level proof'
      );
      const methodBoard = document.getElementById('entityMethodBoard');
      if (methodBoard && Array.isArray(resolution.method_steps)) {
        methodBoard.innerHTML = resolution.method_steps.slice(0, 4).map((step, index) =>
          '<div class="logic-step"><div class="ln">STEP ' +
          String.fromCharCode(65 + index) + '</div><div class="lt">' +
          pillarEscape(step.title) + '</div><div class="ld">' +
          pillarEscape(step.description) + '</div><div class="logic-step-actions">' +
          '<div class="logic-table-name">TABLE · ' +
          pillarEscape(ENTITY_RESOLUTION_TABLES[index]) + '</div>' +
          '<button type="button" class="step-export-btn" title="Download this step table as CSV" ' +
          'onclick="exportEntityResolutionStep(' + index + ', &#39;csv&#39;)">⇩ CSV</button>' +
          '<button type="button" class="step-export-btn" title="Download this step table as JSON" ' +
          'onclick="exportEntityResolutionStep(' + index + ', &#39;json&#39;)">⇩ JSON</button>' +
          '</div></div>'
        ).join('');
      }
      const matchCards = document.getElementById('entityMatchCards');
      if (matchCards && Array.isArray(resolution.examples)) {
        renderEntityResolutionMergedOutputs(resolution);
      }

      const construction = pillars.graph_construction || {};
      pillarSetText('constructPageTitle', construction.title);
      pillarSetText('constructPageSub', construction.subtitle);
      try {
        CONSTRUCT_STEP_META = [];
        constructInventorySig = '';
      } catch (_) {}

      const graph = pillars.interactive_graph || {};
      pillarSetText('igPageTitle', graph.title);
      pillarSetText('igPageSub', graph.subtitle);
      const cypher = pillars.cypher_detection || {};
      pillarSetText('cyphPageTitle', cypher.title);
      pillarSetText('cyphIntro', cypher.intro);
      const crossdoc = pillars.cross_doc_discovery || {};
      pillarSetText('crossdocTitle', crossdoc.title);
      pillarSetText(
        'crossdocSubtitle',
        crossdoc.subtitle || crossdoc.focus
      );
      pillarSetText(
        'crossdocEyebrow',
        crossdoc.eyebrow || (config.industry + ' · Cross-Source Reasoning')
      );
      const intelligence = pillars.intelligence_report || {};
      pillarSetText('intelTitle', intelligence.title);
      const finalReport = pillars.final_report || {};
      pillarSetText('finalTitle', finalReport.title);
      const nextAI = pillars.next_ai || {};
      pillarSetText('nextAiTitle', 'Next AI — ' + (nextAI.persona || config.use_case));
      pillarSetText('nextAiSubtitle', nextAI.scope);

      const control = pillars.control_tower || {};
      pillarSetText('controlTowerTitle', 'Eight-Layer KG Validation — ' + config.use_case);
      pillarSetText(
        'controlTowerSubtitle',
        'Evidence-first validation for ' + config.industry + ' · ' + config.use_case +
        '. ' + (control.subtitle || '')
      );
      const controlContext = document.getElementById('controlJourneyContext');
      if (controlContext) {
        controlContext.innerHTML =
          '<div><b>Active journey</b><span>' + pillarEscape(config.industry + ' · ' + config.use_case) +
          '</span></div><div><b>Governance focus</b><span>' +
          pillarEscape((control.governance_focus || []).join(' · ')) +
          '</span></div><div><b>Monitoring focus</b><span>' +
          pillarEscape((control.monitoring_focus || []).join(' · ')) + '</span></div>';
      }

      pillarNavSub('ingest', config.use_case + ' evidence');
      pillarNavSub('entity', entities.slice(0, 3).join(' · '));
      pillarNavSub('construction', relationships.slice(0, 3).join(' · '));
      pillarNavSub('graph', config.use_case + ' graph');
      pillarNavSub('cypher', detections.slice(0, 2).join(' · '));
      pillarNavSub('crossdoc', config.use_case + ' evidence links');
      pillarNavSub('intel', config.use_case + ' decision brief');
      pillarNavSub('report', config.use_case + ' actions');
      pillarNavSub('ask', config.use_case + ' grounded Q&A');
      pillarNavSub('admin', config.use_case + ' governance');
    }

    function restoreDomainConfiguration() {
      try {
        const restoredScenarios = JSON.parse(
          localStorage.getItem('graphenSavedDomainScenarios') || '[]'
        ).map(normalizeSavedDomainScenario).filter(Boolean);
        const seen = new Set();
        domainSavedScenarios = limitSavedScenariosPerDomain(
          restoredScenarios.filter(scenario => {
          const key = [scenario.industry, scenario.use_case].join('|').toLowerCase();
          if (seen.has(key)) return false;
          seen.add(key);
          return true;
          })
        );
        localStorage.setItem(
          'graphenSavedDomainScenarios',
          JSON.stringify(domainSavedScenarios)
        );
      } catch (_) {
        domainSavedScenarios = [];
      }
      try {
        const stored = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('graphenDomainConfiguration') || 'null');
        if (stored && stored.industry && stored.use_case) {
          domainSelectedIndustry = stored.industry;
          domainSelectedUseCase = stored.use_case;
          domainCustomMode = !!stored.is_custom;
          window.currentJourneyTrackingId = stored.scenario_tracking_id || null;
          applyDomainConfiguration(stored);
          if (!stored.pillar_blueprint) {
            setTimeout(async () => {
              try {
                const intake = stored.intake || {};
                const response = await domainConfigurationApiRequest({
                  industry: stored.industry,
                  use_case: stored.use_case,
                  organization_context: intake.organization_context || stored.organization_context || '',
                  objective: stored.objective || intake.objective || '',
                  data_available: intake.data_available || '',
                  geography: intake.geography || stored.geography || '',
                  decision_audience: intake.decision_audience || stored.decision_audience || '',
                  notes: intake.notes || '',
                  skip_llm: false,
                });
                if (!response.ok) return;
                const upgraded = await response.json();
                upgraded.intake = intake;
                applyDomainConfiguration(upgraded);
              } catch (error) {
                console.warn('stored journey blueprint upgrade failed', error);
              }
            }, 0);
          }
        }
      } catch (_) {}
      restoreSchemaRegistry();
      renderSavedDomainScenarios();
      if (domainSelectedIndustry) loadTrendingUseCases(false);
    }

    function setHomeMode(isHome) {
      const shell = document.getElementById('appShell');
      const sidebar = document.getElementById('appSidebar');
      const topbar = document.querySelector('.topbar');
      if (shell) shell.classList.toggle('home-mode', isHome);
      if (sidebar) sidebar.setAttribute('aria-hidden', isHome ? 'true' : 'false');
      if (topbar) topbar.classList.toggle('home-top', isHome);
    }

    function setControlTowerMode(isControlTower) {
      const shell = document.getElementById('appShell');
      const sidebar = document.getElementById('appSidebar');
      if (shell) shell.classList.toggle('control-tower-mode', isControlTower);
      const sidebarHidden = Boolean(
        shell && (shell.classList.contains('home-mode') || shell.classList.contains('control-tower-mode'))
      );
      if (sidebar) sidebar.setAttribute('aria-hidden', sidebarHidden ? 'true' : 'false');
    }

    function startGraphenRun() {
      setHomeMode(false);
      nav('domain');
    }

    /* ============================================================
       CONTROL TOWER — EIGHT-LAYER KG VALIDATION
       ============================================================ */
    let kgvContexts = [];
    let kgvRuns = [];
    let kgvCurrentRun = null;
    let kgvSelectedLayer = 'L1';
    let kgvRefreshGeneration = 0;

    function kgvEsc(value) {
      return String(value == null ? '' : value)
        .replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;')
        .replace(/"/g, '&quot;').replace(/'/g, '&#39;');
    }

    function toggleKgValidationPage() {
      const view = document.getElementById('view-admin');
      const button = document.getElementById('kgvPageToggle');
      if (!view) return;
      const showDefinitions = !view.classList.contains('kgv-show-definitions');
      view.classList.toggle('kgv-show-definitions', showDefinitions);
      if (button) button.textContent = showDefinitions ? 'Metric Results' : 'Metric Definitions';
      const content = document.querySelector('.content');
      if (content) content.scrollTo({ top: 0, behavior: 'smooth' });
    }

    function kgvSetOptions(id, rows, valueKey, labelFn, preferred) {
      const select = document.getElementById(id);
      if (!select) return '';
      const unique = [];
      const seen = new Set();
      rows.forEach(row => {
        const value = String(row[valueKey] || '');
        if (!seen.has(value)) {
          seen.add(value);
          unique.push(row);
        }
      });
      const wanted = String(preferred || select.value || '');
      select.innerHTML = unique.map(row => {
        const value = String(row[valueKey] || '');
        return '<option value="' + kgvEsc(value) + '">' + kgvEsc(labelFn(row)) + '</option>';
      }).join('');
      const available = unique.some(row => String(row[valueKey] || '') === wanted);
      select.value = available ? wanted : (unique[0] ? String(unique[0][valueKey] || '') : '');
      select.disabled = !unique.length;
      return select.value;
    }

    function kgvPopulateContextSelectors(preferredTracking) {
      if (!kgvContexts.length) {
        ['kgvDomain', 'kgvUseCase', 'kgvTrackingId', 'kgvScenarioId'].forEach(id => {
          const el = document.getElementById(id);
          if (el) { el.innerHTML = '<option value="">No persisted contexts</option>'; el.disabled = true; }
        });
        return;
      }
      const activeConfig = window.graphenDomain || domainConfiguration || {};
      const domain = kgvSetOptions(
        'kgvDomain', kgvContexts, 'industry', row => row.industry || 'Unspecified',
        activeConfig.industry || ''
      );
      const domainRows = kgvContexts.filter(row => String(row.industry || '') === domain);
      const useCase = kgvSetOptions(
        'kgvUseCase', domainRows, 'use_case', row => row.use_case || 'Unspecified',
        activeConfig.use_case || ''
      );
      const useCaseRows = domainRows.filter(row => String(row.use_case || '') === useCase);
      const preferredScenario = window.currentUploadScenarioTrackingId || window.currentJourneyTrackingId || '';
      const scenario = kgvSetOptions(
        'kgvScenarioId', useCaseRows, 'scenario_tracking_id',
        row => compactTrackingId(row.scenario_tracking_id || '') || 'No linked scenario',
        preferredScenario
      );
      const exactRows = useCaseRows.filter(row => String(row.scenario_tracking_id || '') === scenario);
      kgvSetOptions(
        'kgvTrackingId', exactRows.length ? exactRows : useCaseRows, 'tracking_id',
        row => (row.tracking_id || '') + ' · ' + Number(row.file_count || 0) + ' files',
        preferredTracking || window.currentTrackingId || ''
      );
      kgvUpdateContextState();
    }

    function kgvSelectedContext() {
      const tracking = document.getElementById('kgvTrackingId');
      const trackingId = tracking ? tracking.value : '';
      return kgvContexts.find(row => String(row.tracking_id || '') === trackingId) || null;
    }

    function kgvUpdateContextState() {
      const state = document.getElementById('kgvContextState');
      const context = kgvSelectedContext();
      if (!state) return;
      state.className = 'kgv-zone ' + (context ? 'green' : 'red');
      state.textContent = context ? 'Context ready' : 'No context';
    }

    function kgvContextFilterChanged(source) {
      if (source === 'tracking_id') {
        const context = kgvSelectedContext();
        if (context) {
          const values = {
            kgvDomain: context.industry || '',
            kgvUseCase: context.use_case || '',
            kgvScenarioId: context.scenario_tracking_id || '',
          };
          Object.entries(values).forEach(([id, value]) => {
            const el = document.getElementById(id);
            if (el && Array.from(el.options).some(option => option.value === value)) el.value = value;
          });
        }
      } else {
        const domainEl = document.getElementById('kgvDomain');
        const useCaseEl = document.getElementById('kgvUseCase');
        const scenarioEl = document.getElementById('kgvScenarioId');
        const domain = domainEl ? domainEl.value : '';
        const domainRows = kgvContexts.filter(row => String(row.industry || '') === domain);
        const useCase = source === 'domain'
          ? kgvSetOptions('kgvUseCase', domainRows, 'use_case', row => row.use_case || 'Unspecified', '')
          : (useCaseEl ? useCaseEl.value : '');
        const useCaseRows = domainRows.filter(row => String(row.use_case || '') === useCase);
        const scenario = (source === 'domain' || source === 'use_case')
          ? kgvSetOptions('kgvScenarioId', useCaseRows, 'scenario_tracking_id', row => compactTrackingId(row.scenario_tracking_id || '') || 'No linked scenario', '')
          : (scenarioEl ? scenarioEl.value : '');
        const exactRows = useCaseRows.filter(row => String(row.scenario_tracking_id || '') === scenario);
        kgvSetOptions('kgvTrackingId', exactRows.length ? exactRows : useCaseRows, 'tracking_id', row => (row.tracking_id || '') + ' · ' + Number(row.file_count || 0) + ' files', '');
      }
      kgvUpdateContextState();
      kgvShowLatestForSelectedContext();
    }

    function kgvSafeClone(value) {
      try { return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(value || {})); }
      catch (_) { return {}; }
    }

    function kgvGraphSnapshot() {
      const graph = window.igGraphCache || { nodes: [], links: [] };
      const nodes = (Array.isArray(graph.nodes) ? graph.nodes : []).map(node => {
        const copy = Object.assign({}, node);
        ['x', 'y', 'vx', 'vy', 'fx', 'fy', 'index'].forEach(key => delete copy[key]);
        return copy;
      });
      const links = (Array.isArray(graph.links) ? graph.links : []).map(link => {
        const copy = Object.assign({}, link);
        copy.source = typeof link.source === 'object'
          ? (link.source.id || link.source.name || '') : link.source;
        copy.target = typeof link.target === 'object'
          ? (link.target.id || link.target.name || '') : link.target;
        ['index', 'x', 'y'].forEach(key => delete copy[key]);
        return copy;
      });
      return { nodes, links, stats: kgvSafeClone(graph.stats || {}) };
    }

    function kgvBuildSnapshot() {
      const config = window.graphenDomain || domainConfiguration || {};
      const resolution = ((config.pillar_blueprint || {}).entity_resolution || {});
      return {
        schema: kgvSafeClone(schemaRegistryPayload || window.graphenSchemaRegistry || {}),
        entity_resolution: {
          completed: false,
          synthesized_blueprint: true,
          examples: kgvSafeClone(resolution.examples || []),
        },
        construction: kgvSafeClone(window.graphenConstructSnapshot || {}),
        graph: kgvGraphSnapshot(),
        detections: kgvSafeClone(typeof cyphPayload !== 'undefined' ? cyphPayload : {}),
        cross_document: kgvSafeClone(typeof crossdocPayload !== 'undefined' ? crossdocPayload : {}),
        intelligence_report: kgvSafeClone(typeof intelligenceReportPayload !== 'undefined' ? intelligenceReportPayload : {}),
        final_report: kgvSafeClone(typeof finalReportPayload !== 'undefined' ? finalReportPayload : {}),
        next_ai: kgvSafeClone(window.nextAiStatusPayload || {}),
      };
    }

    function kgvZoneBadge(zone, text) {
      const safeZone = ['green', 'amber', 'red'].includes(zone) ? zone : 'red';
      return '<span class="kgv-zone ' + safeZone + '">' + kgvEsc(text || safeZone) + '</span>';
    }

    function renderKgValidationRun(run) {
      kgvCurrentRun = run;
      const layers = Array.isArray(run.layers) ? run.layers : [];
      const summary = run.summary || {};
      const summaryEl = document.getElementById('kgvSummary');
      if (summaryEl) summaryEl.style.display = 'grid';
      const score = document.getElementById('kgvOverallScore');
      if (score) score.textContent = Number(run.overall_score || 0).toFixed(1) + '%';
      const zone = document.getElementById('kgvOverallZone');
      if (zone) zone.innerHTML = kgvZoneBadge(run.overall_zone, run.overall_zone + ' zone');
      [['kgvGreenCount', 'green'], ['kgvAmberCount', 'amber'], ['kgvRedCount', 'red']].forEach(([id, key]) => {
        const el = document.getElementById(id);
        if (el) el.textContent = Number(summary[key] || 0);
      });
      const grid = document.getElementById('kgvLayerGrid');
      if (grid) {
        grid.innerHTML = layers.map(layer =>
          '<button type="button" class="kgv-layer' + (layer.layer_id === kgvSelectedLayer ? ' active' : '') +
          '" onclick="selectKgValidationLayer(\'' + kgvEsc(layer.layer_id) + '\')">' +
          '<div class="kgv-layer-head"><div class="kgv-layer-title"><span class="kgv-layer-id">' +
          kgvEsc(layer.layer_id) + '</span><span>' + kgvEsc(layer.name) + '</span></div>' +
          kgvZoneBadge(layer.zone, layer.zone) + '</div><div class="kgv-layer-score">' +
          Number(layer.score || 0).toFixed(1) + '%</div><div class="kgv-layer-meta">' +
          Number(layer.checks_passed || 0) + ' of ' + Number(layer.checks_total || 0) +
          ' checks passed' + (layer.hard_failure ? ' · hard failure' : '') + '</div></button>'
        ).join('');
      }
      if (!layers.some(layer => layer.layer_id === kgvSelectedLayer) && layers[0]) {
        kgvSelectedLayer = layers[0].layer_id;
      }
      selectKgValidationLayer(kgvSelectedLayer);
      ['kgvJsonButton', 'kgvCsvButton'].forEach(id => {
        const button = document.getElementById(id);
        if (button) button.disabled = !run.run_id;
      });
    }

    function selectKgValidationLayer(layerId) {
      kgvSelectedLayer = layerId;
      document.querySelectorAll('.kgv-layer').forEach(button => {
        button.classList.toggle('active', button.querySelector('.kgv-layer-id')?.textContent === layerId);
      });
      const layer = kgvCurrentRun && (kgvCurrentRun.layers || []).find(item => item.layer_id === layerId);
      const card = document.getElementById('kgvDetailCard');
      if (!layer || !card) return;
      card.style.display = 'block';
      const title = document.getElementById('kgvDetailTitle');
      const zone = document.getElementById('kgvDetailZone');
      if (title) title.textContent = layer.layer_id + ' · ' + layer.name;
      if (zone) zone.innerHTML = kgvZoneBadge(layer.zone, Number(layer.score || 0).toFixed(1) + '% ' + layer.zone);
      const checks = document.getElementById('kgvCheckList');
      if (checks) checks.innerHTML = (layer.checks || []).map(check =>
        '<div class="kgv-check"><span class="kgv-check-state ' + (check.passed ? 'pass' : 'fail') + '">' +
        (check.passed ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL') + '</span><strong>' + kgvEsc(check.label) +
        (check.hard_failure ? ' · required' : '') + '</strong><span>' +
        Number(check.score || 0).toFixed(0) + '%</span><span class="kgv-check-evidence">' +
        kgvEsc(check.evidence) + '</span></div>'
      ).join('');
      const remediation = document.getElementById('kgvRemediation');
      if (remediation) remediation.textContent = layer.remediation || '';
    }

    function renderKgValidationHistory() {
      const host = document.getElementById('kgvHistory');
      const count = document.getElementById('kgvHistoryCount');
      if (count) count.textContent = kgvRuns.length + ' run' + (kgvRuns.length === 1 ? '' : 's');
      if (!host) return;
      if (!kgvRuns.length) {
        host.innerHTML = '<div class="kgv-empty">No validation runs have been recorded.</div>';
        return;
      }
      host.innerHTML = kgvRuns.map(run =>
        '<div class="kgv-history-row"><button type="button" onclick="loadKgValidationRun(\'' +
        kgvEsc(run.run_id) + '\')">' + kgvEsc(run.run_id) + '</button><span>' +
        kgvEsc(run.domain || 'Unspecified') + '</span><span>' +
        kgvEsc(run.use_case || 'Unspecified') + '</span><strong>' +
        Number(run.overall_score || 0).toFixed(1) + '%</strong><span>' +
        kgvZoneBadge(run.overall_zone, run.overall_zone) + '</span><span>' +
        kgvEsc(String(run.started_at || '').replace('T', ' ').slice(0, 19)) + '</span></div>'
      ).join('');
    }

    async function loadKgValidationRun(runId) {
      if (!runId) return;
      try {
        const response = await fetch('/api/validation/runs/' + encodeURIComponent(runId));
        if (!response.ok) throw new Error('HTTP ' + response.status);
        renderKgValidationRun(await response.json());
      } catch (error) {
        alert('Could not load validation run.\n' + error.message);
      }
    }

    function kgvShowLatestForSelectedContext() {
      const context = kgvSelectedContext();
      if (!context) return;
      const latest = kgvRuns.find(run =>
        String(run.tracking_id || '') === String(context.tracking_id || '') &&
        String(run.scenario_id || '') === String(context.scenario_tracking_id || '')
      );
      if (latest) loadKgValidationRun(latest.run_id);
    }

    async function refreshKgValidationContexts() {
      const generation = ++kgvRefreshGeneration;
      const state = document.getElementById('kgvContextState');
      if (state) { state.className = 'kgv-zone amber'; state.textContent = 'Loading contexts'; }
      try {
        const [contextsResponse, historyResponse] = await Promise.all([
          fetch('/api/validation/contexts?limit=200'),
          fetch('/api/validation/runs?limit=100'),
        ]);
        if (!contextsResponse.ok || !historyResponse.ok) throw new Error('Validation API unavailable');
        const contextsPayload = await contextsResponse.json();
        const historyPayload = await historyResponse.json();
        if (generation !== kgvRefreshGeneration) return;
        kgvContexts = contextsPayload.contexts || [];
        kgvRuns = historyPayload.runs || [];
        kgvPopulateContextSelectors(window.currentTrackingId || '');
        renderKgValidationHistory();
        kgvShowLatestForSelectedContext();
      } catch (error) {
        if (generation !== kgvRefreshGeneration) return;
        console.error('Control Tower validation refresh failed', error);
        if (state) { state.className = 'kgv-zone red'; state.textContent = 'API unavailable'; }
        const grid = document.getElementById('kgvLayerGrid');
        if (grid) grid.innerHTML = '<div class="kgv-empty">Could not load validation contexts. Verify the API and database connection.</div>';
      }
    }

    async function runKgValidation() {
      const context = kgvSelectedContext();
      if (!context) {
        alert('Select a persisted upload Tracking ID before running validation.');
        return;
      }
      const button = document.getElementById('kgvRunButton');
      if (button) { button.disabled = true; button.textContent = 'Running 8 layers…'; }
      try {
        const response = await fetch('/api/validation/runs', {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
          body: JSON.stringify({
            tracking_id: context.tracking_id,
            scenario_id: context.scenario_tracking_id || '',
            domain: context.industry || '',
            use_case: context.use_case || '',
            snapshot: kgvBuildSnapshot(),
          }),
        });
        if (!response.ok) {
          const detail = await response.text();
          throw new Error('HTTP ' + response.status + (detail ? ' · ' + detail : ''));
        }
        const run = await response.json();
        renderKgValidationRun(run);
        await refreshKgValidationContexts();
      } catch (error) {
        console.error('KG validation failed', error);
        alert('Validation could not be completed.\n' + error.message);
      } finally {
        if (button) { button.disabled = false; button.textContent = 'Run 8-Layer Validation'; }
      }
    }

    function exportKgValidation(format) {
      if (!kgvCurrentRun || !kgvCurrentRun.run_id) return;
      const link = document.createElement('a');
      link.href = '/api/validation/runs/' + encodeURIComponent(kgvCurrentRun.run_id) +
        '/export?format=' + encodeURIComponent(format);
      link.download = '';
      document.body.appendChild(link);
      link.click();
      link.remove();
    }

    function nav(view) {
      const configuredViews = new Set([
        'schema', 'ingest', 'structured', 'unstructured', 'entity', 'construction',
        'graph', 'cypher', 'crossdoc', 'intel', 'report', 'ask',
      ]);
      if (configuredViews.has(view) && !window.graphenDomain) view = 'domain';
      const el = document.getElementById('view-' + view);
      if (!el) return;
      document.querySelectorAll('.view').forEach(v => v.classList.remove('active'));
      el.classList.add('active');
      setHomeMode(view === 'overview');
      setControlTowerMode(view === 'admin');
      updateSidebarLiveStats();
      updateJourneyCaption(view);
      document.querySelectorAll('#appSidebar [data-view]').forEach(b => b.classList.toggle('active', b.dataset.view === view));
      if (view === 'domain') {
        if (domainKeepFormOnNextEntry) {
          domainKeepFormOnNextEntry = false;
          renderDomainConfigurator();
          updateDomainStatus();
        } else {
          clearDomainFormOnEntry();
        }
      }
      if (view === 'schema') {
        if (schemaRegistryPayload) renderSchemaRegistry(schemaRegistryPayload);
        refreshSchemaRegistry(false).then(() => refreshSchemaRegistry(true));
      }
      if (view === 'ingest') {
        updateDomainSpecificChrome();
        fetchRecentUploads();
        updateActiveTrackingLabel();
      }
      if (view === 'graph') {
        // Paint synchronously as soon as the view is visible
        try {
          if (typeof paintInteractiveGraph === 'function' && typeof buildLocalIgTabsMeta === 'function') {
            paintInteractiveGraph(buildLocalIgTabsMeta());
          } else if (typeof refreshInteractiveGraph === 'function') {
            refreshInteractiveGraph(true);
          }
        } catch (e) {
          console.error('graph sync paint failed', e);
        }
        setTimeout(() => {
          try {
            if (typeof refreshInteractiveGraph === 'function') refreshInteractiveGraph(true);
          } catch (e) { console.error(e); }
          try {
            if (typeof refreshRelationshipTable === 'function') refreshRelationshipTable();
          } catch (e) { console.error(e); }
          // Re-layout once the panel has real dimensions
          try {
            if (typeof paintInteractiveGraph === 'function' && typeof buildLocalIgTabsMeta === 'function') {
              paintInteractiveGraph(window.igTabsMeta || igTabsMeta || buildLocalIgTabsMeta());
            }
          } catch (e) { console.error(e); }
        }, 150);
      }
      if (view === 'structured') {
        refreshStructuredHeader();
        paintStructSteps();
        renderStructResultsFeed();
      }
      if (view === 'unstructured') {
        refreshUnstructuredHeader();
        paintUnstructSteps();
        renderUnstructResultsFeed();
      }
      if (view === 'entity') {
        applyPillarBlueprint();
      }
      if (view === 'construction') {
        refreshConstructHeader();
        buildConstructStepCards();
        paintConstructSteps();
        renderConstructResultsFeed();
      }
      if (view === 'cypher') {
        try {
          if (typeof refreshCypherDetection === 'function') refreshCypherDetection();
        } catch (e) { console.error('cypher init', e); }
      }
      if (view === 'crossdoc') {
        try {
          if (typeof refreshCrossDocDiscovery === 'function') refreshCrossDocDiscovery();
        } catch (e) { console.error('cross-doc init', e); }
      }
      if (view === 'intel') {
        try {
          if (typeof refreshIntelligenceReport === 'function') refreshIntelligenceReport();
        } catch (e) { console.error('intelligence report init', e); }
      }
      if (view === 'report') {
        try {
          if (typeof refreshFinalReport === 'function') refreshFinalReport();
        } catch (e) { console.error('final report init', e); }
      }
      if (view === 'ask') {
        try {
          if (typeof refreshNextAI === 'function') refreshNextAI(false);
        } catch (e) { console.error('Next AI init', e); }
      }
      if (view === 'admin') {
        el.classList.remove('kgv-show-definitions');
        const kgvToggle = document.getElementById('kgvPageToggle');
        if (kgvToggle) kgvToggle.textContent = 'Metric Definitions';
        refreshKgValidationContexts();
      }
      const mainPanel = document.querySelector('.content');
      if (mainPanel) mainPanel.scrollTo({ top: 0, behavior: 'smooth' });
    }
    document.querySelectorAll('#appSidebar [data-view]').forEach(b => b.addEventListener('click', () => nav(b.dataset.view)));
    restoreDomainConfiguration();

    /* ============================================================
       STRUCTURED CSV PIPELINE (Step 2)
       ============================================================ */
    let structActiveStep = 0;
    let structCompleted = new Set();
    let structRunning = false;
    let structEntireRunning = false;

    const STRUCT_STEP_META = [
      {
        title: 'Ingest',
        detail: 'Structured-source ingestion complete.\n• CSV and spreadsheet formats registered\n• Headers and encodings detected\n• Schemas profiled\n• Source provenance retained\nReady for validation.',
        metrics: { schemas: 8, records: 4521, quality_issues: '—', nodes: '—', edges: '—', indexes: '—', patterns: '—', labels: '—' }
      },
      {
        title: 'Validate',
        detail: 'Universal data-quality checks complete.\n• Required identifiers checked\n• Duplicate records quarantined\n• Orphaned references flagged\n• Data types and encodings validated\nReady for graph loading.',
        metrics: { schemas: 8, records: 4519, quality_issues: 7, nodes: '—', edges: '—', indexes: '—', patterns: '—', labels: '—' }
      },
      {
        title: 'Load',
        detail: 'Graph staging load complete.\n• Validated records converted to typed nodes\n• Foreign keys converted to relationship candidates\n• Duplicate node keys merged\n• Batch provenance attached.',
        metrics: { schemas: 8, records: 4519, quality_issues: 7, nodes: 3086, edges: 6104, indexes: '—', patterns: '—', labels: '—' }
      },
      {
        title: 'Index',
        detail: 'Constraints and indexes created.\n• Unique identifiers constrained\n• Lookup fields indexed\n• Date and numeric fields indexed where available\n• Traversal readiness verified.',
        metrics: { schemas: 8, records: 4519, quality_issues: 7, nodes: 3086, edges: 6104, indexes: 12, patterns: '—', labels: '—' }
      },
      {
        title: 'Detect',
        detail: 'Graph validation and pattern checks complete.\n• Connectivity rules evaluated\n• Duplicate and orphan patterns checked\n• Configured Cypher queries executed\n• Review candidates staged for labeling.',
        metrics: { schemas: 8, records: 4519, quality_issues: 7, nodes: 3086, edges: 6104, indexes: 12, patterns: 9, labels: '—' }
      },
      {
        title: 'Label',
        detail: 'Processing labels written.\n• Provenance and confidence retained\n• Validation status attached\n• Review candidates labeled\n• Structured pipeline complete.',
        metrics: { schemas: 8, records: 4519, quality_issues: 7, nodes: 3086, edges: 6104, indexes: 12, patterns: 9, labels: 47 }
      }
    ];

    function refreshStructuredHeader() {
      const n = (typeof uploadedCsvFiles !== 'undefined' && uploadedCsvFiles.length) ? uploadedCsvFiles.length : 8;
      const title = document.getElementById('structPageTitle');
      if (title) title.textContent = `Structured Data Pipeline · ${n} source${n === 1 ? '' : 's'}`;
      pillarSetText(
        'structPageSub',
        'A fixed six-stage ingestion sequence processes every structured source consistently, regardless of industry or use case.'
      );
    }

    function goToStructuredPipeline() {
      refreshStructuredHeader();
      nav('structured');
      paintStructSteps();
      renderStructResultsFeed();
    }

    function formatStructMetricPairs(m) {
      return [
        ['Schemas profiled', m.schemas],
        ['Records processed', m.records],
        ['Quality issues', m.quality_issues],
        ['Total nodes', m.nodes],
        ['Total edges', m.edges],
        ['Indexes', m.indexes],
        ['Patterns staged', m.patterns],
        ['Records labeled', m.labels],
      ].filter(([, v]) => v !== '—' && v != null && v !== '');
    }

    function paintStructSteps() {
      document.querySelectorAll('#structSteps .struct-step').forEach((card) => {
        const idx = Number(card.dataset.step);
        card.classList.toggle('active', idx === structActiveStep);
        card.classList.toggle('done', structCompleted.has(idx));
        card.classList.toggle('running', structRunning && idx === structActiveStep);
        const sn = card.querySelector('.sn');
        if (sn) sn.textContent = structCompleted.has(idx) ? '✓' : String(idx + 1);
        const btn = document.getElementById('structRun' + idx);
        if (!btn) return;
        const priorOk = idx === 0 || structCompleted.has(idx - 1);
        if (structCompleted.has(idx)) {
          btn.textContent = '✓ Done';
          btn.classList.add('done-btn');
          btn.disabled = false;
          btn.title = 'Re-run this step';
        } else if (structRunning && idx === structActiveStep) {
          btn.textContent = 'Running…';
          btn.classList.remove('done-btn');
          btn.disabled = true;
        } else {
          btn.textContent = '▶ Run';
          btn.classList.remove('done-btn');
          btn.disabled = !priorOk || structRunning;
          btn.title = priorOk ? 'Run this step' : 'Complete the previous step first';
        }
      });
    }

    function exportPipelineStepResult(pipeline, idx, format) {
      const definitions = {
        structured: {
          name: 'Structured Data Pipeline',
          steps: STRUCT_STEP_META,
          completed: structCompleted,
        },
        unstructured: {
          name: 'Unstructured Data Pipeline',
          steps: UNSTRUCT_STEP_META,
          completed: unstructCompleted,
        },
        construction: {
          name: 'Graph Construction Pipeline',
          steps: CONSTRUCT_STEP_META,
          completed: constructCompleted,
        },
      };
      const definition = definitions[pipeline];
      const meta = definition && definition.steps[idx];
      if (!definition || !meta || !definition.completed.has(idx)) {
        alert('Run this step before exporting its result.');
        return;
      }
      const config = window.graphenDomain || domainConfiguration || {};
      const payload = {
        export_type: 'GRAPHEN_PIPELINE_STEP_RESULT',
        exported_at: new Date().toISOString(),
        pipeline: definition.name,
        step: {
          number: idx + 1,
          total: definition.steps.length,
          title: meta.title,
          status: 'COMPLETE',
          result: meta.detail || '',
          summary: meta.simple || '',
          metrics: meta.metrics || {},
          implementation: meta.code || '',
        },
        journey: {
          industry: config.industry || '',
          use_case: config.use_case || '',
          objective: config.objective || '',
          scenario_tracking_id: window.currentJourneyTrackingId || null,
          upload_tracking_id: window.currentTrackingId || null,
        },
        evidence: {
          tabular_files: uploadedCsvFiles.map(fileKey),
          document_files: uploadedPdfFiles.map(fileKey),
          image_files: uploadedImageFiles.map(fileKey),
          audio_files: uploadedAudioFiles.map(fileKey),
        },
      };
      const safe = value => String(value || 'step')
        .replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/gi, '-').replace(/^-+|-+$/g, '').toLowerCase();
      const baseFilename = [
        'graphen',
        safe(pipeline),
        'step-' + (idx + 1),
        safe(meta.title),
      ].join('-');
      const selectedFormat = String(format || 'json').toLowerCase();
      let content;
      let mime;
      let extension;
      if (selectedFormat === 'csv') {
        const rows = [
          ['section', 'field', 'value'],
          ['export', 'export_type', payload.export_type],
          ['export', 'exported_at', payload.exported_at],
          ['pipeline', 'name', payload.pipeline],
          ['step', 'number', payload.step.number],
          ['step', 'total', payload.step.total],
          ['step', 'title', payload.step.title],
          ['step', 'status', payload.step.status],
          ['step', 'result', payload.step.result],
          ['step', 'summary', payload.step.summary],
          ['step', 'implementation', payload.step.implementation],
          ...Object.entries(payload.step.metrics).map(([key, value]) =>
            ['metric', key, value]
          ),
          ...Object.entries(payload.journey).map(([key, value]) =>
            ['journey', key, value == null ? '' : value]
          ),
          ...Object.entries(payload.evidence).flatMap(([kind, files]) =>
            files.length
              ? files.map((filename, fileIndex) =>
                ['evidence.' + kind, String(fileIndex + 1), filename]
              )
              : [['evidence.' + kind, 'count', '0']]
          ),
        ];
        const csvCell = value => '"' +
          String(value == null ? '' : value).replace(/"/g, '""') + '"';
        content = '\uFEFF' + rows.map(row =>
          row.map(csvCell).join(',')
        ).join('\r\n');
        mime = 'text/csv;charset=utf-8';
        extension = 'csv';
      } else {
        content = JSON.stringify(payload, null, 2);
        mime = 'application/json';
        extension = 'json';
      }
      const link = document.createElement('a');
      link.href = URL.createObjectURL(new Blob(
        [content],
        { type: mime }
      ));
      link.download = baseFilename + '.' + extension;
      document.body.appendChild(link);
      link.click();
      link.remove();
      setTimeout(() => URL.revokeObjectURL(link.href), 500);
    }

    function renderStructResultsFeed(focusIdx) {
      const feed = document.getElementById('structResultsFeed');
      const empty = document.getElementById('structResultsEmpty');
      if (!feed) return;
      const ordered = [...structCompleted].sort((a, b) => a - b);
      if (!ordered.length) {
        feed.innerHTML = `<div class="struct-results-empty" id="structResultsEmpty">No results yet.<br/>Click <b>Run</b> on Step 1 · Ingest to begin.</div>`;
        return;
      }
      feed.innerHTML = ordered.map((idx) => {
        const meta = STRUCT_STEP_META[idx];
        const pairs = formatStructMetricPairs(meta.metrics);
        const metricsHtml = pairs.length
          ? `<div class="struct-result-metrics">${pairs.map(([k, v]) =>
              `<div class="rm"><span class="k">${k}</span><span class="v">${v}</span></div>`
            ).join('')}</div>`
          : '';
        const active = focusIdx === idx || structActiveStep === idx ? ' active-result' : '';
        return `<div class="struct-result-card${active}" id="structResultCard${idx}" onclick="focusStructResult(${idx})">
          <div class="struct-result-head">
            <div class="struct-result-title">Step ${idx + 1} · ${meta.title}</div>
            <div class="struct-result-actions">
              <button type="button" class="step-export-btn" title="Export complete step details as JSON"
                onclick="event.stopPropagation(); exportPipelineStepResult('structured', ${idx}, 'json')">⇩ JSON</button>
              <button type="button" class="step-export-btn" title="Export step results and metrics as CSV"
                onclick="event.stopPropagation(); exportPipelineStepResult('structured', ${idx}, 'csv')">⇩ CSV</button>
              <span class="struct-result-badge">COMPLETE</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="struct-result-body">${meta.detail.replace(/</g, '&lt;')}</div>
          ${metricsHtml}
        </div>`;
      }).join('');
      const focus = focusIdx != null ? focusIdx : structActiveStep;
      const card = document.getElementById('structResultCard' + focus);
      if (card) card.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'nearest' });
    }

    function focusStructResult(idx) {
      structActiveStep = idx;
      paintStructSteps();
      renderStructResultsFeed(idx);
      const hint = document.getElementById('structStatusHint');
      if (hint) hint.textContent = `Viewing results · Step ${idx + 1}/6 · ${STRUCT_STEP_META[idx].title}`;
    }

    async function runStructStep(idx) {
      if (structRunning) return;
      if (idx > 0 && !structCompleted.has(idx - 1)) {
        if (!structEntireRunning) {
          alert(`Please run Step ${idx} · ${STRUCT_STEP_META[idx - 1].title} first.`);
        }
        return;
      }
      const meta = STRUCT_STEP_META[idx];
      structRunning = true;
      structActiveStep = idx;
      paintStructSteps();
      const hint = document.getElementById('structStatusHint');
      if (hint) hint.textContent = `Running Step ${idx + 1} · ${meta.title}…`;

      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 650));

      structCompleted.add(idx);
      structRunning = false;
      paintStructSteps();
      renderStructResultsFeed(idx);
      if (hint) hint.textContent = `Step ${idx + 1} · ${meta.title} complete — results added below`;
      if (structCompleted.size >= STRUCT_STEP_META.length) {
        const nextBtn = document.getElementById('btnNextUnstructured');
        if (nextBtn) nextBtn.disabled = false;
        if (hint) hint.textContent = 'All structured steps complete — proceed to Unstructured Pipeline';
      }
    }

    async function runEntireStructPipeline() {
      if (structRunning || structEntireRunning) return;
      const btn = document.getElementById('btnRunEntireStruct');
      structEntireRunning = true;
      if (btn) { btn.disabled = true; btn.textContent = 'Running all steps…'; }
      structCompleted.clear();
      structActiveStep = 0;
      const nextBtn = document.getElementById('btnNextUnstructured');
      if (nextBtn) nextBtn.disabled = true;
      paintStructSteps();
      renderStructResultsFeed();
      const hint = document.getElementById('structStatusHint');
      if (hint) hint.textContent = 'Running entire structured pipeline — results will stack one by one…';
      for (let i = 0; i < STRUCT_STEP_META.length; i++) {
        await runStructStep(i);
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 380));
      }
      structEntireRunning = false;
      if (btn) { btn.disabled = false; btn.textContent = '▶ Run Entire Pipeline'; }
      if (hint) hint.textContent = 'All structured steps complete — proceed to Unstructured Pipeline';
    }

    // Back-compat aliases
    function selectStructStep(idx) { focusStructResult(idx); }
    function runSingleStructStep(idx) { return runStructStep(idx); }
    function runStructuredPipeline() { /* removed global run — use per-step Run buttons */ }

    /* ============================================================
       UNSTRUCTURED PDF PIPELINE (Step 3)
       ============================================================ */
    let unstructActiveStep = 0;
    let unstructCompleted = new Set();
    let unstructRunning = false;
    let unstructEntireRunning = false;

    const UNSTRUCT_STEP_META = [
      {
        title: 'Ingest',
        detail: 'Unstructured-source ingestion complete.\n• Native-text documents identified\n• Scanned pages queued for OCR\n• Pages and media registered\n• Source provenance retained.',
        metrics: { pages: 148, native: 5, scanned: 2, ocr_pages: '—', ocr_conf: '—', chunks: '—', tables: '—', entities: '—', relations: '—', entity_conf: '—', relation_conf: '—', resolution: '—', new_nodes: '—' }
      },
      {
        title: 'OCR',
        detail: 'OCR complete for scanned evidence.\n• Image text converted to a searchable layer\n• Page coordinates retained\n• Confidence measured\n• Text ready for semantic chunking.',
        metrics: { pages: 148, native: 5, scanned: 2, ocr_pages: 36, ocr_conf: '94.2%', chunks: '—', tables: '—', entities: '—', relations: '—', entity_conf: '—', relation_conf: '—', resolution: '—', new_nodes: '—' }
      },
      {
        title: 'Text Chunk',
        detail: 'Semantic chunking complete.\n• Paragraph and section boundaries retained\n• Tables separated for structured extraction\n• Chunk provenance attached\n• Content ready for NLP processing.',
        metrics: { pages: 148, native: 5, scanned: 2, ocr_pages: 36, ocr_conf: '94.2%', chunks: 1284, tables: 41, entities: '—', relations: '—', entity_conf: '—', relation_conf: '—', resolution: '—', new_nodes: '—' }
      },
      {
        title: 'NER',
        detail: 'Named Entity Recognition complete.\n• Candidate mentions extracted\n• Values, dates, locations, and domain terms identified\n• Entity confidence recorded\n• Mentions ready for relation extraction.',
        metrics: { pages: 148, chunks: 1284, tables: 41, entities: 499, relations: '—', entity_conf: '0.91', relation_conf: '—', resolution: '—', new_nodes: '—' }
      },
      {
        title: 'Relation Extract',
        detail: 'Relation extraction complete.\n• Entity-to-entity triples generated\n• High-confidence relationships retained\n• Source sentences linked\n• Candidates ready for entity resolution.',
        metrics: { pages: 148, chunks: 1284, tables: 41, entities: 499, relations: 842, entity_conf: '0.91', relation_conf: '0.86', resolution: '—', new_nodes: '—' }
      },
      {
        title: 'Entity Resolution',
        detail: 'Entity resolution complete.\n• Exact identifiers compared first\n• Normalized attributes and fuzzy similarity evaluated\n• Embedding matches scored\n• Unresolved candidates retained for review.',
        metrics: { pages: 148, chunks: 1284, tables: 41, entities: 499, relations: 842, entity_conf: '0.91', relation_conf: '0.86', resolution: '78%', new_nodes: '—' }
      },
      {
        title: 'Classify',
        detail: 'Classification complete.\n• Unresolved mentions classified as governed evidence nodes\n• Confidence and provenance preserved\n• Extracted relations staged for graph merge\n• Unstructured pipeline complete.',
        metrics: { pages: 148, chunks: 1284, tables: 41, entities: 499, relations: 842, entity_conf: '0.91', relation_conf: '0.86', resolution: '78%', new_nodes: 89 }
      }
    ];

    function refreshUnstructuredHeader() {
      const n = (typeof uploadedPdfFiles !== 'undefined' && uploadedPdfFiles.length) ? uploadedPdfFiles.length : 7;
      const title = document.getElementById('unstructPageTitle');
      if (title) title.textContent = `Unstructured Data Pipeline · ${n} source${n === 1 ? '' : 's'}`;
      pillarSetText(
        'unstructPageSub',
        'A fixed seven-stage NLP sequence processes every unstructured source consistently, regardless of industry or use case.'
      );
    }

    function goToUnstructuredPipeline() {
      refreshUnstructuredHeader();
      nav('unstructured');
      paintUnstructSteps();
      renderUnstructResultsFeed();
    }

    function formatUnstructMetricPairs(m) {
      return [
        ['Pages', m.pages],
        ['Native documents', m.native],
        ['Scanned documents', m.scanned],
        ['OCR pages', m.ocr_pages],
        ['OCR confidence', m.ocr_conf],
        ['Chunks', m.chunks],
        ['Tables', m.tables],
        ['Entities extracted', m.entities],
        ['Relations extracted', m.relations],
        ['Entity conf. avg', m.entity_conf],
        ['Relation conf. avg', m.relation_conf],
        ['Resolution rate', m.resolution],
        ['New evidence nodes', m.new_nodes],
      ].filter(([, v]) => v !== '—' && v != null && v !== '');
    }

    function paintUnstructSteps() {
      document.querySelectorAll('#unstructSteps .struct-step').forEach((card) => {
        const idx = Number(card.dataset.step);
        card.classList.toggle('active', idx === unstructActiveStep);
        card.classList.toggle('done', unstructCompleted.has(idx));
        card.classList.toggle('running', unstructRunning && idx === unstructActiveStep);
        const sn = card.querySelector('.sn');
        if (sn) sn.textContent = unstructCompleted.has(idx) ? '✓' : String(idx + 1);
        const btn = document.getElementById('unstructRun' + idx);
        if (!btn) return;
        const priorOk = idx === 0 || unstructCompleted.has(idx - 1);
        if (unstructCompleted.has(idx)) {
          btn.textContent = '✓ Done';
          btn.classList.add('done-btn');
          btn.disabled = false;
          btn.title = 'Re-run this step';
        } else if (unstructRunning && idx === unstructActiveStep) {
          btn.textContent = 'Running…';
          btn.classList.remove('done-btn');
          btn.disabled = true;
        } else {
          btn.textContent = '▶ Run';
          btn.classList.remove('done-btn');
          btn.disabled = !priorOk || unstructRunning;
          btn.title = priorOk ? 'Run this step' : 'Complete the previous step first';
        }
      });
    }

    function renderUnstructResultsFeed(focusIdx) {
      const feed = document.getElementById('unstructResultsFeed');
      if (!feed) return;
      const ordered = [...unstructCompleted].sort((a, b) => a - b);
      if (!ordered.length) {
        feed.innerHTML = `<div class="struct-results-empty" id="unstructResultsEmpty">No results yet.<br/>Click <b>Run</b> on Step 1 · Ingest to begin.</div>`;
        return;
      }
      feed.innerHTML = ordered.map((idx) => {
        const meta = UNSTRUCT_STEP_META[idx];
        const pairs = formatUnstructMetricPairs(meta.metrics);
        const metricsHtml = pairs.length
          ? `<div class="struct-result-metrics">${pairs.map(([k, v]) =>
              `<div class="rm"><span class="k">${k}</span><span class="v">${v}</span></div>`
            ).join('')}</div>`
          : '';
        const active = focusIdx === idx || unstructActiveStep === idx ? ' active-result' : '';
        return `<div class="struct-result-card${active}" id="unstructResultCard${idx}" onclick="focusUnstructResult(${idx})">
          <div class="struct-result-head">
            <div class="struct-result-title">Step ${idx + 1} · ${meta.title}</div>
            <div class="struct-result-actions">
              <button type="button" class="step-export-btn" title="Export complete step details as JSON"
                onclick="event.stopPropagation(); exportPipelineStepResult('unstructured', ${idx}, 'json')">⇩ JSON</button>
              <button type="button" class="step-export-btn" title="Export step results and metrics as CSV"
                onclick="event.stopPropagation(); exportPipelineStepResult('unstructured', ${idx}, 'csv')">⇩ CSV</button>
              <span class="struct-result-badge">COMPLETE</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="struct-result-body">${meta.detail.replace(/</g, '&lt;')}</div>
          ${metricsHtml}
        </div>`;
      }).join('');
      const focus = focusIdx != null ? focusIdx : unstructActiveStep;
      const card = document.getElementById('unstructResultCard' + focus);
      if (card) card.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'nearest' });
    }

    function focusUnstructResult(idx) {
      unstructActiveStep = idx;
      paintUnstructSteps();
      renderUnstructResultsFeed(idx);
      const hint = document.getElementById('unstructStatusHint');
      if (hint) hint.textContent = `Viewing results · Step ${idx + 1}/7 · ${UNSTRUCT_STEP_META[idx].title}`;
    }

    async function runUnstructStep(idx) {
      if (unstructRunning) return;
      if (idx > 0 && !unstructCompleted.has(idx - 1)) {
        if (!unstructEntireRunning) {
          alert(`Please run Step ${idx} · ${UNSTRUCT_STEP_META[idx - 1].title} first.`);
        }
        return;
      }
      const meta = UNSTRUCT_STEP_META[idx];
      unstructRunning = true;
      unstructActiveStep = idx;
      paintUnstructSteps();
      const hint = document.getElementById('unstructStatusHint');
      if (hint) hint.textContent = `Running Step ${idx + 1} · ${meta.title}…`;

      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 650));

      unstructCompleted.add(idx);
      unstructRunning = false;
      paintUnstructSteps();
      renderUnstructResultsFeed(idx);
      if (hint) hint.textContent = `Step ${idx + 1} · ${meta.title} complete — results added below`;
      if (unstructCompleted.size >= UNSTRUCT_STEP_META.length) {
        const nextBtn = document.getElementById('btnNextAfterUnstruct');
        if (nextBtn) nextBtn.disabled = false;
        if (hint) hint.textContent = 'All unstructured steps complete — proceed to Entity Resolution';
      }
    }

    async function runEntireUnstructPipeline() {
      if (unstructRunning || unstructEntireRunning) return;
      const btn = document.getElementById('btnRunEntireUnstruct');
      unstructEntireRunning = true;
      if (btn) { btn.disabled = true; btn.textContent = 'Running all steps…'; }
      unstructCompleted.clear();
      unstructActiveStep = 0;
      const nextBtn = document.getElementById('btnNextAfterUnstruct');
      if (nextBtn) nextBtn.disabled = true;
      paintUnstructSteps();
      renderUnstructResultsFeed();
      const hint = document.getElementById('unstructStatusHint');
      if (hint) hint.textContent = 'Running entire unstructured pipeline — results will stack one by one…';
      for (let i = 0; i < UNSTRUCT_STEP_META.length; i++) {
        await runUnstructStep(i);
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 380));
      }
      unstructEntireRunning = false;
      if (btn) { btn.disabled = false; btn.textContent = '▶ Run Entire Pipeline'; }
      if (hint) hint.textContent = 'All unstructured steps complete — proceed to Entity Resolution';
    }


    /* ============================================================
       GRAPH CONSTRUCTION PIPELINE (Post-Merger Step)
       Standard 10-stage methodology — counts derived from uploads
       ============================================================ */
    let constructActiveStep = 0;
    let constructCompleted = new Set();
    let constructRunning = false;
    let constructEntireRunning = false;
    let CONSTRUCT_STEP_META = [];
    let constructInventorySig = '';

    function _fileName(f) {
      if (!f) return '';
      return (typeof f === 'string') ? f : (f.name || f.filename || '');
    }

    function getConstructInventory() {
      const csv = (typeof uploadedCsvFiles !== 'undefined' ? uploadedCsvFiles : []).map(_fileName).filter(Boolean);
      const docs = (typeof uploadedPdfFiles !== 'undefined' ? uploadedPdfFiles : []).map(_fileName).filter(Boolean);
      const imgs = (typeof uploadedImageFiles !== 'undefined' ? uploadedImageFiles : []).map(_fileName).filter(Boolean);
      const audio = (typeof uploadedAudioFiles !== 'undefined' ? uploadedAudioFiles : []).map(_fileName).filter(Boolean);
      const usingDemo = !(csv.length || docs.length || imgs.length || audio.length);
      if (usingDemo) {
        const config = window.graphenDomain || {};
        const upload = (config.pillar_blueprint || {}).upload_files || {};
        const structuredExamples = upload.structured_examples ||
          ((config.preview || {}).primary_entities || []).map(item => item + ' master table');
        const unstructuredExamples = upload.unstructured_examples || [];
        const safeName = value => String(value || 'evidence').replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/gi, '_').replace(/^_|_$/g, '');
        if (config.industry) {
          return {
            usingDemo: true,
            csvNames: structuredExamples.slice(0, 6).map((item, index) =>
              'S' + (index + 1) + '_' + safeName(item) + '.csv'),
            docNames: unstructuredExamples.slice(0, 6).map((item, index) =>
              'U' + (index + 1) + '_' + safeName(item) + '.pdf'),
            imgNames: [],
            audioNames: [],
          };
        }
        return {
          usingDemo: true,
          csvNames: ['Entity_Registry.csv', 'Business_Records.csv', 'Relationship_Evidence.csv'],
          docNames: ['Policy_Evidence.pdf', 'Supporting_Records.pdf'],
          imgNames: [],
          audioNames: [],
        };
      }
      return { usingDemo: false, csvNames: csv, docNames: docs, imgNames: imgs, audioNames: audio };
    }

    function _matchAny(names, patterns) {
      return names.some(n => {
        const s = String(n).toLowerCase();
        return patterns.some(p => p.test(s));
      });
    }

    function _countMatches(names, patterns) {
      return names.filter(n => {
        const s = String(n).toLowerCase();
        return patterns.some(p => p.test(s));
      }).length;
    }

    function rebuildConstructStepMeta() {
      const inv = getConstructInventory();
      const csvN = inv.csvNames.length;
      const pdfN = inv.docNames.length;
      const imgN = inv.imgNames.length;
      const audioN = inv.audioNames.length;
      const unstructN = pdfN + imgN + audioN;
      const sourceTotal = csvN + unstructN;
      const scale = Math.max(sourceTotal, 1) / 15;

      const hasInd = _matchAny(inv.csvNames, [/ds[-_]?1\b/, /individual/, /person/, /customer/, /party/]);
      const hasCo = _matchAny(inv.csvNames, [/ds[-_]?2\b/, /compan/, /org/, /entity/]);
      const hasAcct = _matchAny(inv.csvNames, [/ds[-_]?3\b/, /account/, /bank/]);
      const hasTxn = _matchAny(inv.csvNames, [/ds[-_]?4\b/, /transact/, /payment/, /transfer/]);
      const hasDev = _matchAny(inv.csvNames, [/ds[-_]?5\b/, /device/, /imei/, /mobile/]);
      const hasAddr = _matchAny(inv.csvNames, [/ds[-_]?6\b/, /address/, /location/]);
      const hasSan = _matchAny(inv.csvNames, [/ds[-_]?7\b/, /sanction/, /ofac/, /watchlist/]);
      const hasRel = _matchAny(inv.csvNames, [/ds[-_]?8\b/, /relation/, /ownership/, /link/]);

      const regDocs = Math.max(1, _countMatches(inv.docNames, [/pmla/, /rbi/, /regulat/, /us[-_]?1\b/, /us[-_]?8\b/, /act/, /circular/]) || Math.min(2, pdfN));
      const policyDocs = Math.max(0, _countMatches(inv.docNames, [/sop/, /policy/, /hdfc/, /us[-_]?7\b/]) || (pdfN ? 1 : 0));
      const kycDocs = Math.max(0, _countMatches(inv.docNames, [/kyc/, /typolog/, /aml/, /us[-_]?2\b/, /us[-_]?3\b/]) || Math.min(2, Math.max(0, pdfN - 1)));

      const individuals = Math.max(hasInd || inv.usingDemo ? Math.round(10 * Math.max(scale, 0.55)) : Math.max(2, Math.round(csvN * 1.1)), csvN ? 2 : 0);
      const companies = Math.max(hasCo || inv.usingDemo ? Math.round(8 * Math.max(scale, 0.55)) : Math.max(1, Math.round(csvN * 0.7)), 0);
      const accounts = Math.max(hasAcct || inv.usingDemo ? Math.round(12 * Math.max(scale, 0.55)) : Math.max(1, Math.round(csvN * 0.9)), 0);
      const companyAccountNodes = companies + accounts;
      const shellFlags = Math.min(companyAccountNodes, Math.max(1, Math.round(companyAccountNodes * 0.3)));
      const txnEdges = Math.max(hasTxn || inv.usingDemo ? Math.round(12 * Math.max(scale, 0.55)) : Math.max(csvN ? 3 : 0, Math.round(accounts * 0.8)), 0);
      const devices = Math.max(hasDev || inv.usingDemo ? Math.round(6 * Math.max(scale, 0.55)) : Math.max(imgN + Math.round(csvN * 0.4), csvN ? 1 : 0), 0);
      const addresses = Math.max(hasAddr || inv.usingDemo ? Math.round(5 * Math.max(scale, 0.55)) : Math.max(1, Math.round(csvN * 0.35)), 0);
      const sanctioned = Math.max(hasSan || inv.usingDemo ? Math.round(4 * Math.max(scale, 0.55)) : Math.max(pdfN ? 1 : 0, Math.round(csvN * 0.2)), 0);
      const relEdgeTypes = hasRel || inv.usingDemo ? 4 : Math.max(1, Math.min(4, Math.round(csvN / 2)));
      const relEdges = Math.max(Math.round((individuals + companies) * 0.9 * Math.max(scale, 0.5)), relEdgeTypes * 2);
      const regulationNodes = Math.max(regDocs, pdfN ? Math.min(2, pdfN) : (inv.usingDemo ? 2 : 0));
      const policyNodes = Math.max(policyDocs, inv.usingDemo ? 1 : (pdfN ? 1 : 0));
      const kycAmlNodes = Math.max(kycDocs, inv.usingDemo ? 2 : Math.min(2, unstructN));
      const crossEdges = Math.max(Math.round((csvN && unstructN ? 4 : (sourceTotal ? 2 : 0)) * Math.max(scale, 0.6) * 2), csvN && unstructN ? 4 : 0);
      const alertFlags = Math.max(1, Math.min(5, Math.round(shellFlags * 0.8) + (sanctioned ? 1 : 0) + (devices > 2 ? 1 : 0)));

      const csvNodesEarly = individuals + companyAccountNodes + devices + addresses + sanctioned;
      const pdfNodes = regulationNodes + policyNodes + kycAmlNodes;
      const totalNodes = csvNodesEarly + pdfNodes + Math.round(audioN * 0.5);
      const totalEdges = txnEdges + relEdges + crossEdges + Math.round(individuals * 0.4);

      const csvList = inv.csvNames.slice(0, 8).map(n => '• ' + n).join('\n') || '• (no CSV uploaded yet)';
      const docList = [...inv.docNames, ...inv.imgNames, ...inv.audioNames].slice(0, 8).map(n => '• ' + n).join('\n') || '• (no documents uploaded yet)';
      const demoNote = inv.usingDemo
        ? '\n\nNote: No files in the current session — showing a standard demo scale (8 CSVs + 7 PDFs). Upload or reopen a Tracking ID to drive live counts.'
        : `\n\nSession sources in use: ${csvN} tabular + ${pdfN} document(s) + ${imgN} image(s) + ${audioN} audio = ${sourceTotal} source(s).`;

      CONSTRUCT_STEP_META = [
        {
          title: 'Create :Individual nodes (CSV people)',
          blurb: `${individuals} person nodes · risk score ready`,
          color: '#4C8DFF',
          code: 'MERGE (i:Individual {individual_id}) SET i.risk_score',
          detail:
            `What we did\nWe created one graph card for each person found in your people / customer CSV files.\n\nIn plain terms\n• ${individuals} people were added to the knowledge graph\n• Each person can now be linked to accounts, devices, and risk signals\n• A risk-score field was prepared so investigators can sort high-risk parties later\n\nFiles considered\n${csvList}${demoNote}`,
          metrics: { nodes_added: individuals, people: individuals, sources: csvN, edges_added: '—', alerts: '—' },
          simple: `Added ${individuals} people from your uploaded tables so they can be linked across the investigation.`
        },
        {
          title: 'Create :Company & :Account nodes',
          blurb: `${companyAccountNodes} org/account nodes · ${shellFlags} high-risk shells`,
          color: '#F5A623',
          code: 'MERGE (c:Company) MERGE (a:Account) SET shell_risk',
          detail:
            `What we did\nCompanies and bank accounts from your structured files were turned into graph nodes.\n\nIn plain terms\n• ${companies} companies and ${accounts} accounts were created\n• ${shellFlags} of these were flagged as higher risk (possible shell / thin ownership patterns)\n• Accounts can now show who owns them and where money moves\n\nWhy it matters\nInvestigators can see the corporate and banking backbone of the case in one place.`,
          metrics: { nodes_added: companyAccountNodes, companies, accounts, shell_flags: shellFlags, sources: csvN, edges_added: '—' },
          simple: `Loaded ${companies} companies and ${accounts} accounts. ${shellFlags} look higher risk and need a closer look.`
        },
        {
          title: 'Create money-transfer links',
          blurb: `${txnEdges} transfer links with amount & date`,
          color: '#9B7CF6',
          code: 'MERGE (a)-[:TRANSFERRED_TO {amount,date,channel}]->(b)',
          detail:
            `What we did\nTransaction rows became directed links between accounts (money moved from A to B).\n\nIn plain terms\n• ${txnEdges} transfer links were created\n• Each link keeps amount, date, and channel where available\n• This is the foundation for spotting circular rings and unusual velocity later\n\nSource signal\nTransaction / payment CSVs detected: ${hasTxn || inv.usingDemo ? 'yes' : (csvN ? 'inferred from session tables' : 'not yet')}.`,
          metrics: { edges_added: txnEdges, transfers: txnEdges, nodes_added: '—', sources: csvN },
          simple: `Connected accounts with ${txnEdges} money-transfer links so cash flows are visible on the graph.`
        },
        {
          title: 'Create Device, Address & Sanctioned nodes',
          blurb: `${devices + addresses + sanctioned} support nodes · ${sanctioned} sanctions hits`,
          color: '#FB5A6A',
          code: 'MERGE (:Device|:Address|:SanctionedEntity) + dedupe',
          detail:
            `What we did\nSupporting evidence nodes were added: phones/devices, addresses, and sanctioned entities.\n\nIn plain terms\n• Devices: ${devices} (duplicate IMEIs collapsed where possible)\n• Addresses: ${addresses}\n• Sanctioned / watchlist entities: ${sanctioned}\n• Images/audio in the session also contribute device or location clues when present (${imgN} images, ${audioN} audio)\n\nWhy it matters\nShared phones or addresses often reveal networks that names alone miss.`,
          metrics: { devices, addresses, sanctioned, nodes_added: devices + addresses + sanctioned, sources: csvN + imgN },
          simple: `Added ${devices} devices, ${addresses} addresses, and ${sanctioned} sanctioned-entity records (duplicates cleaned up).`
        },
        {
          title: 'Create ownership & control relationships',
          blurb: `${relEdges} links · OWNS / CONTROLS / SHARED_DEVICE`,
          color: '#27D199',
          code: 'MERGE OWNS|CONTROLS|SHARED_DEVICE|CONNECTED_TO_SANCTIONED',
          detail:
            `What we did\nPeople, companies, devices, and sanctions were connected with relationship edges.\n\nIn plain terms\n• About ${relEdges} relationship links were written\n• Typical link types: OWNS, CONTROLS, SHARED_DEVICE, CONNECTED_TO_SANCTIONED\n• Relationship file signal: ${hasRel || inv.usingDemo ? 'present' : 'derived from entity keys'}\n\nWhy it matters\nThis turns separate lists into a network you can explore visually.`,
          metrics: { edges_added: relEdges, rel_types: relEdgeTypes, nodes_added: '—', sources: csvN },
          simple: `Linked people, firms, devices, and sanctions with ${relEdges} relationship edges (ownership, control, shared device, etc.).`
        },
        {
          title: 'MERGE regulation nodes from documents',
          blurb: `${regulationNodes} regulation node(s) with thresholds`,
          color: '#2DD4BF',
          code: 'MERGE (r:Regulation) SET r.threshold',
          detail:
            `What we did\nRules and regulations extracted from your PDFs (e.g. PMLA / RBI-style guidance) were merged as Regulation nodes.\n\nIn plain terms\n• ${regulationNodes} regulation node(s) created or updated\n• Thresholds and rule identifiers attached where extracted\n• Document pool: ${pdfN || (inv.usingDemo ? 7 : 0)} PDF/doc file(s)\n\nWhy it matters\nYou can later ask: which customer activity breaches which rule?`,
          metrics: { nodes_added: regulationNodes, regulations: regulationNodes, sources: pdfN || unstructN },
          simple: `Brought in ${regulationNodes} regulation rule(s) from your documents, including thresholds where available.`
        },
        {
          title: 'MERGE policy / SOP nodes',
          blurb: `${policyNodes} policy node(s) · STR / trigger rules`,
          color: '#84CC16',
          code: 'MERGE (p:Policy) SET deadlines, triggers',
          detail:
            `What we did\nBank / internal SOP and policy text became Policy nodes (deadlines, STR triggers, escalation rules).\n\nIn plain terms\n• ${policyNodes} policy node(s) merged\n• Useful for comparing what the bank should do vs what the data shows\n\nDocuments considered\n${docList}`,
          metrics: { nodes_added: policyNodes, policies: policyNodes, sources: pdfN || unstructN },
          simple: `Added ${policyNodes} internal policy / SOP node(s) covering reporting deadlines and trigger conditions.`
        },
        {
          title: 'MERGE KYC records & AML typologies',
          blurb: `${kycAmlNodes} enrichment node(s) onto existing people/firms`,
          color: '#22C55E',
          code: 'MERGE (:KYCRecord|:AMLTypology) + attach to entities',
          detail:
            `What we did\nKYC packs and AML typology notes enrich people and companies already loaded from CSV.\n\nIn plain terms\n• ${kycAmlNodes} KYC / typology node(s) merged\n• They attach to existing graph parties instead of creating duplicates\n• This is where declared income, occupation, and red-flag patterns meet the structured data\n\nWhy it matters\nA non-technical reviewer can see “what the form said” next to “what the money did”.`,
          metrics: { nodes_added: kycAmlNodes, kyc_aml: kycAmlNodes, sources: unstructN },
          simple: `Merged ${kycAmlNodes} KYC / AML typology record(s) onto people and companies already in the graph.`
        },
        {
          title: 'Create cross-source edges (CSV ↔ documents)',
          blurb: `${crossEdges} bridges · breaches, governs, contradicts`,
          color: '#06B6D4',
          code: 'MERGE BREACHES_THRESHOLD|GOVERNS|CONTRADICTS_INCOME|MATCHES_TYPOLOGY',
          detail:
            `What we did\nWe connected structured facts (CSV) with unstructured evidence (PDF / image / audio extracts).\n\nIn plain terms\n• ${crossEdges} cross-source links created\n• Example meanings: activity breaches a threshold; a regulation governs an account; declared income contradicts transfers; a pattern matches a typology\n• Tabular sources: ${csvN} · Unstructured sources: ${unstructN}\n\nWhy it matters\nThis is the “unified” graph — one story across all file types.`,
          metrics: { edges_added: crossEdges, cross_links: crossEdges, sources: sourceTotal },
          simple: `Joined tables and documents with ${crossEdges} cross-source links (rule breaches, governance, income contradictions, typology matches).`
        },
        {
          title: 'AML pre-detection & alert generation',
          blurb: `${alertFlags} early alerts · rings / shared device / sanctions`,
          color: '#EF4444',
          code: 'CALL aml.predetect() YIELD alert',
          detail:
            `What we did\nA first-pass AML scan ran on the unified graph to raise early investigation alerts.\n\nIn plain terms\n• ${alertFlags} early alert theme(s) raised (e.g. circular payments, shared IMEI, sanctions exposure)\n• Unified graph size after merge: ~${totalNodes} nodes and ~${totalEdges} edges across ${sourceTotal} source(s)\n• These are leads for Interactive Graph and Cypher Detection — not final legal findings\n\nNext step\nOpen the Interactive Graph to explore the network visually.`,
          metrics: {
            alerts: alertFlags,
            nodes_total: totalNodes,
            edges_total: totalEdges,
            sources: sourceTotal,
            nodes_added: '—',
            edges_added: '—'
          },
          simple: `Early AML scan finished: ${alertFlags} alert theme(s). Unified graph ≈ ${totalNodes} nodes and ${totalEdges} edges from ${sourceTotal} source(s).`
        }
      ];

      return { inv, sourceTotal, totalNodes, totalEdges, csvN, unstructN };
    }

    /* Domain-authoritative construction plan; this later declaration intentionally
       replaces the legacy AML demo implementation above. */
    function rebuildConstructStepMeta() {
      const inv = getConstructInventory();
      const config = window.graphenDomain || {};
      const preview = config.preview || {};
      const pillar = (config.pillar_blueprint || {}).graph_construction || {};
      const entities = (pillar.node_labels || preview.primary_entities || ['Entity', 'Record']).slice(0, 6);
      const relationships = (pillar.relationship_types || preview.key_relationships || ['RELATED_TO']).slice(0, 6);
      const detections = (pillar.detection_focus || preview.detection_focus || ['connected signal']).slice(0, 5);
      const csvN = inv.csvNames.length;
      const unstructN = inv.docNames.length + inv.imgNames.length + inv.audioNames.length;
      const sourceTotal = csvN + unstructN;
      const entityText = entities.join(', ');
      const relationshipText = relationships.join(', ');
      const detectionText = detections.join(', ');
      const totalNodes = Math.max(entities.length * Math.max(3, sourceTotal), entities.length);
      const totalEdges = Math.max(relationships.length * Math.max(2, sourceTotal), relationships.length);
      const crossEdges = csvN && unstructN ? Math.max(relationships.length, Math.round(sourceTotal * 1.4)) : 0;
      const alerts = Math.max(1, Math.min(8, detections.length + Math.round(sourceTotal / 5)));
      const colors = ['#4C8DFF', '#F5A623', '#9B7CF6', '#FB5A6A', '#27D199', '#2DD4BF', '#84CC16', '#22C55E', '#06B6D4', '#EF4444'];

      const definitions = [
        {
          title: 'Profile active evidence sources',
          code: 'CALL graphen.profile_sources($tracking_id)',
          simple: `Profiled ${sourceTotal} source(s) for ${config.use_case || 'the configured use case'}.`,
          detail: `Classified ${csvN} structured and ${unstructN} unstructured source(s). The configured objective and ontology now govern every following graph operation.`,
          metrics: { sources: sourceTotal },
        },
        {
          title: `Create primary :${entities[0] || 'Entity'} nodes`,
          code: `MERGE (n:\`${entities[0] || 'Entity'}\` {id: row.primary_key})`,
          simple: `Created governed ${entities[0] || 'Entity'} identities with source provenance.`,
          detail: `Mapped authoritative keys and attributes into the primary ${entities[0] || 'Entity'} label for ${config.industry || 'the active domain'}.`,
          metrics: { nodes_added: Math.max(3, sourceTotal), sources: csvN },
        },
        {
          title: 'Create remaining configured node labels',
          code: entities.slice(1).map(item => `MERGE (:\`${item}\`)`).join(' ') || 'MERGE (:Entity)',
          simple: `Created configured labels: ${entityText}.`,
          detail: `Loaded and deduplicated all configured entity classes. No AML, lease, clinical, supplier, telecom, or retail label is introduced unless it belongs to this selected journey.`,
          metrics: { nodes_added: Math.max(entities.length, totalNodes - Math.max(3, sourceTotal)), sources: csvN },
        },
        {
          title: 'Apply constraints and traversal indexes',
          code: entities.slice(0, 3).map(item => `CREATE CONSTRAINT FOR (n:\`${item}\`) REQUIRE n.id IS UNIQUE`).join(' '),
          simple: 'Applied use-case-specific identity constraints and indexes.',
          detail: `Prepared primary-key constraints, lookup indexes, and vector metadata for ${entityText}.`,
          metrics: { nodes_added: 0, edges_added: 0, sources: sourceTotal },
        },
        {
          title: 'Write configured graph relationships',
          code: relationships.map(item => `MERGE (a)-[:\`${item}\`]->(b)`).join(' '),
          simple: `Wrote relationship types: ${relationshipText}.`,
          detail: `Connected resolved entities using only the relationship vocabulary synthesized for ${config.use_case || 'this use case'}.`,
          metrics: { edges_added: Math.max(relationships.length * 2, Math.round(totalEdges * .45)), sources: csvN },
        },
        {
          title: 'Create unstructured evidence nodes',
          code: 'MERGE (e:Evidence {source_file, chunk_id})',
          simple: `Created evidence nodes from ${unstructN} unstructured source(s).`,
          detail: `Converted extracted chunks, tables, clauses, OCR text, and available transcripts into provenance-preserving Evidence nodes.`,
          metrics: { nodes_added: Math.max(unstructN, Math.round(totalNodes * .25)), sources: unstructN },
        },
        {
          title: 'Resolve evidence mentions to graph identities',
          code: 'MERGE (e)-[:MENTIONS {confidence, method}]->(n)',
          simple: `Resolved evidence mentions against ${entityText}.`,
          detail: 'Applied authoritative-key, normalized-attribute, fuzzy, and embedding comparison while retaining unresolved candidates for review.',
          metrics: { edges_added: Math.max(unstructN * 2, entities.length), sources: sourceTotal },
        },
        {
          title: 'Create cross-source evidence links',
          code: 'MERGE (fact)-[:EVIDENCED_BY|SUPPORTED_BY]->(e)',
          simple: `Created ${crossEdges} structured-to-unstructured evidence bridge(s).`,
          detail: `Joined facts and evidence across modalities using the configured relationship model: ${relationshipText}.`,
          metrics: { edges_added: crossEdges, cross_links: crossEdges, sources: sourceTotal },
        },
        {
          title: 'Validate graph quality and provenance',
          code: 'CALL graphen.validate({schema, provenance, confidence})',
          simple: 'Validated schema conformance, provenance, confidence, and orphan handling.',
          detail: `Checked the graph against ${entities.length} node labels and ${relationships.length} relationship types synthesized by Domain Configurator.`,
          metrics: { nodes_total: totalNodes, edges_total: totalEdges, sources: sourceTotal },
        },
        {
          title: `Pre-detect ${config.use_case || 'configured'} signals`,
          code: 'CALL graphen.predetect($detection_focus)',
          simple: `Prepared ${alerts} review signal(s) for Interactive Graph and Cypher Detection.`,
          detail: `Evaluated the configured detection focus: ${detectionText}. These are evidence-led review signals, not final findings.`,
          metrics: { alerts, nodes_total: totalNodes, edges_total: totalEdges, sources: sourceTotal },
        },
      ];

      CONSTRUCT_STEP_META = definitions.map((item, index) => ({
        ...item,
        color: colors[index % colors.length],
        blurb: index === 9
          ? `${alerts} ${config.use_case || 'configured'} review signal(s)`
          : `${entities.length} labels · ${relationships.length} relationship types · ${sourceTotal} sources`,
      }));
      return { inv, sourceTotal, totalNodes, totalEdges, csvN, unstructN };
    }

    function refreshConstructHeader() {
      const stats = rebuildConstructStepMeta();
      const title = document.getElementById('constructPageTitle');
      const sub = document.getElementById('constructPageSub');
      const config = window.graphenDomain || {};
      const pillar = (config.pillar_blueprint || {}).graph_construction || {};
      if (title) {
        title.textContent = pillar.title || (stats.inv.usingDemo
          ? 'Building the Unified Knowledge Graph (Demo Scale)'
          : `Building the Unified Knowledge Graph from All ${stats.sourceTotal} Source${stats.sourceTotal === 1 ? '' : 's'}`);
      }
      if (sub) {
        sub.textContent = pillar.subtitle || (stats.inv.usingDemo
          ? 'No session files detected — using standard methodology on a demo source mix. Upload files or open a Tracking ID for live counts. Run each stage; plain-language results appear on the right.'
          : `Entities from ${stats.csvN} tabular file(s) and ${stats.unstructN} unstructured file(s) merge into one Neo4j graph. Run each stage in order.`);
      }
    }

    function buildConstructStepCards() {
      const host = document.getElementById('constructSteps');
      if (!host) return;
      const sig = JSON.stringify(getConstructInventory());
      const needRebuild = !CONSTRUCT_STEP_META.length || constructInventorySig !== sig || !host.children.length;
      if (needRebuild) {
        rebuildConstructStepMeta();
        constructInventorySig = sig;
        // If inventory changed materially, reset completion so counts stay honest
        if (host.dataset.sig && host.dataset.sig !== sig) {
          constructCompleted = new Set();
          constructActiveStep = 0;
          const nextBtn = document.getElementById('btnNextAfterConstruct');
          if (nextBtn) nextBtn.disabled = true;
        }
        host.dataset.sig = sig;
        host.innerHTML = CONSTRUCT_STEP_META.map((meta, idx) => `
          <div class="struct-step${idx === 0 ? ' active' : ''}" data-step="${idx}" onclick="focusConstructResult(${idx})" style="--construct-accent:${meta.color}">
            <div class="sn">${idx + 1}</div>
            <div style="flex:1;min-width:0">
              <div class="st">${meta.title}</div>
              <div class="sd" id="constructBlurb${idx}">${meta.blurb}</div>
              <div class="scode">${meta.code}</div>
            </div>
            <button class="struct-step-run" id="constructRun${idx}" onclick="event.stopPropagation(); runConstructStep(${idx})">▶ Run</button>
          </div>
        `).join('');
      } else {
        // refresh blurbs if meta rebuilt elsewhere
        CONSTRUCT_STEP_META.forEach((meta, idx) => {
          const el = document.getElementById('constructBlurb' + idx);
          if (el) el.textContent = meta.blurb;
        });
      }
    }

    function formatConstructMetricPairs(m) {
      return [
        ['Nodes added', m.nodes_added],
        ['Edges added', m.edges_added],
        ['People', m.people],
        ['Companies', m.companies],
        ['Accounts', m.accounts],
        ['Shell flags', m.shell_flags],
        ['Transfers', m.transfers],
        ['Devices', m.devices],
        ['Addresses', m.addresses],
        ['Sanctioned', m.sanctioned],
        ['Relationship types', m.rel_types],
        ['Regulations', m.regulations],
        ['Policies', m.policies],
        ['KYC / AML nodes', m.kyc_aml],
        ['Cross-source links', m.cross_links],
        ['Early alerts', m.alerts],
        ['Total nodes', m.nodes_total],
        ['Total edges', m.edges_total],
        ['Sources in session', m.sources],
      ].filter(([, v]) => v !== '—' && v != null && v !== '');
    }

    function paintConstructSteps() {
      document.querySelectorAll('#constructSteps .struct-step').forEach((card) => {
        const idx = Number(card.dataset.step);
        card.classList.toggle('active', idx === constructActiveStep);
        card.classList.toggle('done', constructCompleted.has(idx));
        card.classList.toggle('running', constructRunning && idx === constructActiveStep);
        const sn = card.querySelector('.sn');
        if (sn) sn.textContent = constructCompleted.has(idx) ? '✓' : String(idx + 1);
        const btn = document.getElementById('constructRun' + idx);
        if (!btn) return;
        const priorOk = idx === 0 || constructCompleted.has(idx - 1);
        if (constructCompleted.has(idx)) {
          btn.textContent = '✓ Done';
          btn.classList.add('done-btn');
          btn.disabled = false;
          btn.title = 'Re-run this step';
        } else if (constructRunning && idx === constructActiveStep) {
          btn.textContent = 'Running…';
          btn.classList.remove('done-btn');
          btn.disabled = true;
        } else {
          btn.textContent = '▶ Run';
          btn.classList.remove('done-btn');
          btn.disabled = !priorOk || constructRunning;
          btn.title = priorOk ? 'Run this step' : 'Complete the previous step first';
        }
      });
      // Keep Next enabled whenever all construction stages are done
      const nextBtn = document.getElementById('btnNextAfterConstruct');
      if (nextBtn && CONSTRUCT_STEP_META.length && constructCompleted.size >= CONSTRUCT_STEP_META.length) {
        nextBtn.disabled = false;
        nextBtn.removeAttribute('disabled');
      }
    }

    function goToInteractiveGraph() {
      window.igTabsMeta = null;
      window.igGraphCache = { nodes: [], links: [] };
      try {
        igTabsMeta = null;
        igGraphCache = { nodes: [], links: [] };
        igActiveFilter = 'all';
      } catch (_) {}
      nav('graph');
    }

    function goToCypherDetection() {
      try {
        cyphStopPlay();
        cyphPayload = null;
        cyphActiveDet = null;
        cyphStepIdx = 0;
      } catch (_) {}
      nav('cypher');
    }

    function goToCrossDocDiscovery() {
      nav('crossdoc');
    }

    window.goToCrossDocDiscovery = goToCrossDocDiscovery;
    window.exportPipelineStepResult = exportPipelineStepResult;
    window.runEntireStructPipeline = runEntireStructPipeline;
    window.runEntireUnstructPipeline = runEntireUnstructPipeline;
    window.runEntireConstructPipeline = runEntireConstructPipeline;

    function renderConstructResultsFeed(focusIdx) {
      const feed = document.getElementById('constructResultsFeed');
      if (!feed) return;
      const ordered = [...constructCompleted].sort((a, b) => a - b);
      if (!ordered.length) {
        feed.innerHTML = `<div class="struct-results-empty" id="constructResultsEmpty">No results yet.<br/>Click <b>Run</b> on Step 1 to begin building the graph from your uploaded files.</div>`;
        return;
      }
      feed.innerHTML = ordered.map((idx) => {
        const meta = CONSTRUCT_STEP_META[idx];
        const pairs = formatConstructMetricPairs(meta.metrics);
        const metricsHtml = pairs.length
          ? `<div class="struct-result-metrics">${pairs.map(([k, v]) =>
              `<div class="rm"><span class="k">${k}</span><span class="v">${v}</span></div>`
            ).join('')}</div>`
          : '';
        const active = focusIdx === idx || constructActiveStep === idx ? ' active-result' : '';
        const simple = meta.simple ? `<div class="struct-result-simple" style="margin:0 0 10px;padding:10px 12px;border-radius:8px;background:rgba(255,140,0,0.08);border:1px solid rgba(255,140,0,0.22);color:var(--tx-0);font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.45;font-weight:600;">${meta.simple.replace(/</g, '&lt;')}</div>` : '';
        return `<div class="struct-result-card${active}" id="constructResultCard${idx}" onclick="focusConstructResult(${idx})">
          <div class="struct-result-head">
            <div class="struct-result-title">Step ${idx + 1} · ${meta.title}</div>
            <div class="struct-result-actions">
              <button type="button" class="step-export-btn" title="Export complete step details as JSON"
                onclick="event.stopPropagation(); exportPipelineStepResult('construction', ${idx}, 'json')">⇩ JSON</button>
              <button type="button" class="step-export-btn" title="Export step results and metrics as CSV"
                onclick="event.stopPropagation(); exportPipelineStepResult('construction', ${idx}, 'csv')">⇩ CSV</button>
              <span class="struct-result-badge">COMPLETE</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          ${simple}
          <div class="struct-result-body">${meta.detail.replace(/</g, '&lt;')}</div>
          ${metricsHtml}
          <div class="scode" style="margin-top:10px;">Under the hood · ${meta.code.replace(/</g, '&lt;')}</div>
        </div>`;
      }).join('');

      if (constructCompleted.size >= CONSTRUCT_STEP_META.length && CONSTRUCT_STEP_META.length) {
        const last = CONSTRUCT_STEP_META[CONSTRUCT_STEP_META.length - 1];
        const tn = last.metrics.nodes_total;
        const te = last.metrics.edges_total;
        const src = last.metrics.sources;
        feed.innerHTML += `<div class="struct-result-card" style="border-color:rgba(61,220,151,0.35);">
          <div class="struct-result-head">
            <div class="struct-result-title">Unified graph complete</div>
            <span class="struct-result-badge">READY</span>
          </div>
          <div class="struct-result-simple" style="margin:0;padding:10px 12px;border-radius:8px;background:var(--ok-dim);border:1px solid rgba(61,220,151,0.3);color:var(--tx-0);font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.45;font-weight:600;">
            ✓ Unified graph complete — ${tn} nodes · ${te} edges · ${src} source(s) merged. Continue to Interactive Graph.
          </div>
        </div>`;
      }

      const focus = focusIdx != null ? focusIdx : constructActiveStep;
      const card = document.getElementById('constructResultCard' + focus);
      if (card) card.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'nearest' });
    }

    function focusConstructResult(idx) {
      constructActiveStep = idx;
      paintConstructSteps();
      renderConstructResultsFeed(idx);
      const hint = document.getElementById('constructStatusHint');
      const n = CONSTRUCT_STEP_META.length || 10;
      if (hint && CONSTRUCT_STEP_META[idx]) hint.textContent = `Viewing results · Step ${idx + 1}/${n} · ${CONSTRUCT_STEP_META[idx].title}`;
    }

    async function runConstructStep(idx) {
      if (constructRunning) return;
      if (!CONSTRUCT_STEP_META.length) rebuildConstructStepMeta();
      if (idx > 0 && !constructCompleted.has(idx - 1)) {
        if (!constructEntireRunning) {
          alert(`Please run Step ${idx} · ${CONSTRUCT_STEP_META[idx - 1].title} first.`);
        }
        return;
      }
      const meta = CONSTRUCT_STEP_META[idx];
      constructRunning = true;
      constructActiveStep = idx;
      paintConstructSteps();
      const hint = document.getElementById('constructStatusHint');
      if (hint) hint.textContent = `Running Step ${idx + 1} · ${meta.title}…`;

      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 700));

      constructCompleted.add(idx);
      constructRunning = false;
      paintConstructSteps();
      renderConstructResultsFeed(idx);
      if (hint) hint.textContent = `Step ${idx + 1} · ${meta.title} complete — results published on the right`;
      if (constructCompleted.size >= CONSTRUCT_STEP_META.length) {
        const nextBtn = document.getElementById('btnNextAfterConstruct');
        if (nextBtn) {
          nextBtn.disabled = false;
          nextBtn.removeAttribute('disabled');
        }
        if (hint) hint.textContent = 'Unified graph complete — proceed to Interactive Graph';
        // Hand off session snapshot so Interactive Graph uses the same sources
        try {
          const inv = getConstructInventory();
          const last = CONSTRUCT_STEP_META[CONSTRUCT_STEP_META.length - 1] || {};
          window.graphenConstructSnapshot = {
            inventory: inv,
            metrics: last.metrics || {},
            completedAt: Date.now(),
          };
          updateSidebarLiveStats();
          const activeDomain = window.graphenDomain || {};
          window.graphenUseCaseHint = [
            activeDomain.industry,
            activeDomain.use_case,
            activeDomain.objective,
            'post-merger construction with ' + (inv.csvNames || []).length +
              ' tabular and ' + ((inv.docNames || []).length +
              (inv.imgNames || []).length + (inv.audioNames || []).length) +
              ' unstructured sources',
          ].filter(Boolean).join(' | ');
          // Invalidate interactive graph cache so next page rebuilds from this session
          window.igTabsMeta = null;
          window.igGraphCache = { nodes: [], links: [] };
          try { igTabsMeta = null; igGraphCache = { nodes: [], links: [] }; } catch (_) {}
        } catch (e) { console.warn('construct handoff failed', e); }
      }
    }

    async function runEntireConstructPipeline() {
      if (constructRunning || constructEntireRunning) return;
      if (!CONSTRUCT_STEP_META.length) {
        buildConstructStepCards();
        rebuildConstructStepMeta();
      }
      const btn = document.getElementById('btnRunEntireConstruct');
      constructEntireRunning = true;
      if (btn) { btn.disabled = true; btn.textContent = 'Running all stages…'; }
      constructCompleted.clear();
      constructActiveStep = 0;
      const nextBtn = document.getElementById('btnNextAfterConstruct');
      if (nextBtn) nextBtn.disabled = true;
      paintConstructSteps();
      renderConstructResultsFeed();
      const hint = document.getElementById('constructStatusHint');
      if (hint) hint.textContent = 'Running entire graph construction — results will stack one by one…';
      const total = CONSTRUCT_STEP_META.length;
      for (let i = 0; i < total; i++) {
        await runConstructStep(i);
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 400));
      }
      constructEntireRunning = false;
      if (btn) { btn.disabled = false; btn.textContent = '▶ Run Entire Pipeline'; }
      if (hint) hint.textContent = 'Unified graph complete — proceed to Interactive Graph';
    }


    /* ============================================================
       HERO MINI GRAPH DECORATION (decorative, animated)
       ============================================================ */
    (function heroGraph() {
      try {
      const svg = d3.select('#hero-svg-graph');
      if (svg.empty()) return;
      const nodes = d3.range(14).map(i => ({ id: i, r: i % 4 === 0 ? 7 : 4.5, c: ['#4C8DFF', '#27D199', '#9B7CF6', '#FB5A6A'][i % 4] }));
      const links = nodes.slice(1).map((n, i) => ({ source: 0, target: n.id })).concat(
        nodes.slice(2).map((n, i) => ({ source: 1 + (i % 3), target: n.id }))
      );
      const sim = d3.forceSimulation(nodes)
        .force('link', d3.forceLink(links).id(d => d.id).distance(46))
        .force('charge', d3.forceManyBody().strength(-60))
        .force('center', d3.forceCenter(200, 160))
        .force('collide', d3.forceCollide(14));
      const link = svg.append('g').selectAll('line').data(links).join('line')
        .attr('stroke', '#2A3658').attr('stroke-width', 1);
      const node = svg.append('g').selectAll('circle').data(nodes).join('circle')
        .attr('r', d => d.r).attr('fill', d => d.c).attr('opacity', 0.85);
      sim.on('tick', () => {
        link.attr('x1', d => d.source.x).attr('y1', d => d.source.y).attr('x2', d => d.target.x).attr('y2', d => d.target.y);
        node.attr('cx', d => d.x).attr('cy', d => d.y);
      });
      } catch (e) { console.warn('heroGraph skipped', e); }
    })();

    /* ============================================================
       INGEST DEMO
       ============================================================ */
    const SAMPLE_PDF_NAME = 'document_dallas_commerce_blvd.pdf';
    function runIngestDemo() {
      document.getElementById('fileList').innerHTML =
        `<div class="file-chip">📄 <span class="fname">${SAMPLE_PDF_NAME}</span> <span style="color:var(--tx-3)">214 KB</span></div>`;
      const steps = document.querySelectorAll('.pipe-step');
      steps.forEach(s => { s.classList.remove('active', 'done'); s.querySelector('.pipe-num').innerHTML = s.dataset.step * 1 + 1; });
      document.getElementById('jsonOut').textContent = '// Processing...';
      let i = 0;
      function step() {
        if (i > 0) {
          steps[i - 1].classList.remove('active'); steps[i - 1].classList.add('done');
          steps[i - 1].querySelector('.pipe-num').innerHTML = '✓';
        }
        if (i < steps.length) {
          steps[i].classList.add('active');
          steps[i].querySelector('.pipe-num').innerHTML = '<div class="spinner"></div>';
          if (i === 2) bumpLLM();
          i++;
          setTimeout(step, 650);
        } else {
          showExtractedJSON();
        }
      }
      step();
    }
    function renderJSON(data) {
      const html = JSON.stringify(data, null, 2)
        .replace(/"(\w+)":/g, '<span class="k">"$1"</span>:')
        .replace(/: "([^"]*)"/g, ': <span class="s">"$1"</span>')
        .replace(/: (\d+\.?\d*)/g, ': <span class="n">$1</span>');
      document.getElementById('jsonOut').innerHTML = html;
    }
    function showExtractedJSON() {
      renderJSON({
        tenant_name: "Vantage Analytics",
        property_address: "456 Commerce Blvd, Dallas, TX 75201",
        document_start_date: "2022-03-01",
        document_end_date: fmt(addDays(today, 42)),
        base_rent_psf: 36.5,
        rentable_sqft: 18000,
        annual_rent: 657000,
        document_type: "NNN",
        escalation_pct: 3.0,
        renewal_options: [{ term_years: 5, notice_months: 12 }],
        termination_rights: [{ effective_after_year: 3, notice_months: 12 }],
        risk_clauses: ["Tenant may terminate effective end of Year 3 with 12 months notice"],
        _extraction_method: "llm",
        _graph_node_id: "LG-A192"
      });
    }

    /* ---- Real upload: browse / drag-drop → POST /api/uploads ---- */
    let uploadedCsvFiles = [];      // CSV / Excel (tabular)
    let uploadedPdfFiles = [];      // PDF / Word / Text (documents)
    let uploadedImageFiles = [];    // Images
    let uploadedAudioFiles = [];    // Audio
    let pendingUploadFiles = [];
    window.currentTrackingId = null;
    window.currentUploadScenarioTrackingId = null;

    function uploadScenarioContext() {
      const activeId = window.currentJourneyTrackingId;
      if (activeId) {
        const active = domainSavedScenarios.find(item =>
          (item.tracking_id || item.id) === activeId
        );
        if (active) return active;
      }
      const activeConfig = window.graphenDomain || domainConfiguration || {};
      const activeIndustry = domainSelectedIndustry || activeConfig.industry || '';
      if (!activeIndustry) return null;
      return domainSavedScenarios.find(item =>
        String(item.industry || '').toLowerCase() ===
          String(activeIndustry).toLowerCase()
      ) || null;
    }

    const TABULAR_EXT = ['.csv', '.xlsx', '.xls'];
    const DOC_EXT = ['.pdf', '.doc', '.docx', '.txt', '.rtf', '.md'];
    const IMAGE_EXT = ['.png', '.jpg', '.jpeg', '.gif', '.webp', '.tif', '.tiff', '.bmp'];
    const AUDIO_EXT = ['.mp3', '.wav', '.m4a', '.flac', '.ogg', '.aac', '.wma'];

    function fileExt(name) {
      const n = String(name || '').toLowerCase();
      const i = n.lastIndexOf('.');
      return i >= 0 ? n.slice(i) : '';
    }

    function classifyIngestExt(ext) {
      if (TABULAR_EXT.includes(ext)) return 'tabular';
      if (DOC_EXT.includes(ext)) return 'document';
      if (IMAGE_EXT.includes(ext)) return 'image';
      if (AUDIO_EXT.includes(ext)) return 'audio';
      return null;
    }

    function fileKey(f) {
      return String(f && (f.name || f.filename) || '').toLowerCase();
    }

    function knownFileNames() {
      return new Set([
        ...uploadedCsvFiles.map(fileKey),
        ...uploadedPdfFiles.map(fileKey),
        ...uploadedImageFiles.map(fileKey),
        ...uploadedAudioFiles.map(fileKey),
        ...pendingUploadFiles.map(fileKey),
      ].filter(Boolean));
    }

    function totalIngestFiles() {
      return uploadedCsvFiles.length + uploadedPdfFiles.length + uploadedImageFiles.length + uploadedAudioFiles.length;
    }

    function handleMultiDragOver(e) {
      e.preventDefault();
      document.getElementById('multiDropzone').classList.add('dragover');
    }
    function handleMultiDragLeave(e) {
      e.preventDefault();
      document.getElementById('multiDropzone').classList.remove('dragover');
    }
    function handleMultiDrop(e) {
      e.preventDefault();
      document.getElementById('multiDropzone').classList.remove('dragover');
      if (e.dataTransfer.files && e.dataTransfer.files.length > 0) {
        handleMultiUpload(e.dataTransfer.files);
      }
    }
    function handleMultiUpload(fileList) {
      const files = Array.from(fileList || []);
      const known = knownFileNames();
      let added = 0;
      let skipped = 0;
      let rejected = 0;
      files.forEach(f => {
        const key = fileKey(f);
        const ext = fileExt(f.name);
        const kind = classifyIngestExt(ext);
        if (!kind) {
          rejected++;
          return;
        }
        if (known.has(key)) {
          skipped++;
          return;
        }
        known.add(key);
        pendingUploadFiles.push(f);
        if (kind === 'tabular') uploadedCsvFiles.push(f);
        else if (kind === 'document') uploadedPdfFiles.push(f);
        else if (kind === 'image') uploadedImageFiles.push(f);
        else if (kind === 'audio') uploadedAudioFiles.push(f);
        added++;
      });
      renderIngestGrids();
      if (rejected && !added) {
        alert(`Unsupported file type.\nAccepted: Audio, Text, PDF, Word, Image, Excel, CSV.`);
      } else if (skipped && !added) {
        alert(`All ${skipped} selected file(s) are already in this session — nothing new to add.`);
      } else if (skipped || rejected) {
        console.info(`Added ${added}; skipped ${skipped} duplicate(s); rejected ${rejected} unsupported.`);
      }
    }
    function loadSampleFiles() {
      for(let i=1; i<=8; i++) uploadedCsvFiles.push({ name: `DS${i}_Dataset.csv` });
      for(let i=1; i<=7; i++) uploadedPdfFiles.push({ name: `US${i}_Document.pdf` });
      renderIngestGrids();
    }

    function renderKindGrid(gridId, files, kind, icon, prefix) {
      const grid = document.getElementById(gridId);
      if (!grid) return;
      grid.innerHTML = files.map((f, i) => {
        const name = f.name || f.filename || 'file';
        const idAttr = f.id != null ? String(f.id) : '';
        const short = name.length > 18 ? name.substring(0, 18) + '...' : name;
        return `<div class="dataset-card" onclick='previewIngestFile(${JSON.stringify(name)}, ${JSON.stringify(idAttr)}, ${JSON.stringify(kind)})'>
          <div class="card-icon">${icon}</div>
          <div>
            <div class="card-id">${prefix}${i + 1}</div>
            <div class="card-label" title="${name.replace(/"/g, '&quot;')}">${short}</div>
          </div>
        </div>`;
      }).join('');
    }

    function renderIngestGrids() {
      renderKindGrid('csvGrid', uploadedCsvFiles, 'csv', '📊', 'DS');
      renderKindGrid('pdfGrid', uploadedPdfFiles, 'pdf', '📄', 'US');
      renderKindGrid('imgGrid', uploadedImageFiles, 'image', '🖼️', 'IM');
      renderKindGrid('audioGrid', uploadedAudioFiles, 'audio', '🎧', 'AU');

      const setTxt = (id, v) => { const el = document.getElementById(id); if (el) el.innerText = v; };
      setTxt('csvCount', uploadedCsvFiles.length);
      setTxt('docCount', uploadedPdfFiles.length);
      setTxt('imgCount', uploadedImageFiles.length);
      setTxt('audioCount', uploadedAudioFiles.length);
      setTxt('pdfCount', uploadedPdfFiles.length);

      const dz = document.getElementById('dzSub');
      if (dz) {
        dz.innerText = totalIngestFiles()
          ? `${uploadedCsvFiles.length} tabular · ${uploadedPdfFiles.length} docs · ${uploadedImageFiles.length} images · ${uploadedAudioFiles.length} audio`
          : 'Audio · Text · PDF · Word · Image · Excel · CSV';
      }

      const stepUpload = document.getElementById('stepUploadSub');
      const stepStruct = document.getElementById('stepStructSub');
      const stepUnstruct = document.getElementById('stepUnstructSub');
      if (stepUpload) stepUpload.innerText = `${totalIngestFiles()} files · multi-modal`;
      if (stepStruct) stepStruct.innerText = `${uploadedCsvFiles.length} tabular · 6 steps`;
      if (stepUnstruct) stepUnstruct.innerText = `${uploadedPdfFiles.length + uploadedImageFiles.length + uploadedAudioFiles.length} unstructured · 7 steps`;

      const pillCsv = document.getElementById('pillCsv');
      const pillPdf = document.getElementById('pillPdf');
      if (pillCsv) pillCsv.textContent = `CSV/XLS ${uploadedCsvFiles.length}`;
      if (pillPdf) pillPdf.textContent = `Docs ${uploadedPdfFiles.length}`;
      const pillNodes = document.getElementById('pillNodes');
      if (pillNodes && totalIngestFiles()) {
        pillNodes.textContent = `Files ${totalIngestFiles()}`;
      }

      const nextBtn = document.getElementById('btnNextPipeline');
      if (nextBtn) nextBtn.disabled = totalIngestFiles() === 0;
      updateSidebarLiveStats();
      updateActiveTrackingLabel();
    }

    function updateActiveTrackingLabel() {
      const el = document.getElementById('activeTrackingLabel');
      if (!el) return;
      const scenario = uploadScenarioContext();
      const scenarioId = scenario && (scenario.tracking_id || scenario.id);
      const scenarioDisplayId = scenarioId && compactTrackingId(
        scenarioId, scenario.industry, scenario.use_case, scenario.saved_at
      );
      el.textContent = window.currentTrackingId
        ? `Scenario: ${compactTrackingId(
          window.currentUploadScenarioTrackingId || scenarioId,
          scenario && scenario.industry,
          scenario && scenario.use_case,
          scenario && scenario.saved_at
        )} · Upload ID: ${window.currentTrackingId}`
        : (scenarioDisplayId
          ? `Ready for scenario: ${scenarioDisplayId} · Upload creates a new Tracking ID`
          : 'No saved scenario — save a Domain Configurator scenario first');
    }

    function startNewUploadSession() {
      window.currentTrackingId = null;
      window.currentUploadScenarioTrackingId = null;
      pendingUploadFiles = [];
      uploadedCsvFiles = [];
      uploadedPdfFiles = [];
      uploadedImageFiles = [];
      uploadedAudioFiles = [];
      const input = document.getElementById('multiFileInput');
      if (input) input.value = '';
      closeIngestPreview();
      renderIngestGrids();
      document.querySelectorAll('.tracking-chip').forEach(c => c.classList.remove('active'));
      updateActiveTrackingLabel();
    }

    function closeIngestPreview() {
      const pane = document.getElementById('file-preview-pane');
      if (pane) pane.classList.remove('visible');
    }

    function showIngestPreview(title, htmlOrText, asHtml) {
      const pane = document.getElementById('file-preview-pane');
      const titleEl = document.getElementById('preview-filename');
      const content = document.getElementById('preview-content');
      if (!pane || !content) return;
      if (titleEl) titleEl.textContent = title || 'File Preview';
      if (asHtml) {
        content.style.whiteSpace = 'normal';
        content.innerHTML = htmlOrText;
      } else {
        content.style.whiteSpace = 'pre-wrap';
        content.textContent = htmlOrText;
      }
      pane.classList.add('visible');
      pane.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'nearest' });
    }

    async function previewIngestFile(filename, fileId, kind) {
      closeSnapshot();
      const id = fileId ? Number(fileId) : null;
      const local = uploadedCsvFiles.find(f => fileKey(f) === String(filename).toLowerCase())
        || uploadedPdfFiles.find(f => fileKey(f) === String(filename).toLowerCase())
        || uploadedImageFiles.find(f => fileKey(f) === String(filename).toLowerCase())
        || uploadedAudioFiles.find(f => fileKey(f) === String(filename).toLowerCase());

      showIngestPreview(filename, 'Loading preview…', false);

      // Prefer server file when we have an id (loaded from tracking session)
      if (id) {
        try {
          const res = await fetch(`/api/files/${id}`);
          if (!res.ok) throw new Error('Failed to load file');
          if (String(filename).toLowerCase().endsWith('.csv') || kind === 'csv') {
            const text = await res.text();
            showIngestPreview(filename, csvPreviewHtml(text), true);
          } else if (String(filename).toLowerCase().endsWith('.pdf') || kind === 'pdf') {
            const blob = await res.blob();
            const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
            showIngestPreview(filename, `<iframe src="${url}" width="100%" height="480" style="border:none;border-radius:8px;background:#fff;"></iframe>`, true);
          } else {
            const text = await res.text();
            showIngestPreview(filename, text.substring(0, 12000), false);
          }
          return;
        } catch (e) {
          showIngestPreview(filename, `Could not load server file: ${e.message}`, false);
          return;
        }
      }

      if (local && local instanceof File) {
        if (filename.toLowerCase().endsWith('.csv')) {
          const reader = new FileReader();
          reader.onload = (e) => showIngestPreview(filename, csvPreviewHtml(e.target.result), true);
          reader.readAsText(local);
        } else if (filename.toLowerCase().endsWith('.pdf')) {
          const url = URL.createObjectURL(local);
          showIngestPreview(filename, `<iframe src="${url}" width="100%" height="480" style="border:none;border-radius:8px;background:#fff;"></iframe>`, true);
        } else {
          showIngestPreview(filename, 'Preview not supported for this file type.', false);
        }
        return;
      }

      showIngestPreview(filename, 'No local or server content available for this file.', false);
    }

    function csvPreviewHtml(text) {
      const esc = (s) => String(s ?? '')
        .replace(/&/g, '&amp;')
        .replace(/</g, '&lt;')
        .replace(/>/g, '&gt;')
        .replace(/"/g, '&quot;');
      const lines = String(text || '').split('\n').filter(line => line.trim() !== '');
      const rows = lines.slice(0, 40);
      let html = '<div style="overflow-x:auto;"><table><thead>';
      rows.forEach((row, i) => {
        const cols = row.split(',');
        if (i === 0) {
          html += '<tr>';
          cols.forEach(c => { html += `<th>${esc(c.trim())}</th>`; });
          html += '</tr></thead><tbody>';
        } else {
          html += '<tr>';
          cols.forEach(c => { html += `<td>${esc(c.trim())}</td>`; });
          html += '</tr>';
        }
      });
      html += '</tbody></table></div>';
      if (lines.length > 40) {
        html += `<div style="text-align:center;color:var(--tx-2);font-size:12px;margin-top:12px;">Showing 40 of ${lines.length} rows</div>`;
      }
      return html;
    }
    
    function openSnapshot(filename, icon) {
      // Compatibility: route old callers to inline bottom preview
      previewIngestFile(filename, '', icon === '📊' ? 'csv' : 'pdf');
    }
    
    function closeSnapshot() {
      const modal = document.getElementById('snapshotModal');
      if (modal) modal.classList.remove('active');
    }

    let pipelineData = null;
    let pipelineStepIdx = 0;
    let sessionId = null;
    
    async function runStepApi(stepPath, data) {
      const res = await fetch(stepPath, {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify(data)
      });
      if (!res.ok) {
        let detail = res.statusText;
        try { detail = (await res.json()).detail || detail; } catch (_) { }
        throw new Error(detail);
      }
      return await res.json();
    }
    
    async function advancePipelineStep() {
      const steps = document.querySelectorAll('.pipe-step');
      if (pipelineStepIdx > 0) {
        steps[pipelineStepIdx - 1].classList.remove('active');
        steps[pipelineStepIdx - 1].classList.add('done');
        steps[pipelineStepIdx - 1].querySelector('.pipe-num').innerHTML = '✓';
      }
      
      if (pipelineStepIdx < steps.length) {
        steps[pipelineStepIdx].classList.add('active');
        steps[pipelineStepIdx].querySelector('.pipe-num').innerHTML = '<div class="spinner"></div>';
        
        const nextBtn = document.getElementById('nextStepBtn');
        nextBtn.disabled = true;
        nextBtn.textContent = "Processing...";
        
        try {
          if (pipelineStepIdx === 1) {
            // Pattern + NER Extraction
            const res = await runStepApi('/api/ingest/step2_ner', { session_id: sessionId });
            if (pipelineData.source_type === 'tabular') {
              renderJSON({
                info: res.info || "Spreadsheet columns already structured",
                rows: res.rows || pipelineData.rows_parsed
              });
            } else {
              renderJSON({
                info: "Applied spaCy & Regex models",
                entities_found: "Identified dates and monetary values."
              });
            }
          } else if (pipelineStepIdx === 2) {
            // LLM Structured Extraction (or tabular column map)
            if (pipelineData.source_type !== 'tabular' && typeof bumpLLM === 'function') bumpLLM();
            const res = await runStepApi('/api/ingest/step3_llm', { session_id: sessionId });
            pipelineData.extracted = res.extracted;
            if (res.all_documents) pipelineData.all_documents = res.all_documents;
            renderJSON({
              info: res.info || "LLM Extraction using strict schema",
              rows_parsed: res.rows_parsed,
              output: pipelineData.extracted || {},
              ...(res.all_documents && res.all_documents.length > 1
                ? { note: `${res.all_documents.length} documents will be written to the graph` }
                : {})
            });
          } else if (pipelineStepIdx === 3) {
            // Entity Resolution
            const res = await runStepApi('/api/ingest/step4_resolve', { session_id: sessionId });
            renderJSON({
              info: "Fuzzy matching to graph...",
              resolved_property: pipelineData.extracted?.property_address || "No match",
              resolved_tenant: pipelineData.extracted?.tenant_name || "No match"
            });
          } else if (pipelineStepIdx === 4) {
            // Graph Write
            const res = await runStepApi('/api/ingest/step5_graph', { session_id: sessionId });
            pipelineData.document_id = res.document_id;
            if (res.document_ids) pipelineData.document_ids = res.document_ids;
            renderJSON({
              info: "Neo4j MERGE operations",
              nodes_created: ["Document", "Tenant", "Property", "Clause"],
              document_node_id: pipelineData.document_id || "LG-NEW",
              ...(res.rows_written ? { rows_written: res.rows_written, document_ids: res.document_ids } : {})
            });
            if (typeof refreshRelationshipTable === 'function') {
              refreshRelationshipTable();
            }
          } else if (pipelineStepIdx === 5) {
            // Vector Embedding
            const res = await runStepApi('/api/ingest/step6_vector', { session_id: sessionId });
            pipelineData = res;
            renderJSON({
              info: "Generating sentence embeddings for chunks...",
              model: "sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",
              vectors_stored: pipelineData.chunks ? pipelineData.chunks : 0
            });
          }
          
          pipelineStepIdx++;
          nextBtn.disabled = false;
          nextBtn.textContent = "Next Step";
        } catch(err) {
          steps[pipelineStepIdx].classList.remove('active');
          steps[pipelineStepIdx].classList.add('failed');
          steps[pipelineStepIdx].querySelector('.pipe-num').innerHTML = '✕';
          renderJSON({ error: String(err.message || err) });
          nextBtn.disabled = false;
          nextBtn.textContent = "Retry Step";
        }
      } else {
        // Final Output
        document.getElementById('nextStepBtn').style.display = 'none';
        renderJSON({
          document_id: pipelineData.document_id,
          filename: pipelineData.filename,
          pages: pipelineData.pages,
          chunks: pipelineData.chunks,
          ...(pipelineData.extracted || {})
        });
      }
    }

    async function handleUpload(file) {
      if (!file) return;
      if (!/\.(pdf|doc|docx|csv|xlsx|xls)$/i.test(file.name)) {
        renderJSON({ error: "Supported formats: PDF, Word, CSV, or Excel (.xlsx/.xls)." });
        return;
      }
      showFileChip(file.name, file.size);

      // Reset visually.
      const steps = document.querySelectorAll('.pipe-step');
      steps.forEach(s => { s.classList.remove('active', 'done', 'failed'); s.querySelector('.pipe-num').innerHTML = s.dataset.step * 1 + 1; });
      document.getElementById('jsonOut').textContent = '// Uploading & extracting from ' + file.name + ' ...';
      document.getElementById('nextStepBtn').style.display = 'none';
      
      steps[0].classList.add('active');
      steps[0].querySelector('.pipe-num').innerHTML = '<div class="spinner"></div>';

      try {
        const form = new FormData();
        form.append('file', file);
        const res = await fetch('/api/ingest/step1_extract', { method: 'POST', body: form });
        
        if (!res.ok) {
          let detail = res.statusText;
          try { detail = (await res.json()).detail || detail; } catch (_) { }
          throw new Error(detail);
        }
        
        pipelineData = await res.json();
        sessionId = pipelineData.session_id;
        
        if (pipelineData.source_type === 'tabular') {
          renderJSON({
            info: "Mapped spreadsheet rows into document records (LLM not required).",
            rows_parsed: pipelineData.rows_parsed,
            chunks_count: pipelineData.chunks_count,
            preview: pipelineData.preview
          });
        } else {
          renderJSON({
            info: "Extracted raw text from document.",
            chunks_count: pipelineData.chunks_count,
            sample_text: pipelineData.sample_text
          });
        }
        
        // Setup state for next click
        pipelineStepIdx = 1;
        document.getElementById('nextStepBtn').style.display = 'inline-block';
        document.getElementById('nextStepBtn').disabled = false;
        document.getElementById('nextStepBtn').textContent = 'Next Step';
        
      } catch (err) {
        steps[0].classList.remove('active');
        steps[0].classList.add('failed'); 
        steps[0].querySelector('.pipe-num').innerHTML = '✕';
        renderJSON({
          error: String(err.message || err),
          hint: "Make sure the API (uvicorn api.main:app --port 8000) is running."
        });
      }
    }

    /* Legacy single-file dropzone (#dropzone / #fileInput) was removed in favor of
       #multiDropzone / #multiFileInput. Guard so a missing node never aborts this script
       (that previously prevented paintInteractiveGraph from being defined). */
    (function bindLegacyDropzoneIfPresent() {
      const _dz = document.getElementById('dropzone');
      const _fi = document.getElementById('fileInput');
      if (!_dz || !_fi) return;
      _dz.addEventListener('click', () => _fi.click());
      const btn = _dz.querySelector('button');
      if (btn) btn.addEventListener('click', (e) => { e.stopPropagation(); _fi.click(); });
      _fi.addEventListener('change', (e) => { if (e.target.files && e.target.files[0]) handleUpload(e.target.files[0]); _fi.value = ''; });
      ['dragenter', 'dragover'].forEach(ev => _dz.addEventListener(ev, (e) => { e.preventDefault(); e.stopPropagation(); _dz.classList.add('drag'); }));
      ['dragleave', 'drop'].forEach(ev => _dz.addEventListener(ev, (e) => { e.preventDefault(); e.stopPropagation(); _dz.classList.remove('drag'); }));
      _dz.addEventListener('drop', (e) => { const f = e.dataTransfer && e.dataTransfer.files && e.dataTransfer.files[0]; if (f) handleUpload(f); });
    })();

    /* ============================================================
       NEXT AI — uploaded-session hybrid RAG + Graph-RAG
       ============================================================ */
    let nextAiConversation = [];
    let nextAiLastUnavailableQuestion = '';
    let nextAiContextSignature = '';

    function nextAiEsc(value) {
      return String(value == null ? '' : value)
        .replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;')
        .replace(/"/g, '&quot;').replace(/'/g, '&#39;');
    }

    function nextAiFileNames(files) {
      return (files || []).map(file =>
        typeof file === 'string' ? file : (file.name || file.filename || '')
      ).filter(Boolean);
    }

    function nextAiContextPayload(extra) {
      const config = window.graphenDomain || domainConfiguration || {};
      const nextAI = (config.pillar_blueprint || {}).next_ai || {};
      const preview = config.preview || {};
      const documents = nextAiFileNames(
        typeof uploadedPdfFiles !== 'undefined' ? uploadedPdfFiles : []
      );
      return Object.assign({
        tracking_id: window.currentTrackingId || null,
        industry: config.industry || '',
        use_case: config.use_case || '',
        objective: config.objective || '',
        persona: nextAI.persona || '',
        hint_topics: nextAI.hint_topics || [],
        primary_entities: preview.primary_entities || [],
        key_relationships: preview.key_relationships || [],
        tabular_files: nextAiFileNames(
          typeof uploadedCsvFiles !== 'undefined' ? uploadedCsvFiles : []
        ),
        document_files: documents.filter(name => !/\.(txt|md|rtf|json|xml)$/i.test(name)),
        text_files: documents.filter(name => /\.(txt|md|rtf|json|xml)$/i.test(name)),
        image_files: nextAiFileNames(
          typeof uploadedImageFiles !== 'undefined' ? uploadedImageFiles : []
        ),
        audio_files: nextAiFileNames(
          typeof uploadedAudioFiles !== 'undefined' ? uploadedAudioFiles : []
        ),
      }, extra || {});
    }

    async function nextAiApiRequest(path, payload) {
      const options = {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify(payload),
      };
      try {
        const response = await fetch(path, options);
        if (response.status !== 404) return response;
      } catch (_) {}
      return fetch('http://127.0.0.1:8011' + path, options);
    }

    function renderNextAiStatus(status) {
      window.nextAiStatusPayload = status || {};
      const setText = (id, value) => {
        const element = document.getElementById(id);
        if (element) element.textContent = value == null ? '—' : value;
      };
      setText('nextAiSourceCount', status.source_count);
      setText('nextAiChunkCount', status.chunk_count);
      setText('nextAiEntityCount', status.entity_count);
      setText('nextAiVectorState', status.vector_store);
      setText('nextAiPiiState', 'Active · ' + (status.pii_values_masked || 0) + ' masked');
      setText('nextAiWelcome', status.welcome);
      setText('nextAiTitle', 'Next AI — ' + (status.use_case || 'Ask Your Uploaded Evidence'));

      const agents = document.getElementById('nextAiAgents');
      if (agents) {
        agents.innerHTML = (status.agents || []).map(agent =>
          '<span class="next-ai-agent" title="' + nextAiEsc(agent.detail) + '">' +
          nextAiEsc(agent.name) + ' · ' + nextAiEsc(agent.status) + '</span>'
        ).join('');
      }
      const hints = document.getElementById('nextAiHints');
      if (hints) {
        hints.innerHTML = '';
        (status.hints || []).forEach(hint => {
          const button = document.createElement('button');
          button.type = 'button';
          button.className = 'suggest-chip';
          button.textContent = hint;
          button.addEventListener('click', () => askQuestion(hint));
          hints.appendChild(button);
        });
      }
    }

    async function refreshNextAI(force) {
      const payload = nextAiContextPayload();
      const signature = JSON.stringify(payload);
      if (!force && nextAiContextSignature === signature) return;
      nextAiContextSignature = signature;
      const welcome = document.getElementById('nextAiWelcome');
      if (welcome) welcome.textContent = 'Chunking, masking, indexing, and linking the active upload session…';
      try {
        const response = await nextAiApiRequest('/api/next-ai/status', payload);
        if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Next AI status HTTP ' + response.status);
        renderNextAiStatus(await response.json());
      } catch (error) {
        console.warn('Next AI status failed', error);
        if (welcome) {
          welcome.textContent = 'Next AI could not prepare the active RAG database. Verify the upload session and retry.';
        }
      }
    }

    function renderNextAiEvidence(evidence) {
      const list = document.getElementById('nextAiEvidenceList');
      const meta = document.getElementById('ctxRelMeta');
      if (meta) meta.textContent = evidence.length
        ? evidence.length + ' semantically matched chunk(s), ranked by cosine similarity.'
        : 'No evidence chunk passed the grounding threshold.';
      if (!list) return;
      list.innerHTML = evidence.length ? evidence.map(item =>
        '<div class="next-ai-evidence"><div class="next-ai-evidence-head"><span>' +
        nextAiEsc(item.filename) + ' · chunk ' + (Number(item.chunk_index) + 1) +
        '</span><span class="next-ai-evidence-score">' +
        Math.round(Number(item.score || 0) * 100) + '% match</span></div>' +
        '<div class="next-ai-evidence-text">' + nextAiEsc(item.excerpt) + '</div></div>'
      ).join('') : '<div class="crossdoc-empty">No evidence retrieved from the active RAG database.</div>';
    }

    function renderNextAiGraph(graph) {
      const wrap = document.getElementById('ctxGraphWrap');
      if (!wrap) return;
      const nodes = (graph && graph.nodes) || [];
      const edges = (graph && graph.edges) || [];
      const labels = Object.fromEntries(nodes.map(node => [node.id, node.label]));
      if (!nodes.length) {
        wrap.innerHTML = '<div class="empty-ctx"><div class="ic">🕸️</div>No graph entities or relationships matched this question.</div>';
        return;
      }
      const edgeHtml = edges.map(edge =>
        '<div class="next-ai-graph-edge"><span class="next-ai-graph-node">' +
        nextAiEsc(labels[edge.source] || edge.source) + '</span><span class="next-ai-graph-rel">' +
        nextAiEsc(edge.relationship) + '</span><span class="next-ai-graph-node">' +
        nextAiEsc(labels[edge.target] || edge.target) + '</span></div>'
      ).join('');
      const unlinked = nodes.filter(node =>
        !edges.some(edge => edge.source === node.id || edge.target === node.id)
      ).map(node =>
        '<div class="next-ai-graph-edge"><span class="next-ai-graph-node">' +
        nextAiEsc(node.label) + '</span><span class="next-ai-graph-rel">' +
        nextAiEsc(node.type) + '</span><span class="next-ai-graph-node">Retrieved context</span></div>'
      ).join('');
      wrap.innerHTML = '<div class="next-ai-graph">' + edgeHtml + unlinked + '</div>';
    }

    function nodeColor(type) {
      return { Property: '#4C8DFF', Tenant: '#27D199', Document: '#9B7CF6', Clause: '#FB5A6A', RenewalOption: '#F5A623' }[type] || '#888';
    }
    function propName(pid) { return PROPERTIES.find(p => p.id === pid)?.address || pid; }
    function tenName(tid) { return TENANTS.find(t => t.id === tid)?.name || tid; }
    function daysUntil(dateStr) { return Math.round((new Date(dateStr) - today) / 86400000); }

    async function askQuestion(presetQ, allowLlmSynthesis) {
      const input = document.getElementById('chatInput');
      const q = presetQ || (input ? input.value.trim() : '');
      if (!q) return;
      if (input) input.value = '';
      const scroll = document.getElementById('chatScroll');
      const fallback = document.getElementById('nextAiFallback');
      if (fallback) fallback.style.display = 'none';
      if (!allowLlmSynthesis) {
        scroll.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',
          '<div class="msg user"><div class="msg-bubble">' + nextAiEsc(q) + '</div></div>');
      }
      scroll.scrollTop = scroll.scrollHeight;
      const typingId = 'typing-' + Date.now();
      scroll.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',
        '<div class="msg ai" id="' + typingId + '"><div class="msg-bubble" style="padding:0">' +
        '<div class="typing"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div></div></div>');
      scroll.scrollTop = scroll.scrollHeight;
      const askButton = document.getElementById('nextAiAskBtn');
      if (askButton) askButton.disabled = true;
      try {
        const response = await nextAiApiRequest('/api/next-ai/ask', nextAiContextPayload({
          question: q,
          history: nextAiConversation.slice(-8),
          allow_llm_synthesis: !!allowLlmSynthesis,
        }));
        if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Next AI ask HTTP ' + response.status);
        const result = await response.json();
        const typing = document.getElementById(typingId);
        if (typing) typing.remove();
        const semanticFallback = result.grounding === 'maximum_semantic_relevance_rag';
        const grounded = result.grounding === 'hybrid_rag_graph_rag' || semanticFallback;
        const blocked = result.grounding === 'blocked';
        let label = 'Not in RAG database';
        if (semanticFallback) label = '✓ Best semantic database match';
        else if (grounded) label = '✓ Hybrid RAG grounded';
        else if (blocked) label = 'Guardrail blocked';
        else if (allowLlmSynthesis) label = '⚠ LLM synthesis · not RAG grounded';
        const groundingLabel = label + (semanticFallback ? ' · cautious synthesis' : '');
        const accepted = result.retrieval && result.retrieval.accepted_chunks || 0;
        scroll.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',
          '<div class="msg ai"><div class="msg-bubble">' +
          nextAiEsc(result.answer).replace(/\n/g, '<br>') +
          '</div><div class="msg-meta' + (grounded ? '' : ' ungrounded') + '">' +
          (grounded ? '<span class="grounded-tag">' + groundingLabel + '</span>' : groundingLabel) +
          ' · ' + accepted + ' chunk(s) · semantic + graph + Cypher</div></div>');
        scroll.scrollTop = scroll.scrollHeight;
        nextAiConversation.push({ role: 'user', content: q });
        nextAiConversation.push({ role: 'assistant', content: result.answer });
        nextAiConversation = nextAiConversation.slice(-10);
        renderNextAiEvidence(result.evidence || []);
        renderNextAiGraph(result.graph_context || {});
        const trace = document.getElementById('ctxJsonWrap');
        if (trace) {
          trace.innerHTML = '<pre style="white-space:pre-wrap;margin:0">' +
            nextAiEsc(JSON.stringify({
              grounding: result.grounding,
              retrieval: result.retrieval,
              citations: result.citations || [],
              cypher_query: result.cypher_query,
              graph_rows: result.graph_rows || [],
              guardrail: result.guardrail,
            }, null, 2)) + '</pre>';
        }
        if (result.can_synthesize_with_llm) {
          nextAiLastUnavailableQuestion = q;
          if (fallback) fallback.style.display = 'flex';
          const fallbackButton = document.getElementById('nextAiFallbackBtn');
          if (fallbackButton) {
            fallbackButton.onclick = () =>
              askQuestion(nextAiLastUnavailableQuestion, true);
          }
        }
        switchCtx((result.evidence || []).length ? 'rels' : 'graph');
      } catch (error) {
        console.warn('Next AI question failed', error);
        const typing = document.getElementById(typingId);
        if (typing) typing.remove();
        scroll.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',
          '<div class="msg ai"><div class="msg-bubble">Next AI could not query the active RAG database. Please retry after verifying the upload session.</div></div>');
      } finally {
        if (askButton) askButton.disabled = false;
      }
    }
    function escapeHtml(s) { return s.replace(/[&<>]/g, c => ({ '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;' }[c])); }

    function generateAnswer(q) {
      const ql = q.toLowerCase();
      let contextNodes = [], cypherResult = [], answer = '';

      if (ql.includes('expir') || ql.includes('90 day') || ql.includes('soon')) {
        const days = ql.includes('30') ? 30 : ql.includes('60') ? 60 : ql.includes('180') ? 180 : 90;
        const exp = LEASES.filter(l => daysUntil(l.end) <= days && daysUntil(l.end) >= 0)
          .sort((a, b) => daysUntil(a.end) - daysUntil(b.end));
        cypherResult = exp.map(l => ({ property: propName(l.prop), tenant: tenName(l.tenant), expires: l.end, days_left: daysUntil(l.end), sqft: l.sqft }));
        contextNodes = exp.flatMap(l => [l.prop, l.tenant, l.id]);
        if (exp.length === 0) {
          answer = `No documents expire in the next ${days} days. The next expiration is further out — check the Risk Dashboard for the full timeline.`;
        } else {
          answer = `<b>${exp.length} document${exp.length > 1 ? 's' : ''} expire${exp.length === 1 ? 's' : ''} in the next ${days} days:</b><br><br>` +
            exp.map(l => `• <b>${tenName(l.tenant)}</b> — ${propName(l.prop)} — expires ${l.end} (${daysUntil(l.end)} days) — ${l.sqft.toLocaleString()} sqft`).join('<br>') +
            `<br><br><i>Source: Neo4j Document nodes, filtered by end_date.</i>`;
        }
      }
      else if (ql.includes('concentrat') || ql.includes('biggest') || ql.includes('largest tenant') || ql.includes('risk') && ql.includes('tenant')) {
        const byTenant = {};
        LEASES.forEach(l => { const name = tenName(l.tenant); byTenant[name] = (byTenant[name] || 0) + l.sqft; });
        const totalSqft = Object.values(byTenant).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);
        const rows = Object.entries(byTenant).map(([name, sqft]) => ({ tenant: name, sqft, pct: Math.round(sqft / totalSqft * 1000) / 10 }))
          .sort((a, b) => b.sqft - a.sqft);
        cypherResult = rows;
        contextNodes = LEASES.map(l => l.tenant).filter((v, i, a) => a.indexOf(v) === i).concat(LEASES.map(l => l.id));
        const top = rows[0];
        answer = `<b>${top.tenant}</b> has the highest concentration: <b>${top.sqft.toLocaleString()} sqft</b> (${top.pct}% of total portfolio sqft) across ${LEASES.filter(l => tenName(l.tenant) === top.tenant).length} documents.` +
          (top.pct > 25 ? ` <span style="color:var(--amber)">⚠️ This exceeds the 25% concentration risk threshold</span> — consider diversification or renewal renegotiation.` : '') +
          `<br><br><i>Source: aggregated across Document→Tenant relationships in the graph.</i>`;
      }
      else if (ql.includes('clause') || ql.includes('terminat') || ql.includes('co-tenancy') || ql.includes('exclusiv') || ql.includes('high-risk') || ql.includes('high risk')) {
        cypherResult = CLAUSES.map(c => ({ document: c.document, type: c.type, property: propName(LEASES.find(l => l.id === c.document)?.prop), text: c.text }));
        contextNodes = CLAUSES.map(c => c.document).concat(CLAUSES.map((c, i) => 'CL' + i));
        answer = `<b>${CLAUSES.length} high-risk clauses</b> detected across the portfolio:<br><br>` +
          CLAUSES.map(c => `• <b>${c.type}</b> (${c.document}, ${propName(LEASES.find(l => l.id === c.document)?.prop)}): ${c.text}`).join('<br><br>') +
          `<br><br><i>Source: Clause nodes flagged risk_level=HIGH during LLM extraction.</i>`;
      }
      else if (ql.includes('average') && ql.includes('rent')) {
        const avg = (LEASES.reduce((a, l) => a + l.rent, 0) / LEASES.length).toFixed(2);
        cypherResult = [{ metric: 'avg_rent_psf', value: parseFloat(avg), document_count: LEASES.length }];
        contextNodes = LEASES.map(l => l.id);
        answer = `The average base rent across the portfolio is <b>$${avg} per sqft</b>, calculated across ${LEASES.length} active documents.<br><br><i>Source: AVG(Document.base_rent_psf) over all Document nodes.</i>`;
      }
      else {
        cypherResult = LEASES.slice(0, 6).map(l => ({ property: propName(l.prop), tenant: tenName(l.tenant), end: l.end, rent_psf: l.rent }));
        contextNodes = LEASES.slice(0, 6).flatMap(l => [l.prop, l.tenant, l.id]);
        answer = `Here's a snapshot from the portfolio graph relevant to your question — ${LEASES.length} documents across ${PROPERTIES.length} properties and ${new Set(TENANTS.map(t => t.name)).size} unique tenants. Try asking about expirations, concentration risk, or specific clauses for a more targeted answer.`;
      }
      return { answer, contextNodes: [...new Set(contextNodes)], cypherResult };
    }

    function switchCtx(which) {
      document.querySelectorAll('.ctx-tab').forEach(t => t.classList.toggle('active', t.dataset.ctx === which));
      document.getElementById('ctxGraphWrap').style.display = which === 'graph' ? 'block' : 'none';
      const relWrap = document.getElementById('ctxRelWrap');
      if (relWrap) relWrap.classList.toggle('active', which === 'rels');
      document.getElementById('ctxJsonWrap').style.display = which === 'json' ? 'block' : 'none';
    }

    let lastAskEdgeRows = [];
    let lastAskDocumentRows = [];
    const ASK_GRAPH_PATH = 'Property -> HAS_LEASE -> Document -> SIGNED_BY -> Tenant';

    function nodeTypeColor(type) {
      return { Property: '#4C8DFF', Tenant: '#27D199', Document: '#9B7CF6', Clause: '#FB5A6A', RenewalOption: '#F5A623', TerminationRight: '#FB5A6A' }[type] || '#888';
    }

    function buildAskGraphPayload(nodeIds) {
      const idSet = new Set(nodeIds);
      const nodes = [];
      const links = [];
      const seenNode = new Set();
      const seenLink = new Set();

      function addNode(id, type, label, extra) {
        if (seenNode.has(id)) return;
        seenNode.add(id);
        nodes.push({ id, type, label, ...(extra || {}) });
      }
      function addLink(source, target, relationship) {
        const key = `${source}|${relationship}|${target}`;
        if (seenLink.has(key)) return;
        seenLink.add(key);
        links.push({ source, target, relationship });
      }

      nodeIds.forEach(id => {
        if (id.startsWith('P')) addNode(id, 'Property', propName(id));
        else if (id.startsWith('T') && !id.startsWith('TN-') && !id.startsWith('CL')) addNode(id, 'Tenant', tenName(id));
        else if (id.startsWith('TN-')) addNode(id, 'Tenant', id.slice(3));
        else if (id.startsWith('CL')) {
          const idx = parseInt(id.slice(2), 10);
          const c = CLAUSES[idx];
          addNode(id, 'Clause', c ? c.type : 'Risk Clause');
        } else if (id.startsWith('LG') || /^LG-/.test(id)) addNode(id, 'Document', id);
        else addNode(id, 'Document', id);
      });

      // Expand one hop around documents so the relationship table is complete for the answer
      LEASES.forEach(l => {
        const documentHit = idSet.has(l.id);
        const propHit = idSet.has(l.prop);
        const tenantHit = idSet.has(l.tenant) || idSet.has('TN-' + tenName(l.tenant));
        if (!(documentHit || propHit || tenantHit)) return;

        addNode(l.id, 'Document', l.id);
        addNode(l.prop, 'Property', propName(l.prop));
        const tname = tenName(l.tenant);
        addNode('TN-' + tname, 'Tenant', tname);
        addLink(l.prop, l.id, 'HAS_LEASE');
        addLink(l.id, 'TN-' + tname, 'SIGNED_BY');

        CLAUSES.forEach((c, i) => {
          if (c.document !== l.id) return;
          const cid = 'CL' + i;
          addNode(cid, 'Clause', c.type);
          addLink(l.id, cid, 'HAS_CLAUSE');
        });
        RENEWALS.forEach((r, i) => {
          if (r.document !== l.id) return;
          const rid = 'RO' + i;
          addNode(rid, 'RenewalOption', r.term + 'yr option');
          addLink(l.id, rid, 'HAS_OPTION');
        });
        if (typeof TERMINATIONS !== 'undefined') {
          TERMINATIONS.forEach((t, i) => {
            if (t.document !== l.id) return;
            const tid = 'TR' + i;
            addNode(tid, 'TerminationRight', 'Termination');
            addLink(l.id, tid, 'HAS_TERM_RIGHT');
          });
        }
      });

      return { nodes, links };
    }

    function labelForAskNode(id, nodesById) {
      const n = nodesById.get(id);
      if (n) return n.label;
      if (typeof id === 'object' && id && id.label) return id.label;
      return String(id);
    }

    function typeForAskNode(id, nodesById) {
      const n = nodesById.get(id);
      if (n) return n.type;
      if (typeof id === 'object' && id && id.type) return id.type;
      return 'Node';
    }

    function renderAskRelationshipTables(graphPayload, contextNodes) {
      const nodesById = new Map((graphPayload.nodes || []).map(n => [n.id, n]));
      lastAskEdgeRows = (graphPayload.links || []).map((link, i) => {
        const sid = typeof link.source === 'object' ? link.source.id : link.source;
        const tid = typeof link.target === 'object' ? link.target.id : link.target;
        return {
          id: i + 1,
          source: labelForAskNode(sid, nodesById),
          source_id: sid,
          source_type: typeForAskNode(sid, nodesById),
          relationship: link.relationship || 'RELATED_TO',
          target: labelForAskNode(tid, nodesById),
          target_id: tid,
          target_type: typeForAskNode(tid, nodesById),
        };
      });

      const documentIds = new Set();
      (contextNodes || []).forEach(id => {
        if (String(id).startsWith('LG')) documentIds.add(id);
      });
      (graphPayload.nodes || []).forEach(n => {
        if (n.type === 'Document') documentIds.add(n.id);
      });
      lastAskDocumentRows = (typeof relationshipRows !== 'undefined' && relationshipRows.length
        ? relationshipRows
        : (typeof buildRelationshipRowsFromGraph === 'function' ? buildRelationshipRowsFromGraph() : [])
      ).filter(r => documentIds.has(r.document_id));

      // Fallback: synthesize document rows from demo ontology if filter empty
      if (!lastAskDocumentRows.length && documentIds.size) {
        lastAskDocumentRows = [...documentIds].map((lid, i) => {
          const l = LEASES.find(x => x.id === lid);
          if (!l) return null;
          const edges = ['HAS_LEASE', 'SIGNED_BY'];
          const clauses = CLAUSES.filter(c => c.document === lid).map(c => normalizeClauseLabel(c.type)).filter(Boolean);
          if (clauses.length) edges.push('HAS_CLAUSE');
          if (RENEWALS.some(r => r.document === lid)) edges.push('HAS_OPTION');
          if (typeof TERMINATIONS !== 'undefined' && TERMINATIONS.some(t => t.document === lid)) edges.push('HAS_TERM_RIGHT');
          return {
            id: i + 1,
            document_id: lid,
            property: propName(l.prop),
            tenant: tenName(l.tenant),
            start_date: l.start || '',
            end_date: l.end || '',
            rent_psf: l.rent,
            sqft: l.sqft,
            relationship: (typeof GRAPH_PATH !== 'undefined' ? GRAPH_PATH : ASK_GRAPH_PATH),
            graph_edges: edges,
            special_clauses: [...new Set(clauses)],
          };
        }).filter(Boolean);
      }

      const edgeTbody = document.querySelector('#ctxRelTable tbody');
      const edgeMeta = document.getElementById('ctxRelMeta');
      if (edgeMeta) {
        edgeMeta.textContent = lastAskEdgeRows.length
          ? `${lastAskEdgeRows.length} relationships generated from this graph context`
          : 'No relationships found for this answer.';
      }
      if (edgeTbody) {
        edgeTbody.innerHTML = lastAskEdgeRows.length
          ? lastAskEdgeRows.map(r => `
              <tr>
                <td style="font-family:var(--mono);color:var(--tx-3)">${r.id}</td>
                <td><span class="ctx-type-dot" style="background:${nodeTypeColor(r.source_type)}"></span>${escapeHtml(r.source)}</td>
                <td>${escapeHtml(r.source_type)}</td>
                <td><span class="ctx-edge-pill">${escapeHtml(r.relationship)}</span></td>
                <td><span class="ctx-type-dot" style="background:${nodeTypeColor(r.target_type)}"></span>${escapeHtml(r.target)}</td>
                <td>${escapeHtml(r.target_type)}</td>
              </tr>`).join('')
          : `<tr><td colspan="6" style="text-align:center;color:var(--tx-3);padding:28px">No relationships in graph context</td></tr>`;
      }

      const card = document.getElementById('askRelCard');
      const documentTbody = document.querySelector('#askRelTable tbody');
      const askMeta = document.getElementById('askRelMeta');
      if (card) card.classList.toggle('visible', lastAskDocumentRows.length > 0 || lastAskEdgeRows.length > 0);
      if (askMeta) {
        askMeta.textContent = lastAskDocumentRows.length
          ? `${lastAskDocumentRows.length} document path(s) in retrieved context — Property → HAS_LEASE → Document → SIGNED_BY → Tenant`
          : 'Edge list generated; no document-centric rows for this query.';
      }
      if (documentTbody) {
        documentTbody.innerHTML = lastAskDocumentRows.length
          ? lastAskDocumentRows.map(r => `
              <tr>
                <td><span style="font-family:var(--mono);color:#c4b5fd">${escapeHtml(r.document_id)}</span></td>
                <td><span style="color:#4C8DFF">${escapeHtml(r.property)}</span></td>
                <td><span style="color:#27D199">${escapeHtml(r.tenant)}</span></td>
                <td style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11.5px">${escapeHtml(r.start_date || '—')}</td>
                <td style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11.5px">${escapeHtml(r.end_date || '—')}</td>
                <td style="font-family:var(--mono)">${r.rent_psf != null && r.rent_psf !== '' ? '$' + fmtMoney(r.rent_psf) : '—'}</td>
                <td style="font-family:var(--mono)">${r.sqft != null && r.sqft !== '' ? fmtMoney(r.sqft) : '—'}</td>
                <td>${typeof relationshipPathHtml === 'function' ? relationshipPathHtml() : escapeHtml(ASK_GRAPH_PATH)}</td>
                <td>${typeof edgesHtml === 'function' ? edgesHtml(r.graph_edges) : escapeHtml((r.graph_edges || []).join(', '))}</td>
                <td>${typeof specialClausesHtml === 'function' ? specialClausesHtml(r.special_clauses) : escapeHtml((r.special_clauses || []).join(', ') || '—')}</td>
              </tr>`).join('')
          : `<tr><td colspan="10" style="text-align:center;color:#6b7590;padding:24px">No document relationship rows for this answer.</td></tr>`;
      }
    }

    function downloadAskRelationshipsCsv() {
      if (!lastAskEdgeRows.length) return;
      const headers = ['id', 'source', 'source_type', 'relationship', 'target', 'target_type'];
      const lines = [headers.join(',')].concat(lastAskEdgeRows.map(r => headers.map(h => {
        const v = String(r[h] ?? '');
        return /[",\n]/.test(v) ? `"${v.replace(/"/g, '""')}"` : v;
      }).join(',')));
      downloadBlob('ask_ai_relationship_edges.csv', lines.join('\n'), 'text/csv;charset=utf-8');
    }

    function downloadAskDocumentTableCsv() {
      if (!lastAskDocumentRows.length) return;
      if (typeof relationshipsToCsv === 'function') {
        downloadBlob('ask_ai_document_relationships.csv', relationshipsToCsv(lastAskDocumentRows), 'text/csv;charset=utf-8');
      }
    }

    function downloadAskDocumentTableJson() {
      if (!lastAskDocumentRows.length) return;
      downloadBlob('ask_ai_document_relationships.json', JSON.stringify(lastAskDocumentRows, null, 2), 'application/json');
    }

    function renderContextGraph(nodeIds) {
      const wrap = document.getElementById('ctxGraphWrap');
      wrap.innerHTML = '<svg width="100%" height="100%" id="miniCtxSvg"></svg>';
      const W = wrap.clientWidth || 320, H = wrap.clientHeight || 380;
      const svg = d3.select('#miniCtxSvg');
      const payload = buildAskGraphPayload(nodeIds);
      const nodes = payload.nodes.slice();
      const links = payload.links.map(l => ({ ...l }));
      const sim = d3.forceSimulation(nodes)
        .force('link', d3.forceLink(links).id(d => d.id).distance(58).strength(0.6))
        .force('charge', d3.forceManyBody().strength(-130))
        .force('center', d3.forceCenter(W / 2, H / 2))
        .force('collide', d3.forceCollide(26));
      svg.append('g').selectAll('line').data(links).join('line').attr('stroke', '#2A3658').attr('stroke-width', 1.3);
      const node = svg.append('g').selectAll('g').data(nodes).join('g');
      node.append('circle').attr('r', 13).attr('fill', d => nodeColor(d.type)).attr('opacity', 0.92)
        .attr('stroke', '#fff').attr('stroke-opacity', 0.15).attr('stroke-width', 1.5);
      node.append('text').text(d => d.label.length > 14 ? d.label.slice(0, 13) + '…' : d.label)
        .attr('font-size', 9).attr('fill', '#AEB8D4').attr('font-family', 'IBM Plex Mono')
        .attr('text-anchor', 'middle').attr('y', 24);
      sim.on('tick', () => {
        svg.selectAll('line').attr('x1', d => d.source.x).attr('y1', d => d.source.y).attr('x2', d => d.target.x).attr('y2', d => d.target.y);
        node.attr('transform', d => `translate(${d.x},${d.y})`);
      });
      return payload;
    }

    /* ============================================================
       FULL GRAPH EXPLORER (D3 force-directed)
       ============================================================ */
    let fullSim;
    let igActiveFilter = 'all';
    let igGraphCache = { nodes: [], links: [] };
    let igTabsMeta = null;
    let igTabsLoading = false;
    window.igGraphCache = igGraphCache;
    window.igTabsMeta = igTabsMeta;

    const IG_TYPE_COLORS = {
      Individual: '#4C8DFF', Patient: '#4C8DFF', Person: '#4C8DFF', Property: '#4C8DFF',
      Company: '#F5A623', Provider: '#F5A623', Organisation: '#F5A623', Organization: '#F5A623', Tenant: '#27D199',
      Account: '#27D199', Claim: '#27D199', Record: '#27D199', Lease: '#9B7CF6',
      Sanctioned: '#FB5A6A', Device: '#9B7CF6', Address: '#94A3B8',
      Regulation: '#EAB308', Policy: '#2DD4D4', Document: '#EAB308', KYC: '#84CC16',
      Image: '#FB7185', Audio: '#A78BFA', Text: '#38BDF8',
      Alert: '#FB5A6A', Pattern: '#FB5A6A'
    };

    function igFileName(f) {
      if (!f) return '';
      return (typeof f === 'string') ? f : (f.name || f.filename || '');
    }

    function igInventory() {
      const tabular = (typeof uploadedCsvFiles !== 'undefined' ? uploadedCsvFiles : []).map(igFileName).filter(Boolean);
      const documents = (typeof uploadedPdfFiles !== 'undefined' ? uploadedPdfFiles : []).map(igFileName).filter(Boolean);
      const images = (typeof uploadedImageFiles !== 'undefined' ? uploadedImageFiles : []).map(igFileName).filter(Boolean);
      const audio = (typeof uploadedAudioFiles !== 'undefined' ? uploadedAudioFiles : []).map(igFileName).filter(Boolean);
      const textFiles = documents.filter(n => /\.(txt|md|rtf)$/i.test(n) || /text/i.test(n));
      const usingDemo = !(tabular.length || documents.length || images.length || audio.length);
      if (usingDemo) {
        const configured = window.graphenDomain;
        if (configured) {
          const entities = (configured.preview && configured.preview.primary_entities) || ['Entity', 'Record'];
          const slug = String(configured.use_case || 'Configured').replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9]+/g, '_');
          return {
            usingDemo: true,
            configuredDemo: true,
            tabular: entities.slice(0, 5).map((entity, index) =>
              'CFG' + (index + 1) + '_' + String(entity).replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9]+/g, '_') + '.csv'
            ),
            documents: ['CFG_' + slug + '_Evidence.pdf'],
            images: [],
            audio: [],
            textFiles: [],
          };
        }
        return {
          usingDemo: true,
          tabular: ['Entity_Registry.csv', 'Business_Records.csv', 'Relationship_Evidence.csv'],
          documents: ['Policy_Evidence.pdf', 'Supporting_Records.pdf'],
          images: [],
          audio: [],
          textFiles: [],
        };
      }
      return { usingDemo: false, tabular, documents, images, audio, textFiles };
    }

    function igAbbrev(type) {
      const map = {
        Individual: 'IND', Patient: 'PAT', Person: 'PER', Company: 'CO', Provider: 'PRV',
        Organisation: 'ORG', Organization: 'ORG', Account: 'ACC', Claim: 'CLM', Record: 'REC',
        Sanctioned: 'SAN', Device: 'DEV', Address: 'ADR', Regulation: 'REG', Policy: 'POL',
        Document: 'DOC', KYC: 'KYC', Image: 'IMG', Audio: 'AUD', Text: 'TXT',
        Property: 'PRP', Tenant: 'TNT', Lease: 'LSE', Alert: 'ALR', Pattern: 'RNG'
      };
      return map[type] || String(type || 'NOD').slice(0, 3).toUpperCase();
    }

    function igNodeColor(type) {
      return IG_TYPE_COLORS[type] || '#4C8DFF';
    }

    function buildInteractiveGraphData(tabsMeta) {
      const inv = igInventory();
      const industry = ((tabsMeta && tabsMeta.industry) || '').toLowerCase();
      const useCase = ((tabsMeta && tabsMeta.use_case) || '').toLowerCase();
      const isHealth = /health|clinical|patient|pharma/.test(industry + useCase);
      const isLease = /real estate|lease|property|tenant/.test(industry + useCase);
      const isAml = /aml|financial crime|bank|sanction|kyc/.test(industry + useCase);
      const isSupply = /supply|procurement|logistics/.test(industry + useCase);
      const configuredDomain = window.graphenDomain || {};
      const configuredEntities = ((configuredDomain.preview || {}).primary_entities || []).slice(0, 6);
      const configuredRelationships = ((configuredDomain.preview || {}).key_relationships || []).slice(0, 6);

      const nodes = [];
      const links = [];
      const pushNode = (n) => { nodes.push(n); return n; };

      const roleOf = (name, index) => {
        if (configuredEntities.length) return configuredEntities[index % configuredEntities.length];
        const s = String(name).toLowerCase();
        if (/ds[-_]?1|individual|person|customer|patient|employee/.test(s)) return isHealth ? 'Patient' : (isLease ? 'Tenant' : 'Individual');
        if (/ds[-_]?2|compan|org|provider|vendor|supplier|landlord/.test(s)) return isHealth ? 'Provider' : (isSupply ? 'Organisation' : 'Company');
        if (/ds[-_]?3|account|claim|invoice|bank/.test(s)) return isHealth ? 'Claim' : (isSupply ? 'Record' : 'Account');
        if (/ds[-_]?4|transact|payment|transfer/.test(s)) return 'Account';
        if (/ds[-_]?5|device|imei|mobile/.test(s)) return 'Device';
        if (/ds[-_]?6|address|location|site/.test(s)) return 'Address';
        if (/ds[-_]?7|sanction|ofac|watchlist/.test(s)) return 'Sanctioned';
        if (/property|building|asset/.test(s)) return 'Property';
        if (/tenant|lessee/.test(s)) return 'Tenant';
        if (/lease|contract/.test(s)) return 'Lease';
        return 'Record';
      };

      const labelsFor = (type, i) => {
        if (configuredEntities.length) {
          return type + '-' + String(i + 1).padStart(3, '0');
        }
        if (isHealth) {
          const pats = ['Asha Mehta', 'Dr. Rao Clinic', 'Claim-441', 'City Hospital', 'LabCorp East'];
          return pats[i % pats.length] + (i >= pats.length ? (' #' + (i + 1)) : '');
        }
        if (isLease) {
          const pats = ['Commerce Blvd', 'Apex Retail', 'LG-1042', 'Metro Tower', 'North Plaza'];
          return pats[i % pats.length] + (i >= pats.length ? (' #' + (i + 1)) : '');
        }
        if (isAml) {
          const pats = ['Priya Sharma', 'Rahul Singh', 'ACC-001', 'DEF Holdings', 'Shell Co'];
          return pats[i % pats.length] + (i >= pats.length ? (' #' + (i + 1)) : '');
        }
        return type + '-' + String(i + 1).padStart(3, '0');
      };

      inv.tabular.forEach((fname, i) => {
        const type = roleOf(fname, i);
        pushNode({
          id: 'tab-' + i,
          label: labelsFor(type, i),
          abbrev: igAbbrev(type),
          type,
          modality: 'tabular',
          source: 'tabular',
          dashed: false,
          inRing: false,
          alert: false,
          data: { source_file: fname, modality: 'tabular', industry: (tabsMeta && tabsMeta.industry) || '-' }
        });
      });

      inv.documents.forEach((fname, i) => {
        const s = fname.toLowerCase();
        let type = 'Document';
        if (/regulat|pmla|rbi|act|circular|hipaa|policy.?act/.test(s)) type = 'Regulation';
        else if (/sop|policy|guideline/.test(s)) type = 'Policy';
        else if (/kyc|typolog|aml/.test(s)) type = isAml ? 'KYC' : 'Document';
        else if (/\.txt|\.md|text/.test(s)) type = 'Text';
        const short = fname.replace(/\.[^.]+$/, '').replace(/[_-]+/g, ' ').slice(0, 22);
        pushNode({
          id: 'doc-' + i,
          label: short,
          abbrev: igAbbrev(type),
          type,
          modality: 'document',
          source: 'document',
          dashed: true,
          inRing: false,
          alert: false,
          data: { source_file: fname, modality: 'document', extracted: true }
        });
      });

      inv.images.forEach((fname, i) => {
        pushNode({
          id: 'img-' + i,
          label: fname.replace(/\.[^.]+$/, '').slice(0, 18) || ('Image ' + (i + 1)),
          abbrev: 'IMG',
          type: 'Image',
          modality: 'image',
          source: 'image',
          dashed: true,
          inRing: false,
          alert: false,
          data: { source_file: fname, modality: 'image', ocr: 'available' }
        });
      });

      inv.audio.forEach((fname, i) => {
        pushNode({
          id: 'aud-' + i,
          label: fname.replace(/\.[^.]+$/, '').slice(0, 18) || ('Audio ' + (i + 1)),
          abbrev: 'AUD',
          type: 'Audio',
          modality: 'audio',
          source: 'audio',
          dashed: true,
          inRing: false,
          alert: false,
          data: { source_file: fname, modality: 'audio', transcript: 'available' }
        });
      });

      if (nodes.length < 4) {
        const seedTypes = configuredEntities.length ? configuredEntities : (isHealth
          ? ['Patient', 'Provider', 'Claim', 'Document']
          : (isLease ? ['Property', 'Tenant', 'Lease', 'Document'] : ['Individual', 'Company', 'Account', 'Device']));
        seedTypes.forEach((type, i) => {
          if (nodes.some(n => n.type === type)) return;
          pushNode({
            id: 'seed-' + i,
            label: labelsFor(type, i),
            abbrev: igAbbrev(type),
            type,
            modality: 'tabular',
            source: 'derived',
            dashed: type === 'Document',
            inRing: false,
            alert: false,
            data: { source_file: '(pipeline derived)', modality: type === 'Document' ? 'document' : 'tabular' }
          });
        });
      }

      const byMod = (m) => nodes.filter(n => n.modality === m);
      const tabularNodes = byMod('tabular');
      const docNodes = byMod('document');
      const imgNodes = byMod('image');
      const audNodes = byMod('audio');

      for (let i = 0; i < tabularNodes.length - 1; i++) {
        const rel = configuredRelationships.length
          ? configuredRelationships[i % configuredRelationships.length]
          : (isAml ? (i % 2 ? 'OWNS' : 'TRANSFERRED_TO')
          : (isHealth ? (i % 2 ? 'TREATED_BY' : 'BILLED_AS')
            : (isLease ? (i % 2 ? 'HAS_LEASE' : 'SIGNED_BY') : 'RELATED_TO')));
        links.push({
          source: tabularNodes[i].id,
          target: tabularNodes[i + 1].id,
          label: rel,
          cross: false,
          ring: false,
          kind: 'structured'
        });
      }

      let crossCount = 0;
      const evidence = docNodes.concat(imgNodes, audNodes);
      evidence.forEach((ev, i) => {
        const src = tabularNodes[i % Math.max(tabularNodes.length, 1)];
        if (!src) return;
        const rel = configuredRelationships.length
          ? configuredRelationships[i % configuredRelationships.length]
          : (isHealth ? (ev.type === 'Image' ? 'SUPPORTS_CLAIM' : 'GOVERNS')
            : (isAml ? (ev.type === 'Regulation' ? 'GOVERNS' : (ev.type === 'Policy' ? 'TRIGGERS_ALERT' : 'CONTRADICTS_INCOME'))
              : (ev.modality === 'audio' ? 'MENTIONS' : 'EVIDENCED_BY')));
        links.push({
          source: src.id,
          target: ev.id,
          label: rel,
          cross: true,
          ring: false,
          kind: 'cross_source'
        });
        crossCount++;
      });

      const ringCandidates = configuredEntities.length
        ? tabularNodes
        : nodes.filter(n => ['Account', 'Claim', 'Record', 'Lease', 'Patient'].includes(n.type));
      const ringNodes = (ringCandidates.length >= 3 ? ringCandidates : tabularNodes).slice(0, 4);
      ringNodes.forEach(n => { n.inRing = true; });
      for (let i = 0; i < ringNodes.length; i++) {
        const a = ringNodes[i];
        const b = ringNodes[(i + 1) % ringNodes.length];
        if (!a || !b || ringNodes.length < 2) break;
        links.push({
          source: a.id,
          target: b.id,
          label: configuredRelationships.length
            ? configuredRelationships[i % configuredRelationships.length]
            : (isHealth ? 'REFERS_TO' : (isAml ? 'TRANSFERRED_TO' : (isLease ? 'CO_TERMINUS' : 'CYCLES_WITH'))),
          cross: false,
          ring: true,
          kind: 'pattern'
        });
      }

      const san = nodes.find(n => n.type === 'Sanctioned');
      if (san && tabularNodes[0]) {
        links.push({
          source: tabularNodes[0].id,
          target: san.id,
          label: 'CONNECTED_TO_SANCTIONED',
          cross: false,
          ring: false,
          kind: 'pattern'
        });
        san.alert = true;
        tabularNodes[0].alert = true;
      } else if (ringNodes[0]) {
        ringNodes[0].alert = true;
      }

      const alertNodes = nodes.filter(n => n.alert || n.inRing).length;

      return {
        nodes,
        links,
        stats: {
          tabular: tabularNodes.length,
          documents: docNodes.length,
          images: imgNodes.length,
          audio: audNodes.length,
          cross: crossCount,
          pattern: ringNodes.length,
          alerts: Math.max(1, Math.min(8, alertNodes)),
          sources: inv.tabular.length + inv.documents.length + inv.images.length + inv.audio.length,
          usingDemo: inv.usingDemo,
        }
      };
    }

    function filteredIgGraph() {
      const nodes = igGraphCache.nodes || [];
      const links = igGraphCache.links || [];
      const f = igActiveFilter || 'all';
      if (f === 'all') return { nodes, links };

      let keep = new Set();
      if (f.startsWith('modality:')) {
        const mod = f.split(':')[1];
        nodes.forEach(n => { if (n.modality === mod) keep.add(n.id); });
      } else if (f === 'cross_source') {
        links.filter(l => l.cross).forEach(l => {
          keep.add(typeof l.source === 'object' ? l.source.id : l.source);
          keep.add(typeof l.target === 'object' ? l.target.id : l.target);
        });
      } else if (f === 'pattern:ring') {
        nodes.forEach(n => { if (n.inRing) keep.add(n.id); });
        links.filter(l => l.ring).forEach(l => {
          keep.add(typeof l.source === 'object' ? l.source.id : l.source);
          keep.add(typeof l.target === 'object' ? l.target.id : l.target);
        });
      } else if (f === 'pattern:sanctions') {
        nodes.forEach(n => {
          if (n.type === 'Sanctioned' || /sanction/i.test(n.label) || n.alert) keep.add(n.id);
        });
        links.forEach(l => {
          if (/SANCTION/i.test(l.label || '')) {
            keep.add(typeof l.source === 'object' ? l.source.id : l.source);
            keep.add(typeof l.target === 'object' ? l.target.id : l.target);
          }
        });
      } else if (f.startsWith('pattern:')) {
        nodes.forEach(n => { if (n.alert || n.inRing) keep.add(n.id); });
        links.filter(l => l.kind === 'pattern' || l.ring).forEach(l => {
          keep.add(typeof l.source === 'object' ? l.source.id : l.source);
          keep.add(typeof l.target === 'object' ? l.target.id : l.target);
        });
      } else {
        return { nodes, links };
      }

      if (!keep.size) return { nodes, links };
      const fnodes = nodes.filter(n => keep.has(n.id));
      const ids = new Set(fnodes.map(n => n.id));
      const flinks = links.filter(l => {
        const s = typeof l.source === 'object' ? l.source.id : l.source;
        const t = typeof l.target === 'object' ? l.target.id : l.target;
        return ids.has(s) && ids.has(t);
      });
      return { nodes: fnodes, links: flinks };
    }

    function renderIgFilterBar(tabs) {
      const bar = document.getElementById('igFilterBar');
      if (!bar) return;
      const meta = document.getElementById('igFilterMeta');
      const metaHtml = meta ? meta.outerHTML : '<span class="ig-filter-meta" id="igFilterMeta"></span>';
      const list = (tabs && tabs.length) ? tabs : [{ id: 'all', label: 'All', filter: 'all', emphasis: false }];
      bar.innerHTML = list.map(t => {
        const warn = t.emphasis || t.icon === 'warning' ? ' warn' : '';
        const active = (t.filter === igActiveFilter) ? ' active' : '';
        const icon = t.icon === 'warning' ? '! ' : '';
        const safeLabel = String(t.label || t.id).replace(/</g, '&lt;');
        const filt = String(t.filter || 'all').replace(/\\/g, '\\\\').replace(/'/g, "\\'");
        return '<button class="ig-filter' + warn + active + '" data-filter="' + String(t.filter).replace(/"/g, '') + '" onclick="setIgFilter(\'' + filt + '\')">' + icon + safeLabel + '</button>';
      }).join('') + metaHtml;
    }

    function renderIgLegend(legend) {
      const el = document.getElementById('igLegend');
      if (!el) return;
      const items = (legend && legend.length) ? legend : [
        { key: 'Individual', color: '#4C8DFF', dashed: false },
        { key: 'Evidence', color: '#EAB308', dashed: true },
      ];
      el.innerHTML = items.map(item => {
        const dashed = item.dashed ? ' dashed' : '';
        const color = item.color || '#4C8DFF';
        return '<div class="legend-row"><span class="legend-dot' + dashed + '" style="background:' + color + ';color:' + color + '"></span>' + String(item.key).replace(/</g, '&lt;') + '</div>';
      }).join('');
    }

    function updateIgChrome(stats, tabsMeta) {
      const inv = igInventory();
      const setTxt = (id, v) => { const el = document.getElementById(id); if (el) el.textContent = v; };
      const show = (id, on) => { const el = document.getElementById(id); if (el) el.style.display = on ? '' : 'none'; };

      setTxt('igStatTabular', 'Tabular ' + inv.tabular.length + (inv.tabular.length ? ' OK' : ''));
      setTxt('igStatDocs', 'Documents ' + inv.documents.length + (inv.documents.length ? ' OK' : ''));
      setTxt('igStatImages', 'Images ' + inv.images.length + (inv.images.length ? ' OK' : ''));
      setTxt('igStatAudio', 'Audio ' + inv.audio.length + (inv.audio.length ? ' OK' : ''));
      show('igStatImages', inv.images.length > 0);
      show('igStatAudio', inv.audio.length > 0);

      const nodeCount = (igGraphCache.nodes || []).length;
      const alertCount = (stats && stats.alerts) || 0;
      setTxt('igStatNodes', 'Nodes ' + nodeCount);
      setTxt('igStatAlerts', ((tabsMeta && tabsMeta.alert_label) || 'Alerts') + ' ' + alertCount);

      const title = document.getElementById('igPageTitle');
      if (title) {
        const src = stats ? stats.sources : (inv.tabular.length + inv.documents.length + inv.images.length + inv.audio.length);
        title.textContent = 'Knowledge Graph - All ' + src + ' Source' + (src === 1 ? '' : 's') + ' Visualized';
      }
      const line = document.getElementById('igUseCaseLine');
      if (line && tabsMeta) {
        const conf = tabsMeta.confidence != null ? (' | confidence ' + (Number(tabsMeta.confidence) * 100).toFixed(0) + '%') : '';
        const src = tabsMeta.source === 'llm' ? 'LLM' : (tabsMeta.source || 'rules');
        line.innerHTML = '<b>' + String(tabsMeta.industry || 'General').replace(/</g, '&lt;') + '</b> - ' + String(tabsMeta.use_case || '').replace(/</g, '&lt;') + ' <span style="opacity:.75">(' + src + conf + ')</span>';
      }

      setTxt('igSumTabular', String(stats ? stats.tabular : 0));
      setTxt('igSumDocs', String(stats ? stats.documents : 0));
      setTxt('igSumImages', String(stats ? stats.images : 0));
      setTxt('igSumAudio', String(stats ? stats.audio : 0));
      setTxt('igSumCross', String(stats ? stats.cross : 0));
      setTxt('igSumPattern', String(stats ? stats.pattern : 0));

      const sub = document.getElementById('igPageSub');
      if (sub) {
        const bits = [];
        if (inv.tabular.length) bits.push('tabular = solid circles');
        if (inv.documents.length) bits.push('documents = dashed border');
        if (inv.images.length) bits.push('images = dashed border');
        if (inv.audio.length) bits.push('audio = dashed border');
        bits.push('cross-source edges = teal dashed');
        sub.textContent = bits.join(' | ') + '. Drag, zoom, and click any node to inspect.';
      }
    }

    function buildLocalIgTabsMeta() {
      const inv = igInventory();
      const names = (inv.tabular.concat(inv.documents, inv.images, inv.audio).join(' ') + ' ' + (window.graphenUseCaseHint || '')).toLowerCase();
      let industry = 'General';
      let useCase = 'Multi-source knowledge graph';
      let alertLabel = 'Alerts';
      let patternTabs = [{ id: 'risk', label: 'Risk Cluster', filter: 'pattern:alerts', emphasis: true, icon: 'warning' }];
      let legend = [
        { key: 'Entity', color: '#4C8DFF', dashed: false },
        { key: 'Evidence', color: '#EAB308', dashed: true },
      ];

      if (/health|patient|clinical|hipaa|claim|pharma|hospital/.test(names)) {
        industry = 'Healthcare';
        useCase = 'Healthcare claims & care-network intelligence';
        alertLabel = 'PHI / referral flags';
        patternTabs = [
          { id: 'referral_ring', label: 'Referral Ring', filter: 'pattern:ring', emphasis: true, icon: 'warning' },
          { id: 'phi_risk', label: 'PHI Exposure', filter: 'pattern:alerts', emphasis: true, icon: 'warning' },
        ];
      } else if (/aml|sanction|pmla|kyc|ofac|transaction|account|hdfc|rbi|ds[1-8]/.test(names) || inv.usingDemo) {
        industry = 'Financial Crime / AML';
        useCase = 'AML investigation knowledge graph';
        alertLabel = 'AML alerts';
        patternTabs = [
          { id: 'aml_ring', label: 'AML Ring', filter: 'pattern:ring', emphasis: true, icon: 'warning' },
          { id: 'sanctions', label: 'Sanctions Path', filter: 'pattern:sanctions', emphasis: true, icon: 'warning' },
        ];
        legend = [
          { key: 'Individual', color: '#4C8DFF', dashed: false },
          { key: 'Company', color: '#F5A623', dashed: false },
          { key: 'Account', color: '#27D199', dashed: false },
          { key: 'Sanctioned', color: '#FB5A6A', dashed: false },
          { key: 'Regulation (doc)', color: '#EAB308', dashed: true },
          { key: 'Policy (doc)', color: '#2DD4D4', dashed: true },
        ];
      } else if (/lease|tenant|property|rent|cbre|portfolio/.test(names)) {
        industry = 'Real Estate / Lease';
        useCase = 'Lease & portfolio knowledge graph';
        alertLabel = 'Lease risk flags';
        patternTabs = [
          { id: 'concentration', label: 'Tenant Concentration', filter: 'pattern:alerts', emphasis: true, icon: 'warning' },
          { id: 'expiry', label: 'Expiry Cluster', filter: 'pattern:ring', emphasis: true, icon: 'warning' },
        ];
      }

      const configuredDomain = window.graphenDomain;
      if (configuredDomain) {
        industry = configuredDomain.industry || industry;
        useCase = configuredDomain.use_case || useCase;
        alertLabel = (configuredDomain.use_case || 'Configured') + ' signals';
        const focus = configuredDomain.preview && configuredDomain.preview.detection_focus;
        if (Array.isArray(focus) && focus.length) {
          patternTabs = focus.slice(0, 3).map((label, index) => ({
            id: 'configured_' + index,
            label: String(label).replace(/\b\w/g, ch => ch.toUpperCase()).slice(0, 42),
            filter: index === 0 ? 'pattern:ring' : 'pattern:alerts',
            emphasis: true,
            icon: 'warning',
          }));
        }
        const entities = configuredDomain.preview && configuredDomain.preview.primary_entities;
        if (Array.isArray(entities) && entities.length) {
          const colors = ['#4C8DFF', '#F5A623', '#27D199', '#9B7CF6', '#FB5A6A'];
          legend = entities.slice(0, 5).map((label, index) => ({
            key: label, color: colors[index % colors.length], dashed: false,
          }));
          legend.push({ key: 'Evidence', color: '#EAB308', dashed: true });
        }
      }

      const tabs = [{ id: 'all', label: 'All', filter: 'all', emphasis: false }];
      if (inv.tabular.length) tabs.push({ id: 'tabular', label: 'Tabular (' + inv.tabular.length + ')', filter: 'modality:tabular', emphasis: false });
      if (inv.documents.length) tabs.push({ id: 'documents', label: 'Documents (' + inv.documents.length + ')', filter: 'modality:document', emphasis: false });
      if (inv.images.length) tabs.push({ id: 'images', label: 'Images (' + inv.images.length + ')', filter: 'modality:image', emphasis: false });
      if (inv.audio.length) tabs.push({ id: 'audio', label: 'Audio (' + inv.audio.length + ')', filter: 'modality:audio', emphasis: false });
      if ([inv.tabular.length, inv.documents.length, inv.images.length, inv.audio.length].filter(Boolean).length >= 2) {
        tabs.push({ id: 'cross', label: 'Cross-Source', filter: 'cross_source', emphasis: false });
      }
      patternTabs.forEach(t => tabs.push(t));

      return {
        industry,
        use_case: useCase,
        source: configuredDomain ? 'domain_configurator' : (inv.usingDemo ? 'demo_local' : 'local'),
        confidence: configuredDomain ? 1 : 0.65,
        alert_label: alertLabel,
        tabs,
        legend,
        demo: !!inv.usingDemo,
        _invSig: JSON.stringify(inv),
      };
    }

    function paintInteractiveGraph(tabsMeta) {
      try {
        if (!tabsMeta) tabsMeta = buildLocalIgTabsMeta();
        igTabsMeta = tabsMeta;
        window.igTabsMeta = tabsMeta;
        const filters = (igTabsMeta.tabs || []).map(t => t.filter);
        if (!filters.includes(igActiveFilter)) igActiveFilter = 'all';

        const built = buildInteractiveGraphData(igTabsMeta);
        // Guarantee at least a few nodes so the canvas is never blank
        if (!built.nodes || built.nodes.length < 2) {
          built.nodes = [
            { id: 'n0', label: 'Entity A', abbrev: 'ENT', type: 'Individual', modality: 'tabular', dashed: false, inRing: true, alert: false, data: { source_file: 'session' } },
            { id: 'n1', label: 'Entity B', abbrev: 'ENT', type: 'Company', modality: 'tabular', dashed: false, inRing: true, alert: false, data: { source_file: 'session' } },
            { id: 'n2', label: 'Evidence', abbrev: 'DOC', type: 'Document', modality: 'document', dashed: true, inRing: false, alert: false, data: { source_file: 'session' } },
          ];
          built.links = [
            { source: 'n0', target: 'n1', label: 'RELATED_TO', cross: false, ring: true, kind: 'pattern' },
            { source: 'n0', target: 'n2', label: 'EVIDENCED_BY', cross: true, ring: false, kind: 'cross_source' },
          ];
          built.stats = { tabular: 2, documents: 1, images: 0, audio: 0, cross: 1, pattern: 2, alerts: 1, sources: 3, usingDemo: true };
        }
        igGraphCache = { nodes: built.nodes, links: built.links, stats: built.stats };
        window.igGraphCache = igGraphCache;
        updateSidebarLiveStats();
        try { renderIgFilterBar(igTabsMeta.tabs); } catch (e) { console.warn(e); }
        try { renderIgLegend(igTabsMeta.legend); } catch (e) { console.warn(e); }
        try { updateIgChrome(built.stats, igTabsMeta); } catch (e) { console.warn(e); }
        try { initFullGraph(); } catch (err) { console.warn('initFullGraph failed', err); }
        try { if (typeof refreshRelationshipTable === 'function') refreshRelationshipTable(); } catch (e) { console.warn(e); }
        const meta = document.getElementById('igFilterMeta');
        if (meta) meta.textContent = built.nodes.length + ' nodes - ' + built.links.length + ' edges';
        const line = document.getElementById('igUseCaseLine');
        if (line && igTabsMeta) {
          const conf = igTabsMeta.confidence != null ? (' | confidence ' + (Number(igTabsMeta.confidence) * 100).toFixed(0) + '%') : '';
          const src = igTabsMeta.source === 'llm' ? 'LLM' : (igTabsMeta.source || 'local');
          line.innerHTML = '<b>' + String(igTabsMeta.industry || 'General').replace(/</g, '&lt;') + '</b> - ' + String(igTabsMeta.use_case || '').replace(/</g, '&lt;') + ' <span style="opacity:.75">(' + src + conf + ')</span>';
        }
        return built;
      } catch (err) {
        console.error('paintInteractiveGraph failed', err);
        const line = document.getElementById('igUseCaseLine');
        if (line) line.textContent = 'Graph paint error — click Refresh tabs. ' + (err && err.message ? err.message : '');
        return null;
      }
    }

    async function fetchIgTabs(timeoutMs) {
      const inv = igInventory();
      const configured = window.graphenDomain || {};
      const payload = {
        tabular_files: inv.tabular,
        document_files: inv.documents.filter(n => !/\.(txt|md)$/i.test(n)),
        text_files: inv.documents.filter(n => /\.(txt|md)$/i.test(n)).concat(inv.textFiles || []),
        image_files: inv.images,
        audio_files: inv.audio,
        hint: window.graphenUseCaseHint || (inv.usingDemo ? 'demo session' : (window.currentTrackingId ? ('tracking ' + window.currentTrackingId) : '')),
        industry: configured.industry || '',
        use_case: configured.use_case || '',
      };
      const ctrl = (typeof AbortController !== 'undefined') ? new AbortController() : null;
      const timer = setTimeout(() => { if (ctrl) ctrl.abort(); }, timeoutMs || 8000);
      try {
        const res = await fetch('/api/graph/tabs', {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
          body: JSON.stringify(payload),
          signal: ctrl ? ctrl.signal : undefined,
        });
        if (!res.ok) throw new Error('tabs HTTP ' + res.status);
        const data = await res.json();
        data._invSig = JSON.stringify(inv);
        return data;
      } catch (err) {
        console.warn('fetchIgTabs failed', err);
        return null;
      } finally {
        clearTimeout(timer);
      }
    }

    let igRefreshGen = 0;
    async function refreshInteractiveGraph(forceTabs) {
      try {
        // Always paint first — never block the UI on LLM
        paintInteractiveGraph(buildLocalIgTabsMeta());
      } catch (e) {
        console.error('local graph paint failed', e);
      }

      const gen = ++igRefreshGen;
      igTabsLoading = true;
      try {
        const remote = await fetchIgTabs(6000);
        if (gen !== igRefreshGen) return;
        if (remote && remote.tabs && remote.tabs.length) {
          paintInteractiveGraph(remote);
        }
      } catch (e) {
        console.warn('LLM tab refine skipped', e);
      } finally {
        if (gen === igRefreshGen) igTabsLoading = false;
      }
    }

    // Expose for inline handlers / console debugging
    window.paintInteractiveGraph = paintInteractiveGraph;
    window.buildLocalIgTabsMeta = buildLocalIgTabsMeta;
    window.refreshInteractiveGraph = refreshInteractiveGraph;
    window.goToInteractiveGraph = typeof goToInteractiveGraph === 'function' ? goToInteractiveGraph : function () { nav('graph'); };

    /* ============================================================
       CYPHER DETECTION — dynamic scenarios + step-through playback
       ============================================================ */
    let cyphPayload = null;
    let cyphActiveDet = null;
    let cyphStepIdx = 0;
    let cyphPlaying = false;
    let cyphPlayTimer = null;
    let cyphPlayMs = 1200;
    let cyphSim = null;
    let cyphConsoleLines = [];
    let cyphFlagWrites = {};
    let cyphCompletedDets = new Set();
    let cyphDetectionResults = {};
    let cyphRunAllActive = false;
    let cyphRunResolve = null;

    function cyphInventoryPayload() {
      const inv = (typeof igInventory === 'function') ? igInventory() : { tabular: [], documents: [], images: [], audio: [], textFiles: [], usingDemo: true };
      const meta = window.igTabsMeta || (typeof igTabsMeta !== 'undefined' ? igTabsMeta : null) || {};
      const configured = window.graphenDomain || {};
      return {
        tabular_files: inv.tabular.map(f => (typeof f === 'string' ? f : (f.name || f.filename || ''))).filter(Boolean),
        document_files: inv.documents.filter(n => !/\.(txt|md|rtf)$/i.test(n)).map(f => (typeof f === 'string' ? f : (f.name || ''))),
        text_files: inv.documents.filter(n => /\.(txt|md|rtf)$/i.test(n)),
        image_files: inv.images.map(f => (typeof f === 'string' ? f : (f.name || ''))),
        audio_files: inv.audio.map(f => (typeof f === 'string' ? f : (f.name || ''))),
        hint: window.graphenUseCaseHint || (inv.usingDemo ? 'demo session' : (window.currentTrackingId ? ('tracking ' + window.currentTrackingId) : '')),
        tracking_id: window.currentTrackingId || null,
        industry: configured.industry || meta.industry || '',
        use_case: configured.use_case || meta.use_case || '',
        primary_entities: ((configured.preview || {}).primary_entities || []),
        key_relationships: ((configured.preview || {}).key_relationships || []),
      };
    }

    function cyphEsc(s) {
      return String(s == null ? '' : s)
        .replace(/&/g, '&amp;')
        .replace(/</g, '&lt;')
        .replace(/>/g, '&gt;')
        .replace(/"/g, '&quot;')
        .replace(/'/g, '&#39;');
    }

    function cyphDatasetKey(ds) { return ds.id || ds.filename || ''; }

    function cyphParseFlagValue(msg) {
      const s = String(msg || '');
      const m = s.match(/=\s*'([^']+)'/);
      if (m) return m[1];
      const m2 = s.match(/=\s*"([^"]+)"/);
      if (m2) return m2[1];
      return 'FLAGGED';
    }

    function cyphParseFlagColumn(msg) {
      const m = String(msg || '').match(/([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\s*=/);
      return m ? m[1] : null;
    }

    function cyphGetFlagWrite(ds) {
      return cyphFlagWrites[cyphDatasetKey(ds)] || null;
    }

    function cyphUpdateBanner() {
      const banner = document.getElementById('cyphBanner');
      if (!banner) return;
      const n = Object.keys(cyphFlagWrites).length;
      if (!n) {
        banner.textContent = (cyphPayload && cyphPayload.banner)
          ? cyphPayload.banner
          : 'Zero flags. Zero risk scores. SQL has nothing to query. GRAPHEN will now detect from the raw structure.';
        banner.classList.remove('has-flags');
      } else {
        banner.textContent = n + ' source(s) have now contributed evidence or GRAPHEN-written flags. Results are available to downstream risk intelligence.';
        banner.classList.add('has-flags');
      }
    }

    function cyphMarkFlagsWritten(det, step) {
      if (!det || !step || !step.flags_written || !cyphPayload) return;
      const detId = det.id;
      const flagVal = det.written_flag_value || cyphParseFlagValue(step.flags_message);
      const targetIds = det.target_dataset_ids || [];
      (cyphPayload.raw_datasets || []).forEach(ds => {
        const key = cyphDatasetKey(ds);
        const linked = targetIds.length
          ? targetIds.includes(ds.id)
          : (ds.detection_ids || []).includes(detId);
        if (!linked) return;
        const isStructured = (ds.modality || 'structured') === 'structured';
        const flagCol = isStructured
          ? (ds.flag_column || cyphParseFlagColumn(step.flags_message) || 'risk_flag')
          : 'evidence';
        cyphFlagWrites[key] = {
          written: true,
          flag_column: flagCol,
          value: isStructured ? flagVal : 'USED',
          detection_id: detId,
          evidence_only: !isStructured,
        };
      });
      cyphCompletedDets.add(detId);
      updateSidebarLiveStats();
      renderCyphRawTables(cyphPayload.raw_datasets);
      renderCyphScenarios(cyphPayload.detections);
      cyphUpdateBanner();
    }

    function renderCyphRawTables(datasets) {
      const grid = document.getElementById('cyphRawGrid');
      const sub = document.getElementById('cyphRawSubtitle');
      if (!grid) return;
      const list = datasets && datasets.length ? datasets : [];
      if (sub && cyphPayload && cyphPayload.raw_datasets_subtitle) {
        sub.textContent = cyphPayload.raw_datasets_subtitle;
      } else if (sub) {
        sub.textContent = list.length
          ? ('Showing ' + list.length + ' prominent structured and unstructured source(s).')
          : 'No prominent sources for the current use case.';
      }
      if (!list.length) {
        grid.innerHTML = '<div class="cyph-loading">No sources are available for the active detection plan.</div>';
        return;
      }
      grid.innerHTML = list.map(ds => {
        const write = cyphGetFlagWrite(ds);
        const modality = ds.modality || 'structured';
        if (modality !== 'structured') {
          const badge = write && write.evidence_only ? 'EVIDENCE USED' : modality.toUpperCase();
          const role = ds.cypher_role ? '<div class="cyph-raw-role">' + cyphEsc(ds.cypher_role) + '</div>' : '';
          return '<div class="cyph-raw-card unstructured"><div class="cyph-raw-card-head"><span>' +
            cyphEsc(ds.title || ds.filename) + '</span><span class="cyph-raw-badge cyph-source-modality">' +
            cyphEsc(badge) + '</span></div>' + role + '<div class="cyph-source-excerpt">' +
            cyphEsc(ds.excerpt || ('Evidence source: ' + ds.filename)) + '</div></div>';
        }
        const flagCol = write ? write.flag_column : (ds.flag_column || 'flag');
        let cols = (ds.columns || []).slice(0, 8);
        if (write && !cols.some(c => String(c).toLowerCase() === String(flagCol).toLowerCase())) {
          cols = cols.concat([flagCol]).slice(0, 8);
        }
        const rows = (ds.rows || []).slice(0, 5).map(r => {
          const row = (r || []).slice();
          while (row.length < cols.length) row.push('-');
          if (write) {
            const fidx = cols.findIndex(c => String(c).toLowerCase() === String(flagCol).toLowerCase());
            if (fidx >= 0) row[fidx] = write.value;
          }
          return row;
        });
        const badgeText = write
          ? (flagCol + ' : WRITTEN')
          : (ds.flag_status || (flagCol + ' : NOT WRITTEN'));
        const badgeCls = 'cyph-raw-badge ' + (write ? 'written' : 'pending');
        const head = cols.map(c => '<th>' + cyphEsc(c) + '</th>').join('');
        const body = rows.map(r => '<tr>' + cols.map((_, i) => '<td>' + cyphEsc((r[i] == null || r[i] === '') ? '-' : r[i]) + '</td>').join('') + '</tr>').join('');
        const role = ds.cypher_role ? '<div class="cyph-raw-role">' + cyphEsc(ds.cypher_role) + '</div>' : '';
        return '<div class="cyph-raw-card"><div class="cyph-raw-card-head"><span>' + cyphEsc(ds.title || ds.filename) + '</span><span class="' + badgeCls + '">' + cyphEsc(badgeText) + '</span></div>' + role + '<div class="cyph-raw-table-wrap"><table class="cyph-raw-table"><thead><tr>' + head + '</tr></thead><tbody>' + body + '</tbody></table></div></div>';
      }).join('');
    }

    function renderCyphScenarios(detections) {
      const el = document.getElementById('cyphScenarios');
      if (!el) return;
      const list = detections || [];
      if (!list.length) {
        el.innerHTML = '<div class="cyph-loading">No detection scenarios generated for this session.</div>';
        return;
      }
      el.innerHTML = list.map(d => {
        const active = cyphActiveDet && cyphActiveDet.id === d.id ? ' active' : '';
        const done = cyphCompletedDets.has(d.id) ? ' done' : '';
        const theme = d.theme ? (' theme-' + d.theme) : '';
        const tags = (d.tags || []).map(t => '<span class="cyph-tag">' + cyphEsc(t) + '</span>').join('');
        const safeId = String(d.id).replace(/'/g, "\\'");
        const displayTitle = String(d.title || 'Detection').replace(/^Detection\s+\d+\s*[-—]\s*/i, '');
        const state = cyphCompletedDets.has(d.id)
          ? 'COMPLETE'
          : (cyphPlaying && cyphActiveDet && cyphActiveDet.id === d.id ? 'RUNNING' : 'READY');
        return '<div class="cyph-scenario' + theme + active + done + '" data-id="' + cyphEsc(d.id) + '">' +
          '<div class="cyph-scenario-select" onclick="selectCypherDetection(\'' + safeId + '\')">' +
          '<div class="cyph-scenario-num">Detection ' + cyphEsc(d.index || '') + '</div>' +
          '<div class="cyph-scenario-title">' + cyphEsc(displayTitle) + '</div>' +
          '<div class="cyph-scenario-snippet">' + cyphEsc(d.cypher_snippet || '') + '</div>' +
          '<div class="cyph-scenario-tags">' + tags + '</div></div>' +
          '<div class="cyph-scenario-actions"><span class="cyph-scenario-state">' + state + '</span>' +
          '<button type="button" class="cyph-scenario-run" ' +
          (cyphPlaying || cyphRunAllActive ? 'disabled ' : '') +
          'onclick="runCypherDetection(\'' + safeId + '\')">▶ Run</button></div></div>';
      }).join('');
    }

    function renderCyphRelationshipPath(det) {
      const body = document.getElementById('cyphPathRows');
      const meta = document.getElementById('cyphPathMeta');
      if (!body) return;
      const rows = det && Array.isArray(det.significant_paths) ? det.significant_paths : [];
      if (meta) meta.textContent = rows.length
        ? ('Path rank #1 · ' + rows.length + ' relationship(s)')
        : 'No path selected';
      body.innerHTML = rows.length ? rows.map(row =>
        '<tr><td>' + cyphEsc(row.sequence || '-') + '</td>' +
        '<td>' + cyphEsc(row.source) + ' <span style="opacity:.55">(' + cyphEsc(row.source_type) + ')</span></td>' +
        '<td class="rel">' + cyphEsc(row.relationship) + '</td>' +
        '<td>' + cyphEsc(row.target) + ' <span style="opacity:.55">(' + cyphEsc(row.target_type) + ')</span></td>' +
        '<td>' + cyphEsc(row.hops) + '</td><td class="score">' + cyphEsc(row.significance_score) + '</td>' +
        '<td>' + cyphEsc(row.evidence_source) + '</td><td>' + cyphEsc(row.flag_result) + '</td></tr>'
      ).join('') : '<tr><td colspan="8">Select a detection to inspect its most significant path.</td></tr>';
    }

    function renderCyphExecutionResult(det, status) {
      const statusEl = document.getElementById('cyphRunStatus');
      const grid = document.getElementById('cyphResultGrid');
      if (!statusEl || !grid) return;
      const state = status || (det && cyphCompletedDets.has(det.id) ? 'complete' : 'ready');
      statusEl.className = 'cyph-run-status' + (state === 'running' ? ' running' : '') + (state === 'complete' ? ' complete' : '');
      statusEl.textContent = !det
        ? 'READY · Select Run on a detection scenario'
        : (state === 'running'
          ? 'RUNNING · ' + det.title
          : (state === 'complete' ? 'COMPLETE · ' + det.title : 'READY · ' + det.title));
      const summary = (det && det.result_summary) || {};
      const result = det ? (cyphDetectionResults[det.id] || {}) : {};
      const metrics = [
        ['Nodes', summary.nodes_evaluated || 0],
        ['Relationships', summary.relationships_traversed || 0],
        ['Path hops', summary.significant_path_hops || 0],
        ['Target sources', summary.target_sources || (det ? (det.target_dataset_ids || []).length : 0)],
        ['Current step', det ? ((cyphStepIdx + 1) + '/' + ((det.steps || []).length || 0)) : '0/0'],
        ['Flags', result.flags || (det && cyphCompletedDets.has(det.id) ? 'WRITTEN' : 'PENDING')],
      ];
      grid.innerHTML = metrics.map(([key, value]) =>
        '<div class="cyph-result-metric"><div class="k">' + cyphEsc(key) +
        '</div><div class="v">' + cyphEsc(value) + '</div></div>'
      ).join('');
    }

    function cyphFinishDetection() {
      if (!cyphActiveDet) return;
      cyphDetectionResults[cyphActiveDet.id] = {
        status: 'complete',
        flags: 'WRITTEN',
        completedAt: Date.now(),
      };
      cyphStopPlay();
      renderCyphExecutionResult(cyphActiveDet, 'complete');
      renderCyphRelationshipPath(cyphActiveDet);
      renderCyphScenarios(cyphPayload ? cyphPayload.detections : []);
      const resolve = cyphRunResolve;
      cyphRunResolve = null;
      if (resolve) resolve(cyphActiveDet.id);
    }

    function cyphAutoRunDetection() {
      if (!cyphActiveDet || cyphPlaying) return Promise.resolve();
      const steps = cyphActiveDet.steps || [];
      if (!steps.length) return Promise.resolve();
      cyphPlaying = true;
      const btn = document.getElementById('cyphPlayBtn');
      if (btn) btn.textContent = '⏸ Pause';
      cyphUpdateSpeed();
      const ms = Math.min(cyphPlayMs, 850);
      renderCyphExecutionResult(cyphActiveDet, 'running');
      renderCyphScenarios(cyphPayload ? cyphPayload.detections : []);
      const completion = new Promise(resolve => { cyphRunResolve = resolve; });
      cyphPlayTimer = setInterval(() => {
        if (cyphStepIdx >= steps.length - 1) {
          paintCyphStep(true);
          cyphFinishDetection();
          return;
        }
        cyphStepIdx++;
        paintCyphStep(true);
        renderCyphExecutionResult(cyphActiveDet, 'running');
        if (cyphStepIdx >= steps.length - 1) cyphFinishDetection();
      }, ms);
      return completion;
    }

    function selectCypherDetection(id) {
      if (!cyphPayload || !cyphPayload.detections) return;
      if (cyphPlaying) return;
      cyphStopPlay();
      cyphActiveDet = cyphPayload.detections.find(d => d.id === id) || cyphPayload.detections[0];
      cyphStepIdx = 0;
      cyphConsoleLines = [];
      const ws = document.getElementById('cyphWorkspace');
      if (ws) ws.style.display = '';
      renderCyphScenarios(cyphPayload.detections);
      if (cyphCompletedDets.has(id)) {
        cyphStepIdx = Math.max(0, (cyphActiveDet.steps || []).length - 1);
        paintCyphStep(false);
      } else {
        paintCyphStep(false);
      }
      renderCyphRelationshipPath(cyphActiveDet);
      renderCyphExecutionResult(cyphActiveDet);
    }

    async function runCypherDetection(id) {
      if (cyphPlaying) return;
      selectCypherDetection(id);
      cyphStepIdx = 0;
      cyphConsoleLines = [];
      cyphCompletedDets.delete(id);
      delete cyphDetectionResults[id];
      paintCyphStep(false);
      return cyphAutoRunDetection();
    }

    async function cyphRunAllDetections() {
      if (!cyphPayload || cyphPlaying || cyphRunAllActive) return;
      cyphRunAllActive = true;
      cyphFlagWrites = {};
      cyphCompletedDets = new Set();
      cyphDetectionResults = {};
      const allButton = document.getElementById('cyphRunAllBtn');
      if (allButton) { allButton.disabled = true; allButton.textContent = 'Running detections…'; }
      renderCyphRawTables(cyphPayload.raw_datasets);
      renderCyphScenarios(cyphPayload.detections);
      for (const det of cyphPayload.detections) {
        await runCypherDetection(det.id);
      }
      cyphRunAllActive = false;
      if (allButton) { allButton.disabled = false; allButton.textContent = '▶ Run All Detections'; }
      renderCyphScenarios(cyphPayload.detections);
      cyphUpdateBanner();
    }

    function cyphUpdateSpeed() {
      const sl = document.getElementById('cyphSpeed');
      const v = sl ? Number(sl.value) : 5;
      cyphPlayMs = Math.max(400, 2200 - v * 180);
    }

    function cyphStopPlay() {
      cyphPlaying = false;
      if (cyphPlayTimer) { clearInterval(cyphPlayTimer); cyphPlayTimer = null; }
      const btn = document.getElementById('cyphPlayBtn');
      if (btn) btn.textContent = '▶ Play';
    }

    function cyphTogglePlay() {
      if (!cyphActiveDet) return;
      if (cyphRunAllActive) return;
      if (cyphPlaying) { cyphStopPlay(); return; }
      cyphPlaying = true;
      const btn = document.getElementById('cyphPlayBtn');
      if (btn) btn.textContent = '⏸ Pause';
      cyphUpdateSpeed();
      cyphPlayTimer = setInterval(() => {
        const steps = cyphActiveDet.steps || [];
        if (cyphStepIdx >= steps.length - 1) {
          paintCyphStep(true);
          cyphFinishDetection();
          return;
        }
        cyphStepIdx++;
        paintCyphStep(true);
        renderCyphExecutionResult(cyphActiveDet, 'running');
        if (cyphStepIdx >= steps.length - 1) cyphFinishDetection();
      }, cyphPlayMs);
    }

    function cyphStepForward() {
      if (!cyphActiveDet) return;
      const steps = cyphActiveDet.steps || [];
      if (cyphStepIdx < steps.length - 1) {
        cyphStepIdx++;
        paintCyphStep(true);
        if (cyphStepIdx >= steps.length - 1) cyphFinishDetection();
      }
    }

    function cyphStepBack() {
      if (!cyphActiveDet) return;
      if (cyphStepIdx > 0) { cyphStepIdx--; paintCyphStep(false); }
    }

    function cyphRestart() {
      if (!cyphActiveDet || cyphRunAllActive) return;
      cyphStopPlay();
      cyphStepIdx = 0;
      cyphConsoleLines = [];
      paintCyphStep(false);
    }

    function paintCyphStep(stream) {
      if (!cyphActiveDet) return;
      const steps = cyphActiveDet.steps || [];
      const step = steps[cyphStepIdx] || steps[0];
      if (!step) return;

      const hopMeta = document.getElementById('cyphHopMeta');
      const stepMeta = document.getElementById('cyphStepMeta');
      if (hopMeta) hopMeta.textContent = 'Hop ' + (step.hop || 0) + '/' + (step.hop_total || 0);
      if (stepMeta) stepMeta.textContent = 'Step ' + (step.step || 0) + '/' + (step.step_total || 0);

      const narr = document.getElementById('cyphNarrative');
      if (narr) narr.textContent = step.narrative || '';

      const flags = document.getElementById('cyphFlagsBox');
      if (flags) {
        if (step.flags_written && step.flags_message) {
          flags.textContent = 'FLAGS WRITTEN — ' + step.flags_message;
          flags.classList.add('visible');
          cyphMarkFlagsWritten(cyphActiveDet, step);
        } else {
          flags.classList.remove('visible');
        }
      }

      const cypherEl = document.getElementById('cyphCypherLines');
      const lines = cyphActiveDet.cypher_lines || [];
      const through = step.cypher_line_through || 0;
      if (cypherEl) {
        cypherEl.innerHTML = lines.map((ln, i) => {
          const done = i < through;
          const active = i === through - 1;
          const cls = 'cyph-cypher-line' + (done ? ' done' : '') + (active ? ' active' : '');
          return '<div class="' + cls + '"><span class="chk">' + (done ? '✓' : '') + '</span><span>' + cyphEsc(ln) + '</span></div>';
        }).join('');
      }

      const bindEl = document.getElementById('cyphBindings');
      if (bindEl && step.bindings) {
        bindEl.innerHTML = Object.entries(step.bindings).map(([k, v]) => {
          const val = Array.isArray(v) ? v.join(', ') : String(v);
          return '<div class="cyph-bind-row"><span class="k">' + cyphEsc(k) + '</span><span class="v">' + cyphEsc(val) + '</span></div>';
        }).join('');
      }

      const popup = document.getElementById('cyphPopup');
      if (popup && step.popup) {
        popup.innerHTML = '[' + cyphEsc(step.popup.from) + '] — <b>' + cyphEsc(step.popup.rel) + '</b> → [' + cyphEsc(step.popup.to) + ']';
        popup.classList.add('visible');
      } else if (popup) popup.classList.remove('visible');

      (step.console_lines || []).forEach(ln => {
        if (!cyphConsoleLines.includes(ln)) cyphConsoleLines.push(ln);
      });
      const con = document.getElementById('cyphConsole');
      if (con) {
        const ts = new Date().toTimeString().slice(0, 8);
        con.innerHTML = cyphConsoleLines.map((ln, i) => {
          const fresh = stream && i === cyphConsoleLines.length - 1;
          return '<div class="' + (fresh ? 'line-new' : '') + '">' + ts + ' ' + cyphEsc(ln) + '</div>';
        }).join('');
        con.scrollTop = con.scrollHeight;
      }

      initCyphGraph(step);
    }

    function initCyphGraph(step) {
      const svgEl = document.getElementById('cyphGraphSvg');
      if (!svgEl || typeof d3 === 'undefined' || !cyphActiveDet) return;
      const g = cyphActiveDet.graph || {};
      let nodes = (g.nodes || []).map(n => Object.assign({}, n));
      let links = (g.links || []).map(l => Object.assign({}, l));
      const hiN = new Set(step.highlight_nodes || []);
      const hiE = new Set(step.highlight_edges || []);

      svgEl.innerHTML = '';
      const wrap = svgEl.parentElement;
      let W = (wrap && wrap.clientWidth) || 700;
      let H = (wrap && wrap.clientHeight) || 360;
      if (W < 100) W = 700;
      if (H < 100) H = 360;
      const svg = d3.select('#cyphGraphSvg').attr('viewBox', [0, 0, W, H]);
      const root = svg.append('g');
      svg.call(d3.zoom().scaleExtent([0.4, 2.5]).on('zoom', e => root.attr('transform', e.transform)));

      const defs = svg.append('defs');
      defs.append('marker').attr('id', 'cyphArr').attr('viewBox', '0 -4 8 8')
        .attr('refX', 20).attr('refY', 0).attr('markerWidth', 6).attr('markerHeight', 6).attr('orient', 'auto')
        .append('path').attr('d', 'M0,-4L8,0L0,4').attr('fill', '#2DD4D4');

      cyphSim = d3.forceSimulation(nodes)
        .force('link', d3.forceLink(links).id(d => d.id).distance(95).strength(0.6))
        .force('charge', d3.forceManyBody().strength(-320))
        .force('center', d3.forceCenter(W / 2, H / 2))
        .force('collide', d3.forceCollide(26));

      const link = root.append('g').selectAll('line').data(links).join('line')
        .attr('stroke', d => hiE.has(d.id) ? '#2DD4D4' : '#243056')
        .attr('stroke-width', d => hiE.has(d.id) ? 2.4 : 1.2)
        .attr('marker-end', d => hiE.has(d.id) ? 'url(#cyphArr)' : null)
        .attr('opacity', d => hiE.has(d.id) ? 1 : 0.45);

      const node = root.append('g').selectAll('g').data(nodes).join('g')
        .call(d3.drag()
          .on('start', (e, d) => { if (!e.active) cyphSim.alphaTarget(0.2).restart(); d.fx = d.x; d.fy = d.y; })
          .on('drag', (e, d) => { d.fx = e.x; d.fy = e.y; })
          .on('end', (e, d) => { if (!e.active) cyphSim.alphaTarget(0); d.fx = null; d.fy = null; }));

      node.append('circle')
        .attr('r', d => hiN.has(d.id) ? 18 : 14)
        .attr('fill', d => d.color || '#4C8DFF')
        .attr('stroke', d => hiN.has(d.id) ? '#F5A623' : 'rgba(255,255,255,0.15)')
        .attr('stroke-width', d => hiN.has(d.id) ? 2.5 : 1.2)
        .attr('opacity', d => hiN.size && !hiN.has(d.id) ? 0.35 : 0.95);

      node.append('text')
        .text(d => (d.label || '').slice(0, 12))
        .attr('font-size', 9).attr('font-family', 'IBM Plex Mono').attr('fill', '#E2E8F0')
        .attr('text-anchor', 'middle').attr('dy', 28).style('pointer-events', 'none');

      cyphSim.on('tick', () => {
        link.attr('x1', d => d.source.x).attr('y1', d => d.source.y)
            .attr('x2', d => d.target.x).attr('y2', d => d.target.y);
        node.attr('transform', d => 'translate(' + d.x + ',' + d.y + ')');
      });
    }

    async function refreshCypherDetection() {
      const grid = document.getElementById('cyphRawGrid');
      const scen = document.getElementById('cyphScenarios');
      if (grid) grid.innerHTML = '<div class="cyph-loading">Building detection scenarios from your uploads…</div>';
      if (scen) scen.innerHTML = '';
      cyphStopPlay();
      cyphActiveDet = null;
      cyphStepIdx = 0;
      cyphFlagWrites = {};
      cyphCompletedDets = new Set();
      cyphDetectionResults = {};
      cyphRunAllActive = false;
      cyphRunResolve = null;
      const runAllButton = document.getElementById('cyphRunAllBtn');
      if (runAllButton) { runAllButton.disabled = false; runAllButton.textContent = '▶ Run All Detections'; }
      renderCyphRelationshipPath(null);
      renderCyphExecutionResult(null);

      const payload = cyphInventoryPayload();
      let data = null;

      const applyPayload = (d) => {
        if (!d || !d.detections) return;
        cyphPayload = d;
        const phase = document.getElementById('cyphPhaseLabel');
        if (phase && d.phase_label) phase.textContent = d.phase_label;
        const rawTitle = document.getElementById('cyphRawTitle');
        if (rawTitle && d.raw_section_title) rawTitle.textContent = d.raw_section_title;
        const rawSub = document.getElementById('cyphRawSubtitle');
        if (rawSub && d.raw_datasets_subtitle) rawSub.textContent = d.raw_datasets_subtitle;
        const banner = document.getElementById('cyphBanner');
        if (banner && d.banner) banner.textContent = d.banner;
        const pageTitle = document.getElementById('cyphPageTitle');
        if (pageTitle) pageTitle.textContent = (d.use_case || 'Use-Case') + ' · Cypher Detection Plan';
        const intro = document.getElementById('cyphIntro');
        if (intro && d.intro) intro.textContent = d.intro;
        const line = document.getElementById('cyphUseCaseLine');
        if (line) {
          const src = d.source === 'llm' ? 'LLM' : (d.source || 'rules');
          line.innerHTML = '<b>' + cyphEsc(d.industry || 'General') + '</b> - ' + cyphEsc(d.use_case || '') + ' <span style="opacity:.7">(' + src + ')</span>';
        }
        renderCyphRawTables(d.raw_datasets);
        renderCyphScenarios(d.detections);
        if (d.detections.length && (!cyphActiveDet || !d.detections.find(x => x.id === cyphActiveDet.id))) {
          selectCypherDetection(d.detections[0].id);
        } else if (cyphActiveDet) {
          paintCyphStep(false);
        }
      };

      try {
        const res = await fetch('/api/cypher/detections', {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
          body: JSON.stringify(Object.assign({}, payload, { skip_llm: true })),
        });
        if (res.ok) {
          data = await res.json();
          applyPayload(data);
        }
      } catch (e) { console.warn('cypher detections fast fetch', e); }

      if (!data || !data.detections) {
        if (grid) grid.innerHTML = '<div class="cyph-loading">Could not load scenarios - check API on port 8010.</div>';
        return;
      }

      // Refine tabs/scenarios with LLM in background (non-blocking)
      try {
        const res2 = await fetch('/api/cypher/detections', {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
          body: JSON.stringify(payload),
        });
        if (res2.ok) {
          const remote = await res2.json();
          if (
            remote && remote.detections && remote.detections.length
            && !cyphPlaying && !cyphRunAllActive && !cyphCompletedDets.size
          ) applyPayload(remote);
        }
      } catch (e) { console.warn('cypher LLM refine skipped', e); }
    }

    /* ============================================================
       CROSS-DOCUMENT DISCOVERY — requirement-specific LLM findings
       ============================================================ */
    let crossdocRefreshGen = 0;
    let crossdocPayload = null;

    function crossdocEsc(value) {
      return String(value == null ? '' : value)
        .replace(/&/g, '&amp;')
        .replace(/</g, '&lt;')
        .replace(/>/g, '&gt;')
        .replace(/"/g, '&quot;')
        .replace(/'/g, '&#39;');
    }

    function crossdocRequestPayload() {
      const base = (typeof cyphInventoryPayload === 'function')
        ? cyphInventoryPayload()
        : {
            tabular_files: [], document_files: [], image_files: [],
            audio_files: [], text_files: [], tracking_id: window.currentTrackingId || null,
            industry: '', use_case: ''
          };
      const config = window.graphenDomain || domainConfiguration || {};
      const preview = config.preview || {};
      const crossdoc = ((config.pillar_blueprint || {}).cross_doc_discovery) || {};
      return {
        tabular_files: base.tabular_files || [],
        document_files: base.document_files || [],
        image_files: base.image_files || [],
        audio_files: base.audio_files || [],
        text_files: base.text_files || [],
        tracking_id: base.tracking_id || window.currentTrackingId || null,
        industry: config.industry || base.industry || '',
        use_case: config.use_case || base.use_case || '',
        requirement: crossdoc.focus || config.objective ||
          base.use_case || window.graphenUseCaseHint || base.hint || '',
        objective: config.objective || '',
        primary_entities: preview.primary_entities || base.primary_entities || [],
        key_relationships: preview.key_relationships || base.key_relationships || [],
        detection_focus: preview.detection_focus || [],
        page_title: crossdoc.title || '',
        page_subtitle: crossdoc.subtitle || '',
        eyebrow: crossdoc.eyebrow || '',
      };
    }

    function toggleCrossDocFinding(index) {
      const card = document.getElementById('crossdocFinding' + index);
      if (card) card.classList.toggle('collapsed');
    }

    async function crossdocApiRequest(body) {
      const options = {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify(body),
      };
      try {
        const response = await fetch('/api/crossdoc/discover', options);
        if (response.status !== 404) return response;
      } catch (_) {}
      // Compatibility fallback while a stale local dev process still owns 8010.
      return fetch('http://127.0.0.1:8011/api/crossdoc/discover', options);
    }

    function renderCrossDocPayload(payload, refining) {
      if (!payload) return;
      crossdocPayload = payload;
      const phase = document.getElementById('crossdocPhase');
      const eyebrow = document.getElementById('crossdocEyebrow');
      const title = document.getElementById('crossdocTitle');
      const subtitle = document.getElementById('crossdocSubtitle');
      const industry = document.getElementById('crossdocIndustry');
      const sourceCount = document.getElementById('crossdocSourceCount');
      const engine = document.getElementById('crossdocEngine');
      const host = document.getElementById('crossdocFindings');

      if (phase && payload.phase_label) phase.textContent = payload.phase_label;
      if (eyebrow && payload.eyebrow) eyebrow.textContent = payload.eyebrow;
      if (title && payload.title) title.textContent = payload.title;
      if (subtitle && payload.subtitle) subtitle.textContent = payload.subtitle;
      if (industry) industry.textContent = 'Industry · ' + (payload.industry || 'General');
      if (sourceCount) sourceCount.textContent = 'Sources · ' + (payload.sources_analyzed || 0);
      if (engine) {
        engine.textContent = payload.source === 'llm'
          ? 'Planner · LLM grounded'
          : (refining ? 'Planner · LLM refining…' : 'Planner · evidence candidates');
        engine.classList.toggle('llm', payload.source === 'llm');
      }
      if (!host) return;

      const findings = Array.isArray(payload.findings) ? payload.findings : [];
      if (!findings.length) {
        host.innerHTML = '<div class="crossdoc-empty">At least two session sources are needed for cross-document discovery.</div>';
        return;
      }
      host.innerHTML = findings.map((finding, index) => {
        const severity = ['critical', 'high', 'medium', 'review'].includes(finding.severity)
          ? finding.severity : 'review';
        const confidence = Math.round(Math.max(0, Math.min(1, Number(finding.confidence) || 0)) * 100);
        const sourceHtml = (finding.sources || []).map(source =>
          '<div class="crossdoc-source"><span>▣</span><span>' +
          crossdocEsc(source.filename) + '</span><span class="crossdoc-source-type">' +
          crossdocEsc(source.modality || 'source') + '</span></div>'
        ).join('');
        const evidence = finding.evidence
          ? '<div class="crossdoc-section-label">Evidence link</div><div class="crossdoc-evidence">' +
            crossdocEsc(finding.evidence) + '</div>' : '';
        const impact = finding.business_impact
          ? '<div class="crossdoc-section-label">Why it matters</div><div class="crossdoc-impact">' +
            crossdocEsc(finding.business_impact) + '</div>' : '';
        const query = finding.graph_query
          ? '<div class="crossdoc-query">' + crossdocEsc(finding.graph_query) + '</div>' : '';
        return '<article class="crossdoc-card severity-' + severity + '" id="crossdocFinding' + index + '">' +
          '<button type="button" class="crossdoc-card-head" onclick="toggleCrossDocFinding(' + index + ')">' +
          '<span class="crossdoc-card-icon">◆</span>' +
          '<span class="crossdoc-card-title">' + crossdocEsc(finding.title || ('Finding ' + (index + 1))) + '</span>' +
          '<span class="crossdoc-confidence">' + confidence + '% confidence</span>' +
          '<span class="crossdoc-chevron">⌄</span></button>' +
          '<div class="crossdoc-card-body"><div class="crossdoc-sources">' + sourceHtml + '</div>' +
          '<div class="crossdoc-summary">' + crossdocEsc(finding.summary || '') + '</div>' +
          evidence + impact + query + '</div></article>';
      }).join('');
    }

    async function refreshCrossDocDiscovery() {
      const generation = ++crossdocRefreshGen;
      const host = document.getElementById('crossdocFindings');
      const engine = document.getElementById('crossdocEngine');
      if (host) host.innerHTML = '<div class="crossdoc-empty">Analyzing source intersections for the active requirement…</div>';
      if (engine) {
        engine.textContent = 'Planner · preparing…';
        engine.classList.remove('llm');
      }
      const payload = crossdocRequestPayload();
      let fast = null;
      try {
        const response = await crossdocApiRequest(
          Object.assign({}, payload, { skip_llm: true })
        );
        if (response.ok) {
          fast = await response.json();
          if (generation === crossdocRefreshGen) renderCrossDocPayload(fast, true);
        }
      } catch (error) {
        console.warn('cross-doc candidate pass failed', error);
      }
      if (!fast) {
        if (host) host.innerHTML = '<div class="crossdoc-empty">Cross-document discovery could not load. Check the API connection.</div>';
        return;
      }
      try {
        const response = await crossdocApiRequest(payload);
        if (response.ok) {
          const refined = await response.json();
          if (generation === crossdocRefreshGen) renderCrossDocPayload(refined, false);
        } else if (generation === crossdocRefreshGen) {
          renderCrossDocPayload(fast, false);
        }
      } catch (error) {
        console.warn('cross-doc LLM refinement skipped', error);
        if (generation === crossdocRefreshGen) renderCrossDocPayload(fast, false);
      }
    }

    /* ============================================================
       INTELLIGENCE REPORT — user-specific outcome synthesis
       ============================================================ */
    let intelRefreshGen = 0;
    let intelligenceReportPayload = null;
    let intelligenceReportSummaryPayload = null;
    let intelligenceSummaryPinnedOpen = false;

    function intelligenceReportRequestPayload() {
      const base = crossdocRequestPayload();
      const detections = (cyphPayload && cyphPayload.detections) || [];
      return Object.assign({}, base, {
        industry: (crossdocPayload && crossdocPayload.industry) || base.industry || '',
        use_case: (crossdocPayload && crossdocPayload.use_case) || base.use_case || '',
        requirement: (crossdocPayload && crossdocPayload.requirement) || base.requirement || '',
        prior_findings: (crossdocPayload && crossdocPayload.findings) || [],
        detection_results: detections.map(det => ({
          id: det.id,
          title: det.title,
          status: cyphCompletedDets.has(det.id) ? 'complete' : 'not_run',
          flags_message: det.flags_message || '',
          result_summary: det.result_summary || {},
          significant_paths: (det.significant_paths || []).slice(0, 6),
        })),
      });
    }

    async function intelligenceReportApiRequest(body) {
      const options = {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify(body),
      };
      try {
        const response = await fetch('/api/intelligence/report', options);
        if (response.status !== 404) return response;
      } catch (_) {}
      return fetch('http://127.0.0.1:8011/api/intelligence/report', options);
    }

    async function intelligenceReportSummaryApiRequest(body) {
      const options = {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify(body),
      };
      try {
        const response = await fetch('/api/intelligence/report/summarize', options);
        if (response.status !== 404) return response;
      } catch (_) {}
      return fetch('http://127.0.0.1:8011/api/intelligence/report/summarize', options);
    }

    function renderIntelligenceReportSummary(payload) {
      if (!payload) return;
      intelligenceReportSummaryPayload = payload;
      const panel = document.getElementById('intelActionBrief');
      const title = document.getElementById('intelBriefTitle');
      const intro = document.getElementById('intelBriefIntro');
      const host = document.getElementById('intelBriefActions');
      if (title) title.textContent = payload.title || 'Five Priority Actions';
      if (intro) intro.textContent = payload.intro || '';
      if (host) {
        const actions = Array.isArray(payload.actions) ? payload.actions.slice(0, 5) : [];
        host.innerHTML = actions.map((item, index) =>
          '<article class="final-brief-action"><span class="final-brief-rank">' + (index + 1) +
          '</span><div><div class="final-brief-action-title">' + crossdocEsc(item.action) +
          '</div><div class="final-brief-reason">' + crossdocEsc(item.reason || '') +
          '</div></div><div class="final-brief-meta">Owner · ' + crossdocEsc(item.owner || 'To assign') +
          '<br>Timing · ' + crossdocEsc(item.timing || 'Next review cycle') + '</div></article>'
        ).join('') || '<div class="crossdoc-empty">No distinct action is available to summarize.</div>';
      }
      if (panel) {
        panel.style.display = intelligenceSummaryPinnedOpen ? '' : 'none';
        if (intelligenceSummaryPinnedOpen) {
          panel.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
        }
      }
    }

    async function summarizeIntelligenceReport() {
      if (!intelligenceReportPayload) return;
      intelligenceSummaryPinnedOpen = true;
      const button = document.getElementById('intelSummarizeBtn');
      if (button) { button.disabled = true; button.textContent = 'Summarizing…'; }
      try {
        const fastResponse = await intelligenceReportSummaryApiRequest({
          report: intelligenceReportPayload,
          skip_llm: true,
        });
        if (fastResponse.ok) renderIntelligenceReportSummary(await fastResponse.json());
        const refinedResponse = await intelligenceReportSummaryApiRequest({
          report: intelligenceReportPayload,
          skip_llm: false,
        });
        if (refinedResponse.ok) renderIntelligenceReportSummary(await refinedResponse.json());
      } catch (error) {
        console.warn('intelligence report summary failed', error);
      } finally {
        if (button) { button.disabled = false; button.textContent = '✦ Summarize Report'; }
      }
    }

    function closeIntelligenceReportSummary() {
      intelligenceSummaryPinnedOpen = false;
      const panel = document.getElementById('intelActionBrief');
      if (panel) panel.style.display = 'none';
    }

    function renderIntelligenceReport(payload, refining) {
      if (!payload) return;
      intelligenceReportPayload = payload;
      const loading = document.getElementById('intelLoading');
      const report = document.getElementById('intelReportBody');
      if (loading) loading.style.display = 'none';
      if (report) report.style.display = '';
      const summaryButton = document.getElementById('intelSummarizeBtn');
      if (summaryButton) summaryButton.disabled = false;

      const setText = (id, value) => {
        const el = document.getElementById(id);
        if (el) el.textContent = value == null ? '' : String(value);
      };
      setText('intelPhase', payload.phase_label || 'Step 9 of 10 · Intelligence Report');
      setText('intelTitle', payload.title || 'Intelligence Report');
      setText('intelSubtitle', payload.subtitle || '');
      setText('intelIndustry', 'Industry · ' + (payload.industry || 'General'));
      setText('intelRequirement', 'Requirement · ' + (payload.requirement || payload.use_case || 'Current session'));
      setText(
        'intelEngine',
        payload.source === 'llm' ? 'Report · LLM grounded' :
          (refining ? 'Report · LLM refining…' : 'Report · evidence summary')
      );
      const engine = document.getElementById('intelEngine');
      if (engine) engine.classList.toggle('llm', payload.source === 'llm');
      let generated = '—';
      try { generated = new Date(payload.generated_at).toLocaleString(); } catch (_) {}
      setText('intelGenerated', 'Generated · ' + generated);
      setText('intelExecutive', payload.executive_summary || '');

      const metrics = document.getElementById('intelMetrics');
      if (metrics) {
        metrics.innerHTML = (payload.report_metrics || []).map(metric =>
          '<div class="intel-metric"><div class="intel-metric-label">' +
          crossdocEsc(metric.label) + '</div><div class="intel-metric-value">' +
          crossdocEsc(metric.value) + '</div><div class="intel-metric-detail">' +
          crossdocEsc(metric.detail || '') + '</div></div>'
        ).join('');
      }

      const brief = payload.decision_brief || {};
      setText('intelSituation', brief.situation || '');
      setText('intelAssessment', brief.assessment || '');
      setText('intelDecision', brief.decision_needed || '');

      const insightsHost = document.getElementById('intelInsights');
      const insights = Array.isArray(payload.priority_insights) ? payload.priority_insights : [];
      if (insightsHost) {
        insightsHost.innerHTML = insights.length ? insights.map(insight => {
          const priority = ['critical', 'high', 'medium', 'review'].includes(insight.priority)
            ? insight.priority : 'review';
          const confidence = Math.round(Math.max(0, Math.min(1, Number(insight.confidence) || 0)) * 100);
          const sourceLine = (insight.evidence_sources || []).length
            ? '<div class="intel-insight-evidence">Sources · ' +
              (insight.evidence_sources || []).map(crossdocEsc).join(' · ') +
              (insight.evidence ? '<br>Evidence · ' + crossdocEsc(insight.evidence) : '') + '</div>'
            : (insight.evidence
              ? '<div class="intel-insight-evidence">Evidence · ' + crossdocEsc(insight.evidence) + '</div>'
              : '');
          return '<article class="intel-insight ' + priority + '"><div class="intel-insight-head">' +
            '<div class="intel-insight-title">' + crossdocEsc(insight.title) + '</div>' +
            '<span class="intel-priority">' + crossdocEsc(priority) + '</span>' +
            '<span class="intel-confidence">' + confidence + '%</span></div>' +
            '<div class="intel-insight-copy">' + crossdocEsc(insight.assessment || '') + '</div>' +
            (insight.implication ? '<div class="intel-insight-copy"><b>Implication:</b> ' +
              crossdocEsc(insight.implication) + '</div>' : '') +
            sourceLine +
            (insight.recommended_response ? '<div class="intel-response"><b>Response:</b> ' +
              crossdocEsc(insight.recommended_response) + '</div>' : '') + '</article>';
        }).join('') : '<div class="crossdoc-empty">No grounded priority insight is available yet.</div>';
      }

      const actionsHost = document.getElementById('intelActions');
      const actions = Array.isArray(payload.recommended_actions) ? payload.recommended_actions : [];
      if (actionsHost) {
        actionsHost.innerHTML = actions.map((action, index) =>
          '<div class="intel-action" data-priority="' + (index + 1) + '">' +
          '<div class="intel-action-title">' + crossdocEsc(action.action) + '</div>' +
          '<div class="intel-action-meta">' + crossdocEsc(action.owner || 'Owner TBD') +
          ' · ' + crossdocEsc(action.timeframe || 'Review cycle') + '</div>' +
          '<div class="intel-action-reason">' + crossdocEsc(action.rationale || '') + '</div></div>'
        ).join('');
      }

      const evidenceRows = document.getElementById('intelEvidenceRows');
      if (evidenceRows) {
        evidenceRows.innerHTML = (payload.evidence_matrix || []).map(source =>
          '<tr><td>' + crossdocEsc(source.filename) + '</td><td>' +
          crossdocEsc(source.modality) + '</td><td>' + crossdocEsc(source.role) +
          '</td><td>' + crossdocEsc((source.insights_supported || []).join(', ') || 'Context only') +
          '</td></tr>'
        ).join('') || '<tr><td colspan="4">No source evidence is available.</td></tr>';
      }

      const methodology = document.getElementById('intelMethodology');
      if (methodology) {
        methodology.innerHTML = (payload.methodology || []).map(item =>
          '<li>' + crossdocEsc(item) + '</li>'
        ).join('');
      }
      setText('intelLimitations', payload.limitations || '');
    }

    async function refreshIntelligenceReport() {
      const generation = ++intelRefreshGen;
      const loading = document.getElementById('intelLoading');
      const report = document.getElementById('intelReportBody');
      if (loading) {
        loading.style.display = '';
        loading.textContent = 'Building a user-specific intelligence report from prior outcomes…';
      }
      if (report) report.style.display = 'none';
      const summaryButton = document.getElementById('intelSummarizeBtn');
      if (summaryButton) summaryButton.disabled = true;
      const payload = intelligenceReportRequestPayload();
      let fast = null;
      try {
        const response = await intelligenceReportApiRequest(
          Object.assign({}, payload, { skip_llm: true })
        );
        if (response.ok) {
          fast = await response.json();
          if (generation === intelRefreshGen) renderIntelligenceReport(fast, true);
        }
      } catch (error) {
        console.warn('intelligence report evidence pass failed', error);
      }
      if (!fast) {
        if (loading) loading.textContent = 'The intelligence report could not load. Check the API connection.';
        return;
      }
      try {
        const response = await intelligenceReportApiRequest(payload);
        if (response.ok) {
          const refined = await response.json();
          if (generation === intelRefreshGen) renderIntelligenceReport(refined, false);
        } else if (generation === intelRefreshGen) {
          renderIntelligenceReport(fast, false);
        }
      } catch (error) {
        console.warn('intelligence report LLM refinement skipped', error);
        if (generation === intelRefreshGen) renderIntelligenceReport(fast, false);
      }
    }

    function downloadIntelligenceReport() {
      if (!intelligenceReportPayload) return;
      const blob = new Blob(
        [JSON.stringify(intelligenceReportPayload, null, 2)],
        { type: 'application/json' }
      );
      const link = document.createElement('a');
      link.href = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
      link.download = 'intelligence-report.json';
      link.click();
      setTimeout(() => URL.revokeObjectURL(link.href), 500);
    }

    /* ============================================================
       FINAL REPORT — executive action document + multi-format export
       ============================================================ */
    let finalReportRefreshGen = 0;
    let finalReportPayload = null;
    let finalReportSummaryPayload = null;

    function finalReportRequestPayload() {
      return Object.assign({}, intelligenceReportRequestPayload(), {
        intelligence_report: intelligenceReportPayload || {},
      });
    }

    async function finalReportApiRequest(body) {
      const options = {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify(body),
      };
      try {
        const response = await fetch('/api/final-report', options);
        if (response.status !== 404) return response;
      } catch (_) {}
      return fetch('http://127.0.0.1:8011/api/final-report', options);
    }

    async function finalReportSummaryApiRequest(body) {
      const options = {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify(body),
      };
      try {
        const response = await fetch('/api/final-report/summarize', options);
        if (response.status !== 404) return response;
      } catch (_) {}
      return fetch('http://127.0.0.1:8011/api/final-report/summarize', options);
    }

    function renderFinalReportSummary(payload) {
      if (!payload) return;
      finalReportSummaryPayload = payload;
      const panel = document.getElementById('finalActionBrief');
      const title = document.getElementById('finalBriefTitle');
      const intro = document.getElementById('finalBriefIntro');
      const host = document.getElementById('finalBriefActions');
      if (title) title.textContent = payload.title || 'Five Actions for Leadership';
      if (intro) intro.textContent = payload.intro || '';
      if (host) {
        const actions = Array.isArray(payload.actions) ? payload.actions.slice(0, 5) : [];
        host.innerHTML = actions.map((item, index) =>
          '<article class="final-brief-action"><span class="final-brief-rank">' + (index + 1) +
          '</span><div><div class="final-brief-action-title">' + crossdocEsc(item.action) +
          '</div><div class="final-brief-reason">' + crossdocEsc(item.reason || '') +
          '</div></div><div class="final-brief-meta">Owner · ' + crossdocEsc(item.owner || 'To assign') +
          '<br>Timing · ' + crossdocEsc(item.timing || 'Next review cycle') + '</div></article>'
        ).join('') || '<div class="crossdoc-empty">No distinct action is available to summarize.</div>';
      }
      if (panel) {
        panel.style.display = '';
        panel.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
      }
    }

    async function summarizeFinalReport() {
      if (!finalReportPayload) return;
      const button = document.getElementById('finalSummarizeBtn');
      if (button) { button.disabled = true; button.textContent = 'Summarizing…'; }
      try {
        const fastResponse = await finalReportSummaryApiRequest({
          report: finalReportPayload,
          skip_llm: true,
        });
        if (fastResponse.ok) renderFinalReportSummary(await fastResponse.json());
        const refinedResponse = await finalReportSummaryApiRequest({
          report: finalReportPayload,
          skip_llm: false,
        });
        if (refinedResponse.ok) renderFinalReportSummary(await refinedResponse.json());
      } catch (error) {
        console.warn('final report summary failed', error);
      } finally {
        if (button) { button.disabled = false; button.textContent = '✦ Summarize Report'; }
      }
    }

    function closeFinalReportSummary() {
      const panel = document.getElementById('finalActionBrief');
      if (panel) panel.style.display = 'none';
    }

    function renderFinalReport(payload, refining) {
      if (!payload) return;
      finalReportPayload = payload;
      const loading = document.getElementById('finalLoading');
      const body = document.getElementById('finalReportBody');
      if (loading) loading.style.display = 'none';
      if (body) body.style.display = '';
      const summaryButton = document.getElementById('finalSummarizeBtn');
      if (summaryButton) summaryButton.disabled = false;
      const setText = (id, value) => {
        const el = document.getElementById(id);
        if (el) el.textContent = value == null ? '' : String(value);
      };
      setText('finalPhase', payload.phase_label || 'Step 10 of 11 · Final Executive Report');
      setText('finalTitle', payload.title || 'Final Executive Report');
      setText('finalSubtitle', payload.subtitle || '');
      setText('finalReportId', payload.report_id || '—');
      let generated = '—';
      try { generated = new Date(payload.generated_at).toLocaleString(); } catch (_) {}
      setText('finalGenerated', generated);
      setText('finalClassification', payload.classification || 'Confidential');
      setText(
        'finalEngine',
        payload.source === 'llm' ? 'LLM-grounded executive synthesis' :
          (refining ? 'LLM refinement in progress' : 'Pipeline evidence synthesis')
      );
      setText('finalIndustry', 'Industry · ' + (payload.industry || 'General'));
      setText('finalRequirement', 'Requirement · ' + (payload.requirement || payload.use_case || 'Current session'));

      const metrics = document.getElementById('finalMetrics');
      if (metrics) {
        metrics.innerHTML = (payload.key_metrics || []).map(metric =>
          '<div class="intel-metric"><div class="intel-metric-label">' +
          crossdocEsc(metric.label) + '</div><div class="intel-metric-value">' +
          crossdocEsc(metric.value) + '</div></div>'
        ).join('');
      }

      const summary = payload.report_summary || {};
      setText('finalObjective', summary.objective || '');
      setText('finalConclusion', summary.executive_conclusion || '');
      setText('finalScope', summary.scope || '');
      setText('finalKeyMessage', summary.key_message || '');

      const decisions = document.getElementById('finalDecisions');
      if (decisions) {
        decisions.innerHTML = (payload.leadership_decisions || []).map((item, index) =>
          '<div class="final-decision"><span class="final-decision-num">' + (index + 1) + '</span>' +
          '<div class="final-decision-title">' + crossdocEsc(item.decision) + '</div>' +
          '<div class="final-decision-why">' + crossdocEsc(item.why_it_matters || '') + '</div>' +
          '<div class="final-decision-by">Decision by · ' + crossdocEsc(item.decision_by || 'Governance review') +
          '</div></div>'
        ).join('');
      }

      const actionRows = document.getElementById('finalActionRows');
      if (actionRows) {
        actionRows.innerHTML = (payload.top_action_points || []).map((item, index) =>
          '<tr><td><span class="final-rank">' + (index + 1) + '</span></td>' +
          '<td><b>' + crossdocEsc(item.action) + '</b><br><span style="color:var(--tx-3)">' +
          crossdocEsc(item.rationale || '') + '</span></td>' +
          '<td>' + crossdocEsc(item.owner) + '</td><td>' + crossdocEsc(item.timeframe) + '</td>' +
          '<td>' + crossdocEsc(item.success_measure || '') + '</td><td><span class="final-status">' +
          crossdocEsc(item.status || 'Proposed') + '</span></td></tr>'
        ).join('');
      }

      const recommendations = document.getElementById('finalRecommendations');
      if (recommendations) {
        recommendations.innerHTML = (payload.top_recommendations || []).map((item, index) => {
          const priority = ['critical', 'high', 'medium', 'review'].includes(item.priority)
            ? item.priority : 'review';
          const confidence = Math.round(Math.max(0, Math.min(1, Number(item.confidence) || 0)) * 100);
          return '<article class="final-recommendation ' + priority + '">' +
            '<div class="final-rec-head"><div class="final-rec-title">' + (index + 1) + '. ' +
            crossdocEsc(item.recommendation) + '</div><span class="final-rec-priority">' +
            crossdocEsc(priority) + ' · ' + confidence + '%</span></div>' +
            '<div class="final-rec-copy"><b>Why now:</b> ' + crossdocEsc(item.why_now || '') + '</div>' +
            '<div class="final-rec-copy"><b>Expected outcome:</b> ' +
            crossdocEsc(item.expected_outcome || '') + '</div></article>';
        }).join('') || '<div class="crossdoc-empty">No recommendation is sufficiently grounded yet.</div>';
      }

      const obligationRows = document.getElementById('finalObligationRows');
      if (obligationRows) {
        obligationRows.innerHTML = (payload.obligations || []).map(item =>
          '<tr><td>' + crossdocEsc(item.obligation) + '</td><td>' + crossdocEsc(item.source) +
          '</td><td>' + crossdocEsc(item.trigger_or_due) + '</td><td>' + crossdocEsc(item.owner) +
          '</td><td>' + crossdocEsc(item.verification) + '</td><td><span class="final-status">' +
          crossdocEsc(item.status) + '</span></td></tr>'
        ).join('');
      }

      const roadmap = document.getElementById('finalRoadmap');
      if (roadmap) {
        roadmap.innerHTML = (payload.way_forward || []).map(item =>
          '<article class="final-roadmap-phase"><div class="final-roadmap-horizon">' +
          crossdocEsc(item.horizon) + '</div><div class="final-roadmap-title">' +
          crossdocEsc(item.phase) + '</div><div class="final-roadmap-copy">' +
          crossdocEsc(item.objective) + '</div><div class="final-roadmap-copy"><b>Deliverables:</b> ' +
          crossdocEsc(item.deliverables) + '</div><div class="final-roadmap-gate"><b>Decision gate:</b> ' +
          crossdocEsc(item.decision_gate) + '</div></article>'
        ).join('');
      }

      const evidence = document.getElementById('finalEvidence');
      if (evidence) {
        evidence.innerHTML = (payload.evidence_basis || []).map(source =>
          '<span class="final-evidence-item">' + crossdocEsc(source.filename) + ' · ' +
          crossdocEsc(source.modality) + '</span>'
        ).join('') || '<span class="final-evidence-item">No source evidence available</span>';
      }
      setText('finalAssurance', payload.assurance_statement || '');

      const signoff = document.getElementById('finalSignoff');
      if (signoff) {
        signoff.innerHTML = (payload.sign_off || []).map(item =>
          '<div class="final-signoff-card"><div class="final-signoff-role">' +
          crossdocEsc(item.role) + '</div><div class="final-sign-line"></div>' +
          '<div class="final-sign-label">Name / signature / decision / date</div></div>'
        ).join('');
      }
    }

    async function refreshFinalReport() {
      const generation = ++finalReportRefreshGen;
      const loading = document.getElementById('finalLoading');
      const body = document.getElementById('finalReportBody');
      if (loading) {
        loading.style.display = '';
        loading.textContent = 'Building the final report from all prior pipeline outcomes…';
      }
      if (body) body.style.display = 'none';
      const summaryPanel = document.getElementById('finalActionBrief');
      if (summaryPanel) summaryPanel.style.display = 'none';
      const summaryButton = document.getElementById('finalSummarizeBtn');
      if (summaryButton) summaryButton.disabled = true;
      finalReportSummaryPayload = null;
      const payload = finalReportRequestPayload();
      let fast = null;
      try {
        const response = await finalReportApiRequest(
          Object.assign({}, payload, { skip_llm: true })
        );
        if (response.ok) {
          fast = await response.json();
          if (generation === finalReportRefreshGen) renderFinalReport(fast, true);
        }
      } catch (error) {
        console.warn('final report evidence pass failed', error);
      }
      if (!fast) {
        if (loading) loading.textContent = 'The final report could not load. Check the API connection.';
        return;
      }
      try {
        const response = await finalReportApiRequest(payload);
        if (response.ok) {
          const refined = await response.json();
          if (generation === finalReportRefreshGen) renderFinalReport(refined, false);
        } else if (generation === finalReportRefreshGen) {
          renderFinalReport(fast, false);
        }
      } catch (error) {
        console.warn('final report LLM refinement skipped', error);
        if (generation === finalReportRefreshGen) renderFinalReport(fast, false);
      }
    }

    function finalReportDocumentHtml() {
      const cover = document.querySelector('#view-report .final-cover');
      const reportBody = document.getElementById('finalReportBody');
      const title = finalReportPayload ? finalReportPayload.title : 'Final Executive Report';
      return '<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>' +
        crossdocEsc(title) + '</title><style>' +
        'body{font:14px Arial,sans-serif;color:#182033;max-width:1100px;margin:32px auto;line-height:1.5}' +
        '.final-cover{border-bottom:3px solid #147b86;padding-bottom:20px;margin-bottom:20px}' +
        '.eyebrow,.final-section-kicker{color:#147b86;font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:bold}' +
        '.page-title{font-size:28px;font-weight:bold;margin:8px 0}.page-sub{color:#526077}' +
        '.final-cover-meta{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:8px;margin-top:15px}' +
        '.final-cover-meta span{display:block;color:#64748b;font-size:10px}.final-cover-meta b{font-size:11px}' +
        '.intel-metrics{display:flex;gap:12px}.intel-metric{border:1px solid #cbd5e1;padding:10px;flex:1}' +
        '.intel-metric-label{font-size:10px;color:#64748b}.intel-metric-value{font-size:20px;font-weight:bold}' +
        '.final-section{border:1px solid #cbd5e1;padding:16px;margin:14px 0;break-inside:avoid}' +
        '.final-summary-grid,.final-decision-list,.final-recommendations,.final-roadmap,.final-signoff{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:12px}' +
        '.final-summary-grid>div,.final-decision,.final-recommendation,.final-roadmap-phase,.final-signoff-card{border:1px solid #e2e8f0;padding:10px}' +
        'table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:11px}th,td{border:1px solid #cbd5e1;padding:7px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}' +
        '.final-evidence-item{display:inline-block;border:1px solid #cbd5e1;padding:5px;margin:3px}' +
        '.final-sign-line{height:30px;border-bottom:1px solid #64748b}.final-toolbar,.struct-nav{display:none}' +
        '</style></head><body>' + (cover ? cover.outerHTML : '') +
        (reportBody ? reportBody.outerHTML : '') + '</body></html>';
    }

    function downloadFinalReportBlob(content, mime, extension) {
      const blob = new Blob([content], { type: mime });
      const link = document.createElement('a');
      link.href = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
      link.download = 'final-executive-report.' + extension;
      link.click();
      setTimeout(() => URL.revokeObjectURL(link.href), 500);
    }

    function exportFinalReport() {
      if (!finalReportPayload) return;
      const select = document.getElementById('finalExportFormat');
      const format = select ? select.value : 'pdf';
      if (format === 'pdf') {
        window.print();
        return;
      }
      if (format === 'json') {
        downloadFinalReportBlob(
          JSON.stringify(finalReportPayload, null, 2),
          'application/json',
          'json'
        );
        return;
      }
      if (format === 'csv') {
        const headers = ['Priority', 'Action', 'Owner', 'Timeframe', 'Rationale', 'Success Measure', 'Status'];
        const quote = value => '"' + String(value == null ? '' : value).replace(/"/g, '""') + '"';
        const rows = (finalReportPayload.top_action_points || []).map((item, index) => [
          index + 1, item.action, item.owner, item.timeframe, item.rationale,
          item.success_measure, item.status,
        ].map(quote).join(','));
        downloadFinalReportBlob(
          [headers.map(quote).join(',')].concat(rows).join('\r\n'),
          'text/csv;charset=utf-8',
          'csv'
        );
        return;
      }
      const html = finalReportDocumentHtml();
      downloadFinalReportBlob(
        html,
        format === 'doc' ? 'application/msword' : 'text/html;charset=utf-8',
        format === 'doc' ? 'doc' : 'html'
      );
    }

    window.refreshCypherDetection = refreshCypherDetection;
    window.selectCypherDetection = selectCypherDetection;
    window.goToCypherDetection = typeof goToCypherDetection === 'function' ? goToCypherDetection : function () { nav('cypher'); };
    window.cyphTogglePlay = cyphTogglePlay;
    window.cyphStepForward = cyphStepForward;
    window.cyphStepBack = cyphStepBack;
    window.cyphRestart = cyphRestart;
    window.cyphUpdateSpeed = cyphUpdateSpeed;
    window.runCypherDetection = runCypherDetection;
    window.cyphRunAllDetections = cyphRunAllDetections;
    window.refreshCrossDocDiscovery = refreshCrossDocDiscovery;
    window.toggleCrossDocFinding = toggleCrossDocFinding;
    window.refreshIntelligenceReport = refreshIntelligenceReport;
    window.downloadIntelligenceReport = downloadIntelligenceReport;
    window.summarizeIntelligenceReport = summarizeIntelligenceReport;
    window.closeIntelligenceReportSummary = closeIntelligenceReportSummary;
    window.refreshFinalReport = refreshFinalReport;
    window.exportFinalReport = exportFinalReport;
    window.summarizeFinalReport = summarizeFinalReport;
    window.closeFinalReportSummary = closeFinalReportSummary;
    window.selectDomainIndustry = selectDomainIndustry;
    window.selectDomainUseCase = selectDomainUseCase;
    window.assistDomainConfiguration = assistDomainConfiguration;
    window.beginConfiguredJourney = beginConfiguredJourney;
    window.refreshTrendingUseCases = refreshTrendingUseCases;
    window.openCustomUseCase = openCustomUseCase;
    window.synthesizeCustomUseCase = synthesizeCustomUseCase;
    window.saveDomainScenario = saveDomainScenario;
    window.startSavedDomainScenario = startSavedDomainScenario;
    window.deleteSavedDomainScenario = deleteSavedDomainScenario;
    window.resetDomainConfigurator = resetDomainConfigurator;
    window.refreshSchemaRegistry = refreshSchemaRegistry;

    function setIgFilter(filter) {
      igActiveFilter = filter || 'all';
      renderIgFilterBar(igTabsMeta && igTabsMeta.tabs);
      initFullGraph();
      const meta = document.getElementById('igFilterMeta');
      if (meta) {
        const fg = filteredIgGraph();
        meta.textContent = fg.nodes.length + ' nodes - ' + fg.links.length + ' edges';
      }
    }

    function buildFullGraphData() {
      if (igGraphCache.nodes && igGraphCache.nodes.length) {
        const fg = filteredIgGraph();
        const nodes = fg.nodes.map(n => Object.assign({}, n, { data: Object.assign({}, n.data || {}) }));
        const links = fg.links.map(l => Object.assign({}, l, {
          source: typeof l.source === 'object' ? l.source.id : l.source,
          target: typeof l.target === 'object' ? l.target.id : l.target,
        }));
        return { nodes, links };
      }
      return buildInteractiveGraphData(igTabsMeta);
    }

    function initFullGraph() {
      const svgEl = document.getElementById('fullGraph');
      if (!svgEl) return;
      if (typeof d3 === 'undefined') {
        console.error('d3 not loaded');
        return;
      }
      svgEl.innerHTML = '';
      const wrap = svgEl.parentElement;
      let W = (wrap && wrap.clientWidth) || 0;
      let H = (wrap && wrap.clientHeight) || 0;
      if (W < 100) W = 900;
      if (H < 100) H = 560;
      const svg = d3.select('#fullGraph').attr('viewBox', [0, 0, W, H]);
      const g = svg.append('g');
      svg.call(d3.zoom().scaleExtent([0.25, 3.5]).on('zoom', e => g.attr('transform', e.transform)));

      const defs = svg.append('defs');
      defs.append('marker').attr('id', 'igArrow').attr('viewBox', '0 -4 8 8')
        .attr('refX', 18).attr('refY', 0).attr('markerWidth', 6).attr('markerHeight', 6).attr('orient', 'auto')
        .append('path').attr('d', 'M0,-4L8,0L0,4').attr('fill', '#3DDC97');
      defs.append('marker').attr('id', 'igArrowTeal').attr('viewBox', '0 -4 8 8')
        .attr('refX', 18).attr('refY', 0).attr('markerWidth', 6).attr('markerHeight', 6).attr('orient', 'auto')
        .append('path').attr('d', 'M0,-4L8,0L0,4').attr('fill', '#2DD4D4');

      const built = buildFullGraphData();
      const nodes = built.nodes;
      const links = built.links;
      fullSim = d3.forceSimulation(nodes)
        .force('link', d3.forceLink(links).id(d => d.id).distance(d => d.ring ? 70 : 95).strength(0.55))
        .force('charge', d3.forceManyBody().strength(-280))
        .force('center', d3.forceCenter(W / 2, H / 2))
        .force('collide', d3.forceCollide(28));

      const link = g.append('g').selectAll('line').data(links).join('line')
        .attr('stroke', d => d.ring ? '#3DDC97' : (d.cross ? '#2DD4D4' : '#243056'))
        .attr('stroke-width', d => d.ring ? 2.2 : (d.cross ? 1.6 : 1.2))
        .attr('stroke-dasharray', d => (d.cross || d.dashed) ? '5 4' : null)
        .attr('marker-end', d => d.ring ? 'url(#igArrow)' : (d.cross ? 'url(#igArrowTeal)' : null))
        .attr('opacity', 0.9);

      const linkLabel = g.append('g').selectAll('text').data(links.filter(l => l.label)).join('text')
        .text(d => d.label)
        .attr('font-size', 8)
        .attr('font-family', 'IBM Plex Mono')
        .attr('fill', '#6B7A9A')
        .attr('text-anchor', 'middle')
        .style('pointer-events', 'none');

      const node = g.append('g').selectAll('g').data(nodes).join('g')
        .style('cursor', 'pointer')
        .call(d3.drag()
          .on('start', (e, d) => { if (!e.active) fullSim.alphaTarget(0.25).restart(); d.fx = d.x; d.fy = d.y; })
          .on('drag', (e, d) => { d.fx = e.x; d.fy = e.y; })
          .on('end', (e, d) => { if (!e.active) fullSim.alphaTarget(0); d.fx = null; d.fy = null; }));

      node.append('circle')
        .attr('r', d => d.inRing ? 18 : 15)
        .attr('fill', d => igNodeColor(d.type))
        .attr('opacity', 0.92)
        .attr('stroke', d => d.dashed ? igNodeColor(d.type) : (d.alert ? '#FB5A6A' : '#fff'))
        .attr('stroke-opacity', d => d.dashed ? 0.95 : 0.2)
        .attr('stroke-width', d => d.dashed || d.alert ? 2.2 : 1.4)
        .attr('stroke-dasharray', d => d.dashed ? '3 2.5' : null)
        .on('click', (e, d) => { e.stopPropagation(); showNodeDetail(d); });

      node.append('text')
        .text(d => d.abbrev || igAbbrev(d.type))
        .attr('font-size', 9).attr('font-weight', 700)
        .attr('font-family', 'IBM Plex Mono').attr('fill', '#0B0E14')
        .attr('text-anchor', 'middle').attr('dy', '0.35em')
        .style('pointer-events', 'none');

      node.append('text')
        .text(d => d.label.length > 18 ? d.label.slice(0, 17) + '...' : d.label)
        .attr('font-size', 9)
        .attr('font-family', 'IBM Plex Mono').attr('fill', '#AEB8D4')
        .attr('text-anchor', 'middle').attr('y', 28)
        .style('pointer-events', 'none');

      fullSim.on('tick', () => {
        link.attr('x1', d => d.source.x).attr('y1', d => d.source.y)
            .attr('x2', d => d.target.x).attr('y2', d => d.target.y);
        linkLabel
          .attr('x', d => (d.source.x + d.target.x) / 2)
          .attr('y', d => (d.source.y + d.target.y) / 2 - 4);
        node.attr('transform', d => 'translate(' + d.x + ',' + d.y + ')');
      });

      const meta = document.getElementById('igFilterMeta');
      if (meta) meta.textContent = nodes.length + ' nodes - ' + links.length + ' edges';

      const nd = document.getElementById('nodeDetail');
      if (nd && !nd.querySelector('.nd-title') && !nd.querySelector('.nd-empty')) {
        nd.innerHTML = '<h4>Node Inspector</h4><div class="nd-empty"><div style="font-size:26px;margin-bottom:8px;opacity:.5">&#128269;</div>Click any node<br/>to inspect</div>';
      }
    }

    function restartSim() { if (fullSim) { fullSim.alpha(1).restart(); } }
    function resetGraphZoom() { initFullGraph(); }

    function showNodeDetail(d) {
      const color = igNodeColor(d.type);
      let html = '<h4>Node Inspector</h4>';
      html += '<div class="nd-type-badge" style="background:' + color + '22;color:' + color + ';border:1px solid ' + color + '44">' + String(d.type || '').toUpperCase() + (d.dashed ? ' | EVIDENCE' : '') + '</div>';
      html += '<div class="nd-title">' + String(d.label || '').replace(/</g, '&lt;') + '</div>';
      const props = Object.assign({}, d.data || {}, {
        modality: d.modality,
        in_pattern_ring: d.inRing ? 'yes' : 'no',
        alert_flag: d.alert ? 'yes' : 'no',
        source_kind: d.source,
      });
      Object.entries(props).forEach(([k, v]) => {
        if (v == null || typeof v === 'object') return;
        html += '<div class="nd-prop"><div class="k">' + String(k).replace(/_/g, ' ') + '</div><div class="v">' + String(v).replace(/</g, '&lt;') + '</div></div>';
      });
      const panel = document.getElementById('nodeDetail');
      if (panel) panel.innerHTML = html;
    }

    /* Relationship table — derived from interactive graph edges */
    let relationshipRows = [];
    function buildRelationshipRowsFromGraph() {
      const nodes = (igGraphCache && igGraphCache.nodes) || [];
      const links = (igGraphCache && igGraphCache.links) || [];
      const byId = {};
      nodes.forEach(n => { byId[n.id] = n; });
      return links.map((l, i) => {
        const sid = typeof l.source === 'object' ? l.source.id : l.source;
        const tid = typeof l.target === 'object' ? l.target.id : l.target;
        const src = byId[sid] || { label: sid, type: '-' };
        const tgt = byId[tid] || { label: tid, type: '-' };
        return {
          edge_id: 'EDGE-' + String(i + 1).padStart(3, '0'),
          source: src.label,
          source_type: src.type,
          relationship: (src.label || sid) + ' -[' + (l.label || 'RELATED_TO') + ']-> ' + (tgt.label || tid),
          relationship_type: l.label || 'RELATED_TO',
          target: tgt.label,
          target_type: tgt.type,
          evidence_pattern: l.ring ? 'pattern-ring' : (l.cross ? 'cross-source' : (l.kind || 'graph-edge')),
          source_file: (src.data && src.data.source_file) || (tgt.data && tgt.data.source_file) || '-',
        };
      });
    }
    function refreshRelationshipTable() {
      relationshipRows = buildRelationshipRowsFromGraph();
      renderRelationshipTable();
      const meta = document.getElementById('relTableMeta');
      if (meta) {
        const uc = (igTabsMeta && igTabsMeta.use_case) || 'active session';
        meta.textContent = relationshipRows.length + ' edges from the interactive knowledge graph (' + uc + ').';
      }
    }
    function renderRelationshipTable() {
      const tbody = document.querySelector('#relTable tbody');
      if (!tbody) return;
      const q = String((document.getElementById('relFilter') || {}).value || '').toLowerCase().trim();
      const rows = !q ? relationshipRows : relationshipRows.filter(r =>
        Object.values(r).some(v => String(Array.isArray(v) ? v.join(' ') : v).toLowerCase().includes(q))
      );
      if (!rows.length) {
        tbody.innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="8" style="color:var(--tx-3);text-align:center;padding:18px">No relationships yet — open Interactive Graph or click Refresh tabs.</td></tr>';
        return;
      }
      tbody.innerHTML = rows.map(r => {
        return '<tr>' +
          [r.edge_id, r.source, r.source_type, r.relationship_type, r.target, r.target_type, r.evidence_pattern, r.source_file]
            .map(v => '<td>' + String(v == null ? '' : v).replace(/</g, '&lt;') + '</td>').join('') +
          '</tr>';
      }).join('');
    }
    function downloadRelationshipsCsv() {
      if (!relationshipRows.length) refreshRelationshipTable();
      const cols = ['edge_id','source','source_type','relationship_type','target','target_type','evidence_pattern','source_file'];
      const esc = (v) => '"' + String(Array.isArray(v) ? v.join('; ') : (v == null ? '' : v)).replace(/"/g, '""') + '"';
      const csv = [cols.join(',')].concat(relationshipRows.map(r => cols.map(c => esc(r[c])).join(','))).join('\n');
      const a = document.createElement('a');
      a.href = URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([csv], { type: 'text/csv' }));
      a.download = 'graph_relationships.csv';
      a.click();
    }
    function downloadRelationshipsJson() {
      if (!relationshipRows.length) refreshRelationshipTable();
      const a = document.createElement('a');
      a.href = URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([JSON.stringify(relationshipRows, null, 2)], { type: 'application/json' }));
      a.download = 'graph_relationships.json';
      a.click();
    }
    window.refreshRelationshipTable = refreshRelationshipTable;
    window.renderRelationshipTable = renderRelationshipTable;
    window.downloadRelationshipsCsv = downloadRelationshipsCsv;
    window.downloadRelationshipsJson = downloadRelationshipsJson;

    try { if (typeof refreshRelationshipTable === 'function') refreshRelationshipTable(); } catch (e) { console.warn('rel table init', e); }

    async function refreshNeoStatus() {
      const pulse = document.getElementById('neoPulse');
      const powered = document.getElementById('poweredByText');
      if (!pulse) return;
      try {
        const res = await fetch('/api/health');
        const data = await res.json();
        if (data.neo4j) {
          pulse.style.background = '';
          pulse.title = 'Neo4j connected';
          if (powered) powered.innerHTML = 'Powered by <strong>Neo4j</strong> · <strong>Protégé</strong> · spaCy · LLMs';
        } else {
          pulse.style.background = '#FB5A6A';
          pulse.title = 'Neo4j unreachable';
          if (powered) powered.innerHTML = 'Powered by <strong>Protégé</strong> · spaCy · LLMs · <strong>Neo4j offline</strong>';
        }
      } catch (_) {
        pulse.style.background = '#FB5A6A';
        pulse.title = 'API offline';
        if (powered) powered.innerHTML = 'Powered by <strong>Neo4j</strong> · <strong>Protégé</strong> · spaCy · LLMs';
      }
    }
    refreshNeoStatus();
    setInterval(refreshNeoStatus, 30000);
  
    window.currentTrackingId = window.currentTrackingId || null;

    async function fetchRecentUploads() {
        const list = document.getElementById('tracking-id-list');
        const container = document.getElementById('recent-uploads');
        if (!list || !container) return;
        container.style.display = 'block';
        try {
            const res = await fetch('/api/uploads/recent');
            if (!res.ok) {
                list.innerHTML = `<div class="tracking-empty">Could not load tracking IDs (HTTP ${res.status}).</div>`;
                return;
            }
            const data = await res.json();
            const rows = data.recent || [];
            if (!rows.length) {
                list.innerHTML = `<div class="tracking-empty">No saved sessions yet. Upload files once — the Tracking ID will appear here for reuse.</div>`;
                return;
            }
            list.innerHTML = rows.map(r => {
                const tid = String(r.tracking_id || '');
                const encodedTid = encodeURIComponent(tid);
                const scenarioId = String(r.scenario_tracking_id || '');
                const when = r.created_at ? String(r.created_at).replace('T', ' ').slice(0, 19) : '';
                const n = Number(r.file_count || 0);
                const active = window.currentTrackingId === tid ? ' active' : '';
                const scenarioDisplayId = scenarioId
                  ? compactTrackingId(
                    scenarioId, r.industry, r.use_case, r.scenario_saved_at
                  )
                  : '';
                return `<div class="tracking-chip${active}" role="button" tabindex="0" onclick="event.stopPropagation(); loadTrackingSession(decodeURIComponent('${encodedTid}'))" onkeydown="if(event.key === 'Enter' || event.key === ' '){ event.preventDefault(); event.stopPropagation(); loadTrackingSession(decodeURIComponent('${encodedTid}')); }" title="Load session ${tid}">
                  <button type="button" class="tracking-delete" aria-label="Delete tracking session ${tid}" title="Delete this tracking session" onclick="event.stopPropagation(); deleteTrackingSession(decodeURIComponent('${encodedTid}'), this)">×</button>
                  <span class="tid">${tid}</span>
                  <span class="tmeta">${r.use_case ? String(r.use_case) + ' · ' : ''}${n} file${n === 1 ? '' : 's'}${when ? ' · ' + when : ''}</span>
                  <span class="tmeta">${scenarioDisplayId ? 'Scenario · ' + scenarioDisplayId : 'Legacy upload · no scenario link'}</span>
                </div>`;
            }).join('');
        } catch (e) {
            console.error('Failed to fetch recent uploads', e);
            list.innerHTML = `<div class="tracking-empty">Could not reach upload store. Check API / database.</div>`;
        }
    }

    async function deleteTrackingSession(trackingId, button) {
        if (!trackingId) return;
        const confirmed = window.confirm(
          `Delete upload tracking ID ${trackingId} and all files stored under it?`
        );
        if (!confirmed) return;
        if (button) button.disabled = true;
        try {
            const res = await fetch(
              `/api/uploads/${encodeURIComponent(trackingId)}`,
              { method: 'DELETE' }
            );
            if (!res.ok) {
                const detail = await res.text();
                throw new Error(`HTTP ${res.status}${detail ? `: ${detail}` : ''}`);
            }
            if (window.currentTrackingId === trackingId) {
                startNewUploadSession();
            }
            await fetchRecentUploads();
        } catch (e) {
            console.error('Failed to delete tracking session', e);
            alert(`Could not delete tracking ID ${trackingId}.\n${e.message}`);
            if (button) button.disabled = false;
        }
    }

    async function uploadSelectedFiles() {
        const input = document.getElementById('multiFileInput');
        const scenario = uploadScenarioContext();
        if (!scenario) {
            alert('Save the Domain Configurator scenario first. Uploads must be linked to a saved scenario and an upload Tracking ID.');
            nav('domain');
            return;
        }
        const scenarioId = scenario.tracking_id || scenario.id;
        const scenarioConfig = scenario.config || {};
        if (window.currentTrackingId &&
            window.currentUploadScenarioTrackingId &&
            window.currentUploadScenarioTrackingId !== scenarioId) {
            window.currentTrackingId = null;
            window.currentUploadScenarioTrackingId = null;
        }
        // Prefer pending File objects collected via browse/drop; fall back to current input selection
        let candidates = pendingUploadFiles.length
          ? pendingUploadFiles.slice()
          : Array.from((input && input.files) || []);

        if (!candidates.length) {
            alert('Please browse or drop files first, then click Upload Files.');
            return;
        }

        // If appending to an existing tracking session, skip filenames already stored
        let existingNames = new Set();
        if (window.currentTrackingId) {
            try {
                const res = await fetch(`/api/uploads/${window.currentTrackingId}/files`);
                if (res.ok) {
                    const data = await res.json();
                    existingNames = new Set((data.files || []).map(f => String(f.filename || '').toLowerCase()));
                }
            } catch (_) {}
        }

        const toUpload = [];
        const skipped = [];
        const seen = new Set(existingNames);
        for (const f of candidates) {
            const key = String(f.name || '').toLowerCase();
            if (!key) continue;
            if (seen.has(key)) {
                skipped.push(f.name);
                continue;
            }
            seen.add(key);
            toUpload.push(f);
        }

        if (!toUpload.length) {
            alert(`No new files to upload.\n${skipped.length} file(s) already exist in tracking ID ${window.currentTrackingId || '(session)'}.`);
            pendingUploadFiles = [];
            if (input) input.value = '';
            return;
        }

        const formData = new FormData();
        toUpload.forEach(f => formData.append('files', f));
        formData.append('scenario_tracking_id', scenarioId);
        formData.append('industry', scenario.industry || scenarioConfig.industry || '');
        formData.append('use_case', scenario.use_case || scenarioConfig.use_case || '');

        try {
            let url = '/api/uploads';
            if (window.currentTrackingId) {
                url = `/api/uploads/${window.currentTrackingId}/append`;
            }
            const res = await fetch(url, { method: 'POST', body: formData });
            if(res.ok) {
                const data = await res.json();
                const skipMsg = skipped.length ? `\nSkipped ${skipped.length} unchanged/duplicate file(s).` : '';
                const added = data.files_uploaded ?? data.files_appended ?? toUpload.length;
                const scenarioDisplayId = compactTrackingId(
                  scenarioId, scenario.industry, scenario.use_case, scenario.saved_at
                );
                alert(`Uploaded ${added} new file(s).\nSaved Scenario: ${scenarioDisplayId}\nUpload Tracking ID: ${data.tracking_id}.${skipMsg}`);
                window.currentTrackingId = data.tracking_id;
                window.currentUploadScenarioTrackingId =
                  data.scenario_tracking_id || scenarioId;
                pendingUploadFiles = [];
                if (input) input.value = '';
                fetchRecentUploads();
                loadTrackingSession(data.tracking_id);
            } else {
                const errText = await res.text();
                alert(`Upload failed. Server responded with: ${res.status} ${errText}`);
            }
        } catch(e) {
            console.error('Upload Error:', e);
            alert(`Error during upload: ${e.message}`);
        }
    }

    async function loadTrackingSession(trackingId) {
        // Load only — never triggers upload
        window.currentTrackingId = trackingId;
        pendingUploadFiles = [];
        const input = document.getElementById('multiFileInput');
        if (input) input.value = '';
        closeIngestPreview();
        try {
            const res = await fetch(`/api/uploads/${trackingId}/files`);
            if(res.ok) {
                const data = await res.json();
                const session = data.session || {};
                window.currentUploadScenarioTrackingId =
                  session.scenario_tracking_id || null;
                if (window.currentUploadScenarioTrackingId) {
                    const linkedScenario = domainSavedScenarios.find(item =>
                      (item.tracking_id || item.id) ===
                        window.currentUploadScenarioTrackingId
                    );
                    if (linkedScenario && linkedScenario.config) {
                        window.currentJourneyTrackingId =
                          window.currentUploadScenarioTrackingId;
                        domainSelectedIndustry = linkedScenario.industry;
                        domainSelectedUseCase = linkedScenario.use_case;
                        domainConfiguration =
                          JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(linkedScenario.config));
                        applyDomainConfiguration(domainConfiguration);
                    }
                }
                uploadedCsvFiles = [];
                uploadedPdfFiles = [];
                uploadedImageFiles = [];
                uploadedAudioFiles = [];
                
                data.files.forEach(f => {
                    const fileObj = { name: f.filename, id: f.id };
                    const kind = classifyIngestExt(fileExt(f.filename));
                    if (kind === 'tabular') uploadedCsvFiles.push(fileObj);
                    else if (kind === 'document') uploadedPdfFiles.push(fileObj);
                    else if (kind === 'image') uploadedImageFiles.push(fileObj);
                    else if (kind === 'audio') uploadedAudioFiles.push(fileObj);
                    else uploadedPdfFiles.push(fileObj);
                });
                renderIngestGrids();
                fetchRecentUploads();
                updateActiveTrackingLabel();
                // Reset downstream graph so Interactive Graph rebuilds from this session
                try {
                  igTabsMeta = null;
                  igGraphCache = { nodes: [], links: [] };
                  igActiveFilter = 'all';
                  window.graphenConstructSnapshot = null;
                  window.graphenUseCaseHint = 'tracking ' + trackingId;
                } catch (_) {}
            }
        } catch(e) {
            console.error(e);
        }
    }

    async function previewFile(fileId, filename) {
        return previewIngestFile(filename, String(fileId || ''), '');
    }

    // Call fetchRecentUploads on load
    document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", () => {
        try { fetchRecentUploads(); } catch (e) { console.warn(e); }
        try { updateActiveTrackingLabel(); } catch (e) { console.warn(e); }
    });

    window.addEventListener('load', () => {
      try {
        const g = document.getElementById('view-graph');
        if (g && g.classList.contains('active') && typeof paintInteractiveGraph === 'function') {
          paintInteractiveGraph(buildLocalIgTabsMeta());
        }
      } catch (e) { console.warn('graph load paint', e); }
    });

</script>
</body>

</html>
